hadiths[774]{hadithnumber,text}:
"2950","Narrated Ibn 'Abbas:that the Prophet (ﷺ) said: \Beware of narrating from me except what I taught you"""
"2951","Narrated Jundab bin 'Abdullah:that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \Whoever says (something) about the Qur'an according to his own opinion and he is correct"""
"2952","Qutaybah narrated to us, he said: Ḥammād ibn Yaḥyya al-Abaḥḥ narrated to us, from Thābit al-Bunānī, from Anas (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said:\n\n\The example of my Ummah is like the rain; it is not known whether its beginning is better or its end.\""\n\nHe (the author) said: In this chapter"
"2953","Narrated 'Adiyy bin Hatim:that the Prophet (ﷺ) said: \The Jews are those who Allah is wrath with"""
"2954","Narrated Abu Musa Al-Ash'ari:that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \Indeed Allah Most High created Adam from a handful that He took from all of the earth. So the children of Adam come in according with the earth"""
"2955","Narrated by al-Hasan ibn Ali al-Khallal and others, who said: Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, saying: Ma'mar informed us, from al-Zuhri, from Salim, from Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with both of them), who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said:\n\n\Verily"
"2956","Narrated 'Abdullah bin 'Amir bin Rabi'ah:from his father who said: \We were with the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) on a journey on a very dark night and we did not know where the Qiblah was. So each man among us prayed in his own direction. In the morning when we mentioned that to the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ)"""
"2957","Qutaybah narrated to us, who said: al-Mughirah ibn Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, from Abu al-Zinad, from al-A'raj, from Abu Hurayrah, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, said:\n\n\My example and the example of my Ummah is like that of a man who kindled a fire"
"2958","Narrated Ibn 'Umar:\The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) would perform voluntary Salat upon his mount facing whichever direction he was headed"""
"2959","Narrated Anas:that 'Umar bin Al-Khattab said: \O Messenger of Allah (ﷺ)! I wish that we could perform Salat behind the Maqam: So the following was revealed: And take you the Maqam of Ibrahim as a place of Salat. (2:)"""
"2960","Narrated Anas:that 'Umar bin Al-Khattab [may Allah be pleased with him] said: \I said: 'O Messenger of Allah (ﷺ)! I wish that you could perform Salat behind the Maqam of Ibrahim.' So the following was revealed: And take you the Maqam of Ibrahim as a place of Salat"""
"2961","Narrated Abu Sa'eed:that about Allah's saying: Thus we have made you a Wasata nation (2:143) - the Prophet (ﷺ) said: \The meaning of Wasata is just.\"" [Abu 'Eisa said: This Hadith is [Hasan] Sahih. (Another chain) From Abu Sa'eed who narrated that: \""The Messenger of Allah a said: 'Nuh will be called and it will be said: \""Did you deliver (the Message)? \""He will say: \""Yes\"" and his people will be called and it will be said: \""Did he call you?\"" They will say: \""No warner came to us. No one came to us.' It will be said: \""Who will testify for you?\"" So it is said: \""Muhammad and his Ummah (community).\"" He (ﷺ) said: You will be brought to testify that he delivered (the Message) and that is His saying: Thus"""
"2962","Narrated Al-Bara bin 'Azib:\When the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) arrived in Al-Madinah"""
"2963","**Muḥammad ibn Bashshār narrated to us, he said:** Abū Aḥmad narrated to us, he said: Sufyān narrated to us, from Ibn Abī Laylā, from his brother, ʿĪsā, from ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Abī Laylā, from Abū Ayyūb al-Anṣārī رضي الله عنه, that he had a storehouse in which there was dates, and a **ghūl** (a type of jinn or devil) used to come and take from it.\n\nHe said: So he complained about that to the Prophet ﷺ. The Prophet ﷺ said: **\Go"
"2964","Narrated Ibn 'Abbas:\When the Prophet (ﷺ) began facing the Ka'bah they said: 'O Messenger of Allah! How about our brothers who died while they were praying toward Bait Al-Maqdis?' So Allah Most High revealed: Allah would not allow your faith to be wasted. (2:)"""
"2965","Narrated Az-Zuhri:that 'Urqah said: \I said to 'Aishah: 'I do not see anything wrong if someone does not go between As-Safa and Al-Marwah"""
"2966","Narrated 'Asim Al-Ahwal:""I asked Anas bin Malik about As-Safa and Al-Marwah, and he said: 'They were among the rites of Jahiliyyah.' He said: 'So during Islam, we refrained from them, then Allah, Blessed and Most High, revealed: Indeed As-Safa and Al-Marwah are of the symbols of Allah. So it is not a sin for those who perform Hajj or 'Umrah to the house to go between them. (2:158)' He said: 'So it is voluntarily then verily, Allah is the All-Recogniser, the All-Knowing. (2:)"
"2967","Narrated Jabir bin 'Abdullah:\When the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) arrived in Makkah"""
"2968","Narrated Al-Bara bin 'Azib:\It was the custom among the Companions of Muhammad (ﷺ)"""
"2969","Narrated An-Nu'man bin Bashir:from the Prophet (ﷺ) regarding Allah's saying: Your Lord said: Invoke Me"
"2970","Narrated 'Adi bin Hatim:\When 'Until the white (light) thread of dawn appears distinct to you from the black thread (of night)' was revealed"""
"2971","Narrated 'Adi bin Hatim:\I asked the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) about the fast"""
"2972","Narrated Aslam bin 'Imran At-Tujibi:\We were in a Roman city"
"2973","Narrated Mujahid:that Ka'b bin 'Ujrah said: \By the one in Whose Hand is my soul! This Ayah was revealed referring to my case: 'And whosoever of you is ill or has an ailment on his scalp (necessitating shaving) he must pay Fidyah of either fasting or giving charity"""
"2974","Narrated 'Abdur-Rahman bin Abi Laila:from Ka'b bin 'Ujrah who said: \The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) came to me while I was lighting a fire under a pot"""
"2975","Narrated 'Abdur-Rahman bin Ya'mar:that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \The Hajj is 'Arafat"""
"2976","Narrated 'Aishah:that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \The most hated man to Allah is the most quarrelsome"""
"2977","**Narrated by Ibn 'Abbas (may Allah be pleased with both of):**\n\nThe Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) said: \When Az-Zilzal (Surah 99) is recited"
"2978","Narrated Jabir:\The Jews would say: \""Whoever goes into his wife's vagina from behind her"""
"2979","**Narrated by Awfa ibn Malik** (may Allah be pleased with him):\n\nQutaybah and Muhammad ibn Bashshar narrated to us, they both said: 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi narrated to us, he said: Za'idah narrated to us, from Mansur, from Hilal ibn Yasaf, from Rabi' ibn Khuthaym, from 'Amr ibn Maymun, from 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Layla, from a woman — she being the wife of Abu Ayyub — from Abu Ayyub (may Allah be pleased with him), who said:\n\nThe Messenger of Allah ﷺ said:\n\n**\Is it not within the ability of any one of you to recite one-third of the Qur'an in a single night?\""""""""**\n\nHe ﷺ then said: **\""""""""Reciting *Qul Huwa Allahu Ahad* (Surah Al-Ikhlas) constitutes one-third of the Qur'an.\""""""""**\n\n**Sub-narrators (Taba'at):** There are narrations on this topic from Abu al-Darda'"
"2980","Narrated Ibn 'Abbas:\'Umar came to the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) and said: 'O Messenger of Allah! I am ruined!' He said: 'Why are you ruined?' He said: 'I turned my mount during the night (meaning that he went into his wife from behind).'\"" He said: \""So the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) did not say anything in reply to him. Then Allah revealed this Ayah to the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ): 'Your wives are a tilth for you"""
"2981","Narrated Al-Hasan:from Ma'qil bin Yasar that he married his sister to a man among the Muslims during the time of the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ). She remained with him as long as she did"
"2982","**Narrated by Abū Hurayrah (may Allāh be pleased with him):**\n\nThe Messenger of Allāh, peace and blessings be upon him, said:\n\n> **\Say: He is Allāh"
"2983","Narrated Samurah bin Jundab:\The Prophet of Allah (ﷺ) said: 'The middle Salat is Salat Al-'Asr"""
"2984","Narrated:'Ubaidah As-Salmani that 'Ali narrated to him that on the Day of Al-Ahzab the Prophet (ﷺ) said: \O Allah! Fill their graves and their homes with fire as they have kept us busy from Salat Al-Wusta (the middle prayer) until the sun set"""
"2985","Narrated 'Abdullah bin Mas'ud:that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \Salat Al-Wusta is Salat Al-'Asr"""
"2986","Narrated Zaid bin Arqam:\During the time of the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ)"""
"2987","Narrated Abu Malik:from Al-Bara (regarding): And do not aim at that which is bad to spend from it (2:267) - he said: \It was revealed about us"""
"2988","Narrated 'Abdullah bin Mas'ud:that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \Indeed the Shaitan has an effect on the son of Adam"""
"2989","Narrated Abu Hurairah:that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \O you people! Indeed Allah is Tayyib (good) and he does not accept but what is good. And indeed Allah ordered the believers with what He ordered the Messengers. He (ﷺ) said: 'O you Messengers! Eat of the good things and do righteous deeds. Verily I am well acquainted with what you do (23:51).' And He said: 'O you who believe! Eat from the good things We have provided you (2:172).' He said: \""And he mentioned a man: 'Who is undertaking a long journey"""
"2990","Narrated Isra'il:from As-Suddi who said: \Someone who heard from 'Ali"""
"2991","Maḥmūd ibn Ghaylān narrated to us; Bishr ibn al-Sarī narrated to us; Sufyān narrated to us, from ʿAlqamah ibn Marthad, from Abū ʿAbd al-Raḥmān al-Sulamī, from ʿUthmān ibn ʿAffān, who said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: ""The best of you—or the most virtuous of you—is the one who learns the Qur'an and teaches it."" This is a ḥasan ṣaḥīḥ ḥadīth. And thus ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Mahdī and others narrated from Sufyān al-Thawrī, from ʿAlqamah ibn Marthad, from Abū ʿAbd al-Raḥmān, from ʿUthmān, from the Prophet ﷺ. Sufyān does not mention Saʿd ibn ʿUbaydah in it. And Yaḥyā ibn Saʿīd al-Qaṭṭān narrated this ḥadīth from Sufyān and Shuʿbah, from ʿAlqamah ibn Marthad, from Saʿd ibn ʿUbaydah, from Abū ʿAbd al-Raḥmān, from ʿUthmān, from the Prophet ﷺ. Muḥammad ibn Bashshār narrated this to us, saying: Yaḥyā ibn Saʿīd narrated to us from Sufyān and Shuʿbah. Muḥammad ibn Bashshār said: Thus Yaḥyā ibn Saʿīd narrated it from Sufyān and Shuʿbah, more than once, from ʿAlqamah ibn Marthad, from Saʿd ibn ʿUbaydah, from Abū ʿAbd al-Raḥmān, from ʿUthmān, from the Prophet ﷺ. Muḥammad ibn Bashshār said: The companions of Sufyān do not mention Saʿd ibn ʿUbaydah from Sufyān. Muḥammad ibn Bashshār said: And that is more correct. Abū ʿĪsā said: Shuʿbah added Saʿd ibn ʿUbaydah to the chain of this ḥadīth, and Sufyān's ḥadīth seems more likely. ʿAlī ibn ʿAbd Allāh said: Yaḥyā ibn Saʿīd said: ""No one equals Shuʿbah in my view. If Sufyān contradicts him, I follow Sufyān's opinion."" Abū ʿĪsā said: I heard Abū ʿAmmār mention from Wakīʿ that Shuʿbah said: ""Sufyān is more retentive than I. Whatever Sufyān narrated to me from anyone, I never asked him about it except I found it exactly as he narrated it."" And in this chapter there are narrations from ʿAlī and Saʿd."
"2992","Narrated Ibn 'Abbas:\When this Ayah was revealed: And whether you disclose what is in yourselves or conceal it"""
"2993","Narrated 'Aishah:""I asked the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) about Allah's saying: So, as for those in whose hearts there is a deviation, they follow that which is not entirely clear thereof, seeking Al-Fitnah and seeking its Ta'wil (3:7). He said: 'When you see them, be aware of them.'"" Yazid (one of the narrators in the chain) said: ""When you see them, be aware of them' - she said it two or three times"
"2994","Narrated 'Aishah:\The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) was asked about this Ayah: 'It is He who sent down to you the Book. In it are Ayat that are entirely clear... (3:7)' until the end of the Ayah. So the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: 'When you see those who seek what is not entirely clear thereof"""
"2995","Narrated 'Abdullah:that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \Every Prophet had a Wali among the Prophets. My Wali is my father Ibrahim the Khalil of my Lord.\"" Then he recited: Verily among mankind who have the best claim to Ibrahim"""
"2996","Narrated 'Abdullah:that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \Whoever takes a false oath to deprive a Muslim of his property"""
"2997","Narrated Anas:\When this Ayah was revealed: By no means shall you attain Al-Birr unless you spend of that which you love (3:92). Or"""
"2998","Narrated Ibn 'Umar:\A man stood before the Prophet (ﷺ) and said: 'Who is the (real) Hajj pilgrim"""
"2999","Narrated 'Amir bin Sa'd bin Abi Waqqas:from his father who said: \When this Ayah was revealed: 'Come"""
"3000","Narrated Abu Ghalib:\Abu Umamah saw heads (of the Khawarij) hanging on the streets of Damascus. He said: 'The dogs of the Fire and the worst dead people under the canopy of the heavens. The best dead men are those whom these have killed.' He then recited: On the Day when some faces will become white and some faces will become black... (3:106) until the end of the Ayah. I said to Abu Umamah: 'Did you hear it from the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ)?' He said: 'If I had not heard it but one time"""
"3001","Muḥammad ibn Ismāʿīl al-Wāsiṭī narrated to us, saying: Wakīʿ narrated to us, saying: Abū Farwah Yazīd ibn Sinān narrated to us, from al-Mubārak, from Ṣuhayb, who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, said: \He has not believed in the Quran who makes lawful its prohibitions.\""\n\nAbū ʿĪsā said: This hadith is not strong in its chain of narration"
"3002","**Narrated by al-Hasan ibn 'Arafah, who said:** Isma'il ibn 'Ayyash narrated to us, from Bahir ibn Sa'd, from Khalid ibn Ma'dan, from Kathir ibn Murrah al-Hadrami, from 'Uqbah ibn 'Amir, who said:\n\n\I heard the Messenger of Allah"
"3003","Narrated Anas:\The face of the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) was wounded"""
"3004","Narrated Salim bin 'Abdullah bin 'Umar:from his father: \On the Day of Uhud"""
"3005","Narrated 'Abdullah bin 'Umar:\The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) was supplicating against four people"""
"3006","Narrated Asma bin Al-Hakam Al-Farazi:\I heard 'Ali saying: 'Indeed I am a man who"""
"3007","Narrated Anas:that Abu Talhah said: \I raised my head to look around on the Day of Uhud"""
"3008","**Jābir ibn 'Abdillāh (may Allāh be pleased with him) reported:**\n\n> The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) used to present himself at the [Makkah] stopping-place, saying: *\Is there not a man who will carry me to his people? For Quraysh have prevented me from conveying the speech of my Lord.\""""""""*\n\n**Abū 'Īsā (al-Tirmidhī) said:** This is a *gharīb ṣaḥīḥ* (unauthenticated yet sound) hadith.\n\n- **'Uthmān ibn al-Mughīrah** narrates from **Sālim ibn Abī al-Ja'd**"
"3009","Narrated Khusaif:from Miqsam that Ibn 'Abbas said: \This Ayah: It is not for a Prophet to illegally take a part of the booty... (3:161) was revealed about a red robe that was missing from the Day of Badr. Some of the people said: 'Perhaps the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) took it.' So Allah"""
"3010","Narrated Musa bin Ibrahim bin Kathir Al-Ansari:\I heard Talhah bin Khirash say: 'I heard Jabir bin 'Abdullah saying: \""The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) met me and said to me: 'O Jabir! Why do I see you upset?' I said: 'O Messenger of Allah! My father was martyred (on the Day of Uhud) leaving my family and debt behind.'\"" \""He (ﷺ) said: 'Shall I give you news of what your father met Allah with?'\"" He said: \""But of course O Messenger of Allah!\"" He said: 'Allah does not speak to anyone except from behind a veil"""
"3011","Narrated Masruq:from 'Abdullah that he was asked about Allah's saying: Think not of those as dead who are killed in the way of Allah. Nay they are alive"
"3012","Narrated Abu Wa'il:\'Abdullah [bin Mas'ud] narrating from the Prophet (ﷺ) that he said: 'There is no person who does not pay the Zakat due on his wealth but on the Day of Resurrection Allah will make a Shuja'a around his neck.' Then he recited the Ayah for us from the Book of Allah"""
"3013","Narrated Abu Hurairah:that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \Indeed the space in Paradise taken up by a whip"""
"3014","Narrated Humaid bin 'Abdur-Rahman bin 'Awf:that Marwan bin Al-Hakam said: \Go O Rafi' - who was his gate-keeper - \""to Ibn 'Abbas and say to him: 'If every person who rejoices with what he has done"""
"3015","Narrated by Yahya ibn Musa, who said: Waki' and Hilal ibn Hisham narrated to us, saying: Harun al-Nahwi narrated to us, from Thabit al-Bunani, from Shahr ibn Hawshab, from Umm Salamah (may Allah be pleased with her), that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) recited this verse: \Indeed"
"3016","Narrated Ubayy ibn Ka'b (may Allah be pleased with him), that the Prophet ﷺ recited the verse **\You have reached"
"3017","Narrated Abu Sa'eed Al-Khudri:\We captured some women on the Day of Awtas and they had husbands among their people. That was mentioned to the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) so Allah revealed: '...And women already married"""
"3018","Narrated 'Ubaidullah bin Abi Bakr [bin Anas]:from Anas bin Malik"
"3019","Narrated 'Abdur-Rahman bin Abi Bakrah:from his father that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \Shall I not narrate to you about the worst of the major sins?\"" They said: \""Of course O Messenger of Allah!\"" He said: \""Associating others with Allah and disobeying the parents.\"" He said: \""And he sat reclining and said: 'The false testimony.' Or he said: 'The false statement.'\"" He said: \""So the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) would not stop saying it until we said (to ourselves): 'If he would only stop"""
"3020","Narrated Abu Umamah Al-Ansari:from 'Abdullah bin Unais Al-Juhni who said: \The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: 'Indeed among the worst of the major sins is Shirk with Allah"""
"3021","Narrated 'Abdullah bin 'Amr:that the Prophet (ﷺ) said: \The major sins are associating others with Allah"""
"3022","Narrated Mujahid:from Umm Salamah that she said: \The men fight and the women do not fight"""
"3023","Narrated 'Amr bin Dinar:from a man among the children of Umm Salamah"
"3024","Narrated 'Alqamah:\'Abdullah said: 'The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) commanded me to recite for him while he was on the Minbar. So I recited from Surat An-Nisa for him"""
"3025","Narrated Ibrahim:from 'Abidah that 'Abdullah said: \The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said to me: 'Recite for me.' I said: 'O Messenger of Allah! Shall I recite for you while it is to you whom it was revealed?' He said: 'I love to hear it from other than me.'\"" So I recited Surat An-Nisa until I reached: \""...And We bring you (Muhammad) as a witness against these people? (4:41)\"" He said: \""So I saw the eyes of the Prophet (ﷺ) overflowing with tears"""
"3026","Narrated Abu 'Abdur-Rahman As-Sulami:that 'Ali bin Abi Talib said: \'Abdur-Rahman bin 'Awf prepared some food for which he invited us"""
"3027","Narrated 'Urwah bin Az-Zubair:that 'Abdullah bin Az-Zubair narrated to him: \A man from the Ansar was arguing with Az-Zubair about a stream at Al-Harrah with which they irrigated their date-palms. So the Ansari man said: 'Let the water pass through.' But he refused"""
"3028","Narrated 'Abdullah bin Yazid:from Zaid bin Thabit that he heard about this Ayah: Then what is the matter with you that you are divided into two parties about the hypocrites? (4:88) He said: \People among the Companions of the Prophet (ﷺ) returned on the Day of Uhud and there were two parties among them"""
"3029","Narrated 'Amr bin Dinar:from Ibn 'Abbas that the Prophet (ﷺ) said: \On the Day of Judgement"""
"3030","Narrated Ibn 'Abbas:\A man from Banu Sulaim who had some sheep with him"""
"3031","Narrated Al-Bara bin 'Azib:\When the following was revealed: 'Not equal are those of the believers who sit (4:95)' 'Amr bin Umm Maktum came to the Prophet (ﷺ).\"" He said: \""He was blind"""
"3032","**Narrated by 'Abdullāh ibn 'Amr (may Allāh be pleased with him):**\n\nThe Prophet ﷺ said:\n\n**\He who recites the Qur'ān in less than three days does not understand it.\""""""""**\n\n**Narrated to us Maḥmūd ibn Ghaylān** — he said: **Narrated to us** **al-Naḍr ibn Shumayl** — he said: **Narrated to us Shu'bah**"
"3033","Narrated Ya'la bin Umayyah:\I said to 'Umar [bin Al-Khattab]: 'Allah said: That you shorten the Salat if you fear and the people are safe (4:101).' So 'Umar said: 'I wondered about that just as you have wondered. So I mentioned that to the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ)"""
"3034","Narrated Abu Hurairah:that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) halted between Dajnan and 'Usfan"
"3035","Narrated Qatadah bin An-Nu'man:\There was a household among us called Banu Ubairiq"""
"3036","Narrated Thuwair - Ibn Abi Fakhitah:from his father that 'Ali bin Abi Talib said: \There is no Ayah in the Qur'an more beloved to me than this Ayah: Verily Allah forgives not associating others with Him"""
"3037","Narrated Abu Hurairah:\When the following was revealed: 'Whoever works evil will have the recompense of it... (4:123)' That worried the Muslims"""
"3038","Narrated Abu Bakr As-Siddiq:\I was with the Prophet (ﷺ) when this Ayah was revealed to him: Whoever works evil will have the recompense of it (4:123). So the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: 'O Abu Bakr! Shall I recite to you an Ayah revealed to me?' I said: 'Of course O Messenger of Allah!' So he recited it to me"""
"3039","Narrated Ibn 'Abbas:\Sawdah feared that the Prophet (ﷺ) was going to divorce her"""
"3040","Abd ibn Humayd narrated to us, Abd al-Razzaq informed us, from Ma'mar, from Hammam ibn Munabbih, from Abu Hurayrah (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said regarding His (Exalted is He) words: \Enter the gate prostrating\"" (Qur'an 2:58)"
"3041","Narrated Al-Bara:\A man came to the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) and said: 'O Messenger of Allah! They ask you about a legal verdict. Say: \""Allah directs (thus) regarding Al-Kalalah (4:176).\"" So the Prophet (ﷺ) said to him: \""You should be sufficed with the Ayah of summer.\"" (Meaning this Ayah"""
"3042","Narrated Tariq bin Shihab:\A man among the Jews said to 'Umar bin Al-Khattab: 'O Commander of the Believers! If we were the ones unto whom this Ayah was revealed"""
"3043","Abd ibn Humayd narrated to us, al-Hajjaj ibn Minhal narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated from Humayd, from Anas"
"3044","Narrated Abu Hurairah:\The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: 'Ar-Rahman's Hand is full"""
"3045","Narrated 'Aishah:\The Prophet (ﷺ) was being guarded until this Ayah was revealed: 'Allah will protect you from mankind.' So the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) stuck his head out from the room and said: 'O you people! Go away"""
"3046","Narrated 'Abdullah bin Mas'ud:\The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: 'When the Children of Isra'il fell into disobedience"""
"3047","Narrated Abu 'Ubaidah:\The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: 'When the Children of Isra'il fell into decline"""
"3048","Narrated 'Amr bin Shurahbil [Abu Maisarah]:from 'Umar bin Al-Khattab"
"3049","Narrated Al-Bara:\A man among the Companions of the Prophet (ﷺ) died before Khamr had been made unlawful. So when Khamr was made unlawful"""
"3050","Narrated Al-Bara bin 'Azib:\Some people among the Companions of the Prophet (ﷺ) died while they had been drinking Khamr. So when it was revealed that it was unlawful"""
"3051","Narrated Ibn 'Abbas:\They (the Companions) said: 'O Messenger of Allah"""
"3052","Narrated 'Abdullah:\When (the following) was revealed: Those who believe and do righteous good deeds"""
"3053","Narrated 'Ikrimah:from Ibn 'Abbas: \A man came to the Prophet (ﷺ) and said: 'O Messenger of Allah! When I consume meat and I get around women"""
"3054","Narrated Abu Al-Bukhtari:from 'Ali who said: \When (the following) was revealed: And Hajj to the House is a duty that mankind owes to Allah"""
"3055","Narrated Anas bin Malik:that a man said: \O Messenger of Allah! Who is my father?\"" He said: \""Your father is so-and-so.\"" He said: \""So (the following) was revealed: O you who believe! Ask not about things which"""
"3056","Narrated Abu Bakr As-Siddiq:\O you people! You recite this Ayah: Take care of yourselves! If you follow the guidance no harm shall come to you from those who are astray (5:105). I indeed heard the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) saying: 'When the people see the wrongdoer"""
"3057","Narrated Abu Umayah Ash-Sha'bani:\I went to Abu Tha'balah Al-Khushani and said to him: 'How do you deal with this Ayah?' He said: 'Which Ayah?' I said: 'Allah's saying: Take care of yourselves! If you follow the guidance no harm shall come to you (5:105).' He said: 'Well"""
"3058","**Narrated Ka'b ibn 'Ujrah (may Allah be pleased with him):**\n\nHe said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) came upon me while I was kindling a fire beneath a cooking pot, and lice were falling upon my forehead — or he said, upon my eyebrows. So he (peace and blessings be upon him) said: **\Do the vermin of your head harm you?\""**\n\nHe said: I replied"
"3059","Narrated Ibn 'Abbas:\A man from Banu Sahm went out with Tamim Ad-Dari and 'Adi bin Badda. The Sahmi man died in a land in which there were no Muslims. When they arrived with what he left behind"""
"3060","Narrated 'Ammar bin Yasir:\The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: 'The Ma'idah was sent down from the Heavens with bread and meat. And they were commanded to not be deceitful with it and hide it for tomorrow. So they were deceitful with it and they hid it"""
"3061","Abd ibn Humayd narrated to us, Sulaymān ibn Ḥarb narrated to me, Ḥammād ibn Salamah narrated to us from Thābit, from Anas رضي الله عنه, who said:\n\n\The Jews"
"3062","Narrated 'Abdullah bin 'Amr:\The last Surah revealed was Surat Al-Ma'idah and Al-Fath"""
"3063","Narrated 'Ali:\Abu Jahl said to the Prophet (ﷺ): 'We do not deny you"""
"3064","Narrated Jabir bin 'Abdullah:\When Allah revealed this Ayah: 'Say: He has the power to send torment on you from above or from under your feet...' The Prophet (ﷺ) said: 'I seek refuge in Your Face.' So when (the following) was revealed: 'Or to cover you in confusion in party strife"""
"3065","**Narrated by 'Abd ibn Humayd** — who said: **Hisham ibn al-Qasim** narrated to us — from **al-Mubarak ibn Fadalah** — from **al-Hasan** — from **Ma'qil ibn Yasar** (may Allah be pleased with him):\n\nThat he gave his sister in marriage to a man from among the Muslims during the era of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. She remained with him for a time, after which he divorced her with a single divorce and did not take her back until her waiting period ('iddah) had expired. Then both he and she developed a mutual longing for one another. Subsequently, he sought her hand in marriage along with other suitors. Ma'qil (may Allah be pleased with him) said to him: \O wretched fellow! I honoured you by giving her to you in marriage"
"3066","Narrated 'Abdullah:\When (the following) was revealed: It is those who believe and confuse not their belief with Zulm (wrong) (6:82) - That bothered some Muslims"""
"3067","Narrated Masruq:\I was reclining in the presence of 'Aishah when she said: 'O Abu 'Aishah! There are three things"""
"3068","Narrated 'Abdullah bin 'Abbas:\Some people came to the Prophet (ﷺ) and they said: 'O Messenger of Allah! Why is it that we can eat what we kill but we can not eat what Allah has killed?' So Allah revealed: So eat of that on which Allah's Name has been mentioned if you are indeed believers in His Ayat...\"" up to His saying: ...And if you obey them"""
"3069","Narrated 'Abdullah bin Mas'ud:\Whoever wishes to look at the Sahifah which Muhammad (ﷺ) placed his seal upon"""
"3070","**Narrated by Zayd ibn Arqam (may Allah be pleased with him):**\n\nAhmad ibn Mani' narrated to us, who said: Marwan ibn Mu'awiyah, Yazid ibn Harun, and Muhammad ibn 'Ubaid narrated to us, from Isma'il ibn Abi Khalid, from al-Harith ibn Shubayl, from Abu 'Amr al-Shaybani, from Zayd ibn Arqam (may Allah be pleased with him), who said:\n\n\We used to speak during the prayer in the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him)"
"3071","ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān narrated to us; ʿUbayd Allāh ibn Mūsā informed us, from Isrāʾīl, from al-Suddī, from Abū Mālik, from al-Barāʾ: (And do not aim at the bad to spend from it.) He said: It was revealed concerning us, the Anṣār. We were people of date palms. A man would bring from his dates according to their abundance or scarcity. A man would bring a bunch or two and hang it in the mosque. The people of the Suffah had no food. When one of them got hungry, he would come to the bunch, strike it with his staff, and the unripe and ripe dates would fall, and he would eat. Some people who did not desire good would bring a bunch containing bad and unripe dates, or a broken bunch, and hang it. So Allah revealed: (O you who have believed, spend from the good things which you have earned and from what We have produced for you from the earth. And do not aim at the bad to spend from it, while you would not take it yourselves except with closed eyes and reluctance.) They said: ""If one of you were gifted the like of what he gave, he would not take it except with closing eyes and shame."" He said: So after that, each of us would bring the best of what he had. Abū ʿĪsā said: This is a ḥasan gharīb ṣaḥīḥ ḥadīth. Abū Mālik is al-Ghifārī, and it is said his name is Ghazwān. And Sufyān narrated something of this from al-Suddī."
"3072","Narrated Abu Hurairah:that the Prophet (ﷺ) said: ""There are three, for which when they appear, a soul will not benefit by its faith, if it did not believe before the Signs: Ad-Dajjal, the Beast, and the rising of the sun from its setting place"" - or ""from the west"
"3073","Narrated Abu Hurairah:that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: ""Allah, Blessed and Most High, has said - and His saying is the Truth: 'When My slave considers doing something good then write it as one good for him. If he acts upon it then write ten of the same for him. And when he considers doing something evil, then do not write it. If he acts upon it, then write it. If he leaves it"" - and perhaps he said: ""if he does not act upon it, then write a good reward for him.'"" Then he [the Prophet (ﷺ)] recited: Whoever comes with a good, then he shall have ten the like thereof (6:)"
"3074","Narrated Muslim bin Yasar Al-Juhani:that 'Umar bin Al-Khattab was asked about this Ayah: And when your Lord brought forth from the Children of Adam"
"3075","Narrated Abu Hurairah:that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \When Allah created Adam He wiped his back and every person that He created among his offspring until the Day of Resurrection fell out of his back. He placed a ray of light between the eyes of every person. Then He showed them to Adam and he said: 'O Lord! Who are these people?' He said: 'These are your offspring.' He saw one of them whose ray between his eyes amazed him"""
"3076","Narrated Samurah bin Jundab:that the Prophet (ﷺ) said: \When Hawwa became pregnant"""
"3077","Narrated Abu Hurairah:that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \When Allah created Adam\"" (and he mentioned) the Hadith"""
"3078","Narrated Mus'ab bin Sa'd:from his father who said: \On the Day of Badr I brought a sword so I said: 'O Messenger of Allah! Indeed Allah has satisfied my breast (i.e. my desire) on the idolaters - or something like that - give me this sword.' So he said: 'This is not for me"""
"3079","Narrated Mus'ab bin Sa'd:from his father who said: ""On the Day of Badr I brought a sword so I said: 'O Messenger of Allah! Indeed Allah has satisfied my breast (i.e. my desire) on the idolaters - or something like that - give me this sword.' So he said: 'This is not for me, nor is it for you.' I said: 'Perhaps he will give this to someone who did not go through some struggle I went through (fighting).' So the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) came to me [and he said:] 'You asked me, but it was not up to me. But now it has occurred that it is up to me, so it is yours.'"" He said: ""So (the following) was revealed: They ask you about the spoils of war (8:)"
"3080","**It was narrated to us by Hannād, who narrated to us from Abū Mu'āwiyah, from al-A'mash, from Shaqīq ibn Salamah, from 'Abdullāh (may Allāh be pleased with him), who said:**\n\nThe Messenger of Allāh (peace and blessings be upon him) said:\n\n> **\Whoever takes an oath upon a falsehood in order to usurp the wealth of a Muslim"
"3081","Narrated to us Ishaq ibn Mansur, who narrated to us Abdullah ibn Bakr al-Sahmi, who narrated to us Humayd, from Anas رضي الله عنه, who said:\n\nWhen this verse was lan: **\Never will you attain [true] righteousness until you spend [in charity] from that which you love\""** (Aal-‘Imran 3:92) — or"
"3082","Narrated 'Uqbah bin 'Amir:that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) recited this Ayah upon the Minbar: And make ready against them all you can of power (8:60). He said: \Verily! Power is shooting\"" - three times - \""Verily! Allah will open the earth for you and suffice you with supplies"""
"3083","Narrated 'Amr bin Murrah:that Abu 'Ubaidah bin 'Abdullah narrated from 'Abdullah bin Mas'ud who said: \On the Day of Badr"""
"3084","Narrated Abu Hurairah:that the Prophet (ﷺ) said: \None of the black heads (meaning the Children of Adam since (most of) their heads are black) before you partook of spoils of war"""
"3085","Narrated Ibn 'Abbas:\I said to 'Uthman bin 'Affan: 'What was your reasoning with Al-Anfal - while it is from the Muthani (Surah with less than one-hundred Ayat)"""
"3086","Narrated Sulaiman bin 'Amr bin Al-Ahwas:\My father narrated to me that he attended the Farewell Hajj with the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ). He (ﷺ) expressed his gratitude to Allah and praised Him"""
"3087","Narrated 'Ali:\I asked the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) about the day of Al-Hajj Al-Akbar"""
"3088","Narrated 'Ali:""I asked the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) about the day of Al-Hajj Al-Akbar, and he said: ""The day of An-Nahr"
"3089","Narrated Anas bin Malik:\The Prophet (ﷺ) sent Abu Bakr with the (announcement of) Bara'ah (the declaration to publicize the disavowal of the idolaters). Then he summoned him and said: 'It is not right for anyone to convey this except a man among my family.'\""So he called for 'Ali and gave it to him"""
"3090","Narrated Ibn 'Abbas:\The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) dispatched Abu Bakr ordering him to announce these statements. Then 'Ali followed him. When Abu Bakr was at a particular road"""
"3091","Narrated Zaid bin Yuthai':\We asked 'Ali what he had been dispatched with during the Hajj. He said: 'I was sent with four: That there shall be no Tawaf around the House while naked"""
"3092","Narrated Abu Sa'eed:that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \When you see a man frequenting the Masjid"""
"3093","Narrated Thawban:\When (the following) was revealed: And those who hoard up gold and silver... (9:34)\"" He said: \""We were with the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) during one of his journeys"""
"3094","Narrated 'Adi bin Hatim:\I came to the Prophet (ﷺ) while I had a cross of gold around my neck. He said: 'O 'Adi! Remove this idol from yourself!' And I heard him reciting from Surah Bara'ah: They took their rabbis and monks as lords besides Allah (9:31). He said: 'As for them"""
"3095","Narrated by Ibn Abi 'Umar, narrated by Sufyan, from Al-A'mash, from Abdullah ibn Murrah, from Masruq, from Abdullah ibn Mas'ud (may Allah be pleased with him), that he was asked regarding the statement of Allah, the Most High: *\And never think of those who have been killed in the cause of Allah as dead. Rather"
"3096","Narrated Ibn 'Abbas:\I heard 'Umar bin Al-Khattab saying: 'When 'Abdullah bin Ubayy died"""
"3097","Narrated Ibn 'Umar:\'Abdullah bin 'Abdullah bin Ubayy came to the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) when his father died"""
"3098","Narrated Abu Sa'eed Al-Khudri:\Two men disagreed over the Masjid whose foundation was laid upon Taqwa from the first day (9:108). A man said: 'It is Masjid Quba' and the other said: 'It is the Masjid of the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ).' So the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: 'It is this Masjid of mine"""
"3099","Narrated Abu Hurairah:that the Prophet (ﷺ) said: \This Ayah was revealed about the people of Quba: In it are men who love to purify themselves. And Allah loves those who make themselves pure (9:108).\"" He said: \""They used water to perform Istinja so this Ayah was revealed about them"""
"3100","Narrated 'Ali:\I heard a man seeking forgiveness for his parents who were idolaters"""
"3101","Narrated 'Abdur-Rahman bin Ka'b bin Malik:from his father who said: \I did not remain behind from any of the battles the Prophet (ﷺ) fought in"""
"3102","Narrated by Muhammad ibn 'Abd al-A'la al-San'ani, from Khalid ibn al-Harith, from Shu'bah, from 'Ubaydullah ibn Abi Bakr ibn Anas, from Anas (may Allah be pleased with him), from the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him), regarding the major sins, he (peace and blessings be upon him) said:\n\n\Associating partners with Allah"
"3103","Narrated Az-Zuhri:from Anas who said: \Hudhaifah bin Al-Yaman came to 'Uthman"""
"3104","Abdullah ibn Unays al-Juhani (may Allah be pleased with him) reported that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said:\n\n\Indeed"
"3105","Narrated 'Ata bin Yasar:from a man among the people of Egypt who said: \I asked Abu Ad-Darda about this Ayah: For them is good news in the life of the present world (10:64). He said: 'No one asked me about since I asked the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) about it"""
"3106","Narrated Ibn 'Abbas:that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \When Allah drowned Fir'awn he said: 'I believe that there is no god except the One that the children of Isra'il believe in.' So Jibrail said: 'O Muhammad! If you could only have seen me"""
"3107","Narrated Shu'bah:\'Adi bin Thabit and 'Ata bin As-Sa'ib informed me"""
"3108","Narrated Waki' bin Hudus:from his uncle Abu Razin who said: \I said: 'O Messenger of Allah! Where was our Lord before He created His creation?' He said: 'He was (above) the clouds - no air was under him"""
"3109","Narrated Abu Musa:that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \Indeed Allah Blessed and Most High gives respite (Yumli)\"" and perhaps he said: \""(Yumhil)\"" respite to the wrong-doer until"""
"3110","Narrated Ibn 'Umar:that 'Umar bin Al-Khattab said: \When this Ayah was revealed: Some among them will be wretches and (others) blessed (11:105). I asked the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) saying: 'O Prophet of Allah! Based upon what are we then working; something that has already finished or something that has not yet happened?' He said: 'Rather something that has happened"""
"3111","Narrated 'Abdullah:\A man came to the Prophet (ﷺ) and said: 'I fondled a woman who lives on the edge of Al-Madinah"""
"3112","Narrated Mu'adh bin Jabal:\A man came to the Prophet (ﷺ) and said: 'O Messenger of Allah! What do you say about a man who meets a woman and there is no acquaintance between them. So there is nothing that a man who would do with his wife but he does it with her"""
"3113","Narrated Ibn Mas'ud:that a man unlawfully kissed a woman. So he came to the Prophet (ﷺ) to ask him about its atonement. So (the following) Ayah was revealed: And perform the Salat"
"3114","Narrated Musa bin Talhah:that Abu Al-Yasar said: \A woman came to me selling dates. I said to her: 'There are better dates than these in the house.' So she entered the house with me. I had an urge for her so I began kissing her. I went to Abu Bakr and mentioned that to him"""
"3115","Narrated Musa bin Talhah:that Abu Al-Yasar said: ""A woman came to me selling dates. I said to her: 'There are better dates than these in the house.' So she entered the house with me. I had an urge for her so I began kissing her. I went to Abu Bakr and mentioned that to him, so he said: 'Cover what you have done, repent, do not inform any one, and never do it again.' So I went to 'Umar and mentioned that to him. He said: 'Cover what you have done, repent, do not inform any one, and never do it again.' Then I went to the Prophet (ﷺ) and mentioned it to him."" He said: 'Is this how you take care of the wife of someone who is away fighting in Allah's cause?"" Such that he had wished he had not accepted Islam until that very time, and he thought that he must be one of the people of the Fire."" He said: ""The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) bowed his head for a long time, until Allah revealed to him: And perform the Salat, at the two ends of the day and in some hours of the night. Verily, the good deeds remove the evil deeds. That is a reminder for the mindful (11:114). Abu Al-Yasar said: ""So I went to him and the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) recited it for me. A companion of his said: ""O Messenger of Allah! Is this specific, or is it for the people in general?"" He said: ""Rather it is for the people in general"
"3116","Narrated Ibn 'Abbas:\The Jews came to the Prophet (ﷺ) and said: 'O Abul-Qasim! Inform us about the thunder"""
"3117","Narrated Abu Hurairah:that the Prophet (ﷺ) commented on: \Some of them We make more excellent than others to eat (13:4).\"" He said: \""The Daqal"""
"3118","Narrated Anas bin Malik:\The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) was brought a dish with unripe dates on it. He said: The parable of a goodly word is that of a goodly tree"""
"3119","Narrated Al-Bara:that regarding Allah's saying: Allah will keep firm those who believe"
"3120","Al-Ḥasan ibn Aḥmad ibn Abī Shuʿayb, Abū Muslim al-Ḥarrānī, narrated to us; Muḥammad ibn Salāmah al-Ḥarrānī narrated to us; Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq narrated to us, from ʿĀṣim ibn ʿUmar ibn Qatādah, from his father, from his grandfather, Qatādah ibn al-Nuʿmān, who said: There was a household among us called Banū al-Ubayriq: Bishr, Bashīr, and Mubashshir. Bashīr was a hypocritical man who composed poetry satirizing the Companions of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, then attributed it to some Arabs, saying: ""So-and-so said such-and-such."" When the Companions heard that poetry, they said: ""By Allah, only this vile person says this poetry,"" or as the man said. They said: ""The son of al-Ubayriq said it."" Their household was one of need and poverty in both Jāhiliyyah and Islam. The people's food in Medina was only dates and barley. If a man had means and a caravan arrived from Syria with raisins (darmak), he would buy from it for himself exclusively, while the family's food remained dates and barley. A caravan arrived from Syria. My uncle Rifāʿah ibn Zayd bought a load of darmak, placed it in his storage room (mashrabah), where there were also weapons, a coat of mail, and a sword. It was broken into from under the house; the storage room was breached, and the food and weapons were taken. In the morning, my uncle Rifāʿah came to me and said: ""O son of my brother, we were burgled last night. Our storage room was breached, and our food and weapons were taken."" I investigated in the house and asked. It was said to us: ""We saw Banū al-Ubayriq kindling a fire that night, and we only suspect them of having some of your food."" Banū al-Ubayriq said, while we were inquiring in the house: ""By Allah, we only see your companion as Labīd ibn Sahl, a man from us with righteousness and Islam."" When Labīd heard, he drew his sword and said: ""I steal? By Allah, this sword will mix with you, or you will clarify this theft."" They said: ""Away with it, man! You are not the one responsible."" We inquired in the house until we had no doubt they were the culprits. My uncle said to me: ""O son of my brother, if you went to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and mentioned this to him."" Qatādah said: I went to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said: ""A household among us, people of harshness, burgled my uncle Rifāʿah ibn Zayd, breached his storage room, and took his weapons and food. Let them return our weapons; as for the food, we have no need of it."" The Prophet ﷺ said: ""I will command concerning that."" When Banū al-Ubayriq heard, they went to a man among them called Asīr ibn ʿUrwah, spoke to him, and a group from the household gathered. They said: ""O Messenger of Allah, Qatādah ibn al-Nuʿmān and his uncle accused a household among us, people of Islam and righteousness, of theft without proof or evidence."" Qatādah said: I went to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and spoke to him. He said: ""You accused a household mentioned for Islam and righteousness of theft without proof or evidence."" I returned, wishing I had given some of my wealth and not spoken to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ about it. My uncle Rifāʿah came to me and said: ""O son of my brother, what did you do?"" I told him what the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to me. He said: ""Allah is the One sought for help."" Not long after, the Qur'an was revealed: (Indeed, We have revealed to you the Book in truth so you may judge between the people by what Allah has shown you. And do not be an advocate for the deceitful.) — Banū al-Ubayriq. (And seek forgiveness of Allah. Indeed, Allah is Forgiving, Merciful.) — i.e., for what you said to Qatādah. (And do not argue on behalf of those who deceive themselves. Indeed, Allah does not love one who is a habitually sinful deceiver. They conceal from the people, but they cannot conceal from Allah...) up to His saying: (Forgiving, Merciful.) — i.e., if they had sought Allah's forgiveness, He would have forgiven them. (And whoever earns sin, it is only against himself...) up to: (a clear sin.) — Their saying to Labīd: (And if not for the favor of Allah upon you and His mercy...) up to: (We would give him a great reward.) When the Qur'an was revealed, the weapons were brought to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and he returned them to Rifāʿah. Qatādah said: When I brought the weapons to my uncle, he was an old man who had become senile or nearly so in Jāhiliyyah, and I used to consider his Islam dubious. But when I brought him the weapons, he said: ""O son of my brother, it is in the cause of Allah."" Then I knew his Islam was sound. When the Qur'an was revealed, Bashīr fled to the polytheists and descended upon Sulāfah bint Saʿd ibn Sumayyah. Allah revealed: (And whoever opposes the Messenger after guidance has become clear to him and follows other than the way of the believers—We will give him what he has taken and burn him in Hell, and evil it is as a destination. Indeed, Allah does not forgive association with Him, but He forgives what is less than that for whom He wills. And whoever associates others with Allah has certainly gone far astray.) When it was revealed upon Sulāfah, Ḥassān ibn Thābit threw verses of his poetry at her. She took her saddle, placed it on her head, went out with it, and threw it in the Baṭḥāʾ, then said: ""You gifted me Ḥassān's poetry? You never brought me anything good."" Abū ʿĪsā said: This is a gharīb ḥadīth; we know of no one who narrated it with a chain except Muḥammad ibn Salāmah al-Ḥarrānī. Yūnus ibn Bukayr and others narrated this ḥadīth from Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq, from ʿĀṣim ibn ʿUmar ibn Qatādah, mursal (without mentioning his father from his grandfather). Qatādah ibn al-Nuʿmān is the maternal brother of Abū Saʿīd al-Khudrī. Abū Saʿīd al-Khudrī's name is Saʿd ibn Mālik ibn Sinān."
"3121","Narrated Ibn 'Abbas:\There was a woman who performed Salat behind the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) who was the most beautiful among the people. Some of the people would go forward to the first line so as not to see her. Others would go back to the last line so when he would bow"""
"3122","Narrated Ibn 'Umar:that the Prophet (ﷺ) said: \There are seven gates of Jahannam: Among them a gate for whoever carries a sword against my Ummah.\"" Or he said: \""Against the Ummah of Muhammad"""
"3123","Narrated Abu Hurairah:that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \Al-Hamdulillah is Umm Al-Qur'an and Umm Al-Kitab and the seven oft-repeated"""
"3124","Narrated Ubayy bin Ka'b:that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \Allah has not revealed the likes of Umm Al-Kitab in the Tawrah"""
"3125","Narrated Anas bin Malik:that regarding Allah's saying: We shall certainly call all of them to account. For all that they used to do (15:92 & 93). The Prophet (ﷺ) said: \About saying La Ilaha Illallah"""
"3126","Narrated Abu Sa'eed Al-Khudri:that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \Beware of the believer's intuition"""
"3127","Narrated 'Abdullah bin 'Umar:\I heard 'Umar bin Al-Khattab saying: 'The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \""Four before Zuhr"""
"3128","Abd ibn Humaid narrated to us, that Yazid ibn Harun informed us, that Hammad ibn Salamah informed us from Ammar ibn Abi Ammar, who said: Ibn Abbas recited: *\Today I have perfected for you your religion"
"3129","Narrated Abu Hurairah:that the Prophet (ﷺ) said: \When I was taken on the Night of Isra I met Musa.\"" He described him saying: \""He was a man who was\"" and I think he said: \""A thin man"""
"3130","Narrated Abu Hurairah:that the Prophet (ﷺ) said: ""When I was taken on the Night of Isra I met Musa."" He described him saying: ""He was a man who was"" and I think he said: ""A thin man, whose hair was as if he was a man from Shanu'ah."" He said: ""I met 'Eisa"" he described him saying: ""Of average build, with a red face, as if he had just come out of the Dimas"" meaning the bath-house. ""And I saw Ibrahim"" he said: ""I am the one among his offspring that most resembles him"" and he said: ""I was brought two vessels, one of them containing milk and the other containing wine. I was told: 'Take whichever one of them you wish.' So I took the milk to drink from it. It was said to me: 'You were guided to the Fitrah' or: 'You chose the Fitrah, if you had take the wine your Ummah would have strayed"
"3131","Narrated Ibn Buraidah:from his father that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \When we reached Bait Al-Maqdis"""
"3132","Narrated Jabir bin 'Abdullah:that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \When the Quraish belied me"""
"3133","Narrated by Abdullah ibn Abd al-Rahman, who reported from Muhammad ibn Yusuf, who reported from Isra'il, who narrated from Abu Ishaq, from 'Umar ibn Sharahil Abu Mayssarah, from 'Umar ibn al-Khattab (may Allah be pleased with him), that he said:\n\n\O Allah"
"3134","Narrated by al-Bara' (may Allah be pleased with he and his father): \Some men among the Companions of the Prophet (peace be upon him) died before the prohibition of wine was revealed. When wine was prohibited"
"3135","It has also been narrated by Shuʿbah, from Abū Isḥāq, from al-Barāʾ. Muḥammad ibn Bashshār Bundār informed us of that; he said: Muḥammad ibn Jaʿfar narrated to us, he said: Shuʿbah narrated to us, from Abū Isḥāq, with this chain. He said: al-Barāʾ ibn ʿāzib (may Allāh be pleased with him) said:\n\n\A number of the Companions of the Prophet (ṣallallāhu ʿalayhi wa-sallam) died while they were drinking khamr (intoxicating wine). When the prohibition of it was revealed"
"3136","Narrated Abu Hurairah:regarding Allah's saying: \It may be that your Lord will raise you to a praised station (17:79)\"" that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) was asked about it and he said: \""It is the intercession"""
"3137","Narrated Ibn Mas'ud:\The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) entered Makkah during the year of the Conquest"""
"3138","**Narrated by ʿAmr ibn ʿAlī Abū Ḥafṣ al-Fallās, who narrated from Abū ʿĀṣim, who narrated from ʿUthmān ibn Saʿd, who narrated from ʿIkrimah, from Ibn ʿAbbās (may Allah be pleased with him):**\n\nA man came to the Prophet ﷺ and said, \O Messenger of Allah"
"3139","Narrated Ibn 'Abbas:\The Quraish said to the Jews: 'Give us something that we can ask this man about.' So he said: 'Ask him about the Ruh.' So they asked him about the Ruh. So Allah Most High"""
"3140","Narrated 'Abdullah:\I took a walk with the Prophet (ﷺ) on a farm in Al-Madinah"""
"3141","Narrated Abu Hurairah:that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \People will be gathered in three classes on the Day of Resurrection: A class walking"""
"3142","Narrated Sa'eed ibn Ya'qoob al-Talaqani, who narrated from 'Abdullah ibn al-Mubarak, who reported from 'Utbah ibn Abi Hakim, who narrated from 'Amr ibn Jariyah al-Lakhmi, from Abu Umayyah al-Sha'bani, who said:\n\n\I came to Abu Tha'labah al-Khushani and said to him"
"3143","Narrated Safwan bin 'Assal Al-Muradi:\A Jew said to his companion: 'Accompany us to this Prophet.' So his companion said: 'Do not say: \""Prophet"""
"3144","**Sufyān ibn Wakīʿ** narrated to us: **Yaḥyā ibn Ādam** narrated to us, from **Ibn Abī Zāʾidah**, from **Muḥammad ibn Abī al-Qāsim**, from **ʿAbd al-Malik ibn Saʿīd**, from his father, from **Ibn ʿAbbāys** رضي الله عنهما, who said:\n\nA man from Banū Sahm went out with Tamīm al-Dārī and ʿAdī ibn Badāʾ. The Sahmī man died in a land where there was no Muslim present. When the two companions returned with his estate, they (the heirs) found that a silver bowl inlaid with gold was missing. So the Messenger of Allah ﷺ administered an oath to the two of them. Subsequently, the bowl was found in Makkah, and it was said: \We purchased it from ʿAdī and Tamīm.\"" Then two men from among the heirs of the Sahmī stood and swore by Allah: \""Our testimony is more deserving than their testimony"
"3145","Narrated Sa'eed bin Jubair:from Ibn 'Abbas regarding Allah's saying: \And offer your Salat neither aloud nor in a low voice but follow a way between.\"" He said: \""It was revealed when the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) was hiding himself in Makkah"""
"3146","Narrated Zirr bin Hubaish:\I said to Hudhaifah bin Al-Yaman: 'Did the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) perform Salat in Bait Al-Maqdis?' He said: 'No.' I said: 'But he did.' He said: 'You say that"""
"3147","Narrated Abu Sa'eed Al-Khudri:that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \I am the chief of the children of Adam on the Day of Judgement and I am not boasting"""
"3148","Narrated Sa'eed bin Jubair:\I said to Ibn 'Abbas: 'Nawf Al-Bikali claims that Musa"""
"3149","Narrated Ibn 'Abbas:that Ubayy bin Ka'b narrated that the Prophet (ﷺ) said: \The boy that Al-Khidr killed was destined to be a disbeliever the day he was created"""
"3150","Narrated Abu Hurairah:that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \He was called Al-Khadir because he sat on a barren Farwah and it turned green beneath him"""
"3151","Narrated Abu Ad-Darda:that regarding Allah's saying: And there was under it a treasure belonging to them (18:82) - the Prophet (ﷺ) said: \Gold and silver"""
"3152","**Narrated by Ahmad ibn Mani' (may Allah have mercy on him):**\n\nIsḥāq ibn Yūsuf al-Azraq narrated to us, Dāwūd ibn Abī Hind narrated to us, from al-Shaʿbī, from Masrūq, who said:\n\n\I was reclining in the company of ʿĀ'ishah (may Allah be pleased with her)"
"3153","Muḥammad ibn Mūsā al-Baṣrī al-Ḥarashī narrated to us, Ziyād ibn ʿAbdullāh al-Bakkāʾī narrated to us, ʿAṭāʾ ibn al-Sāʾib narrated from Saʿīd ibn Jubayr, from ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿAbbās (may Allah be pleased with them both), who said:\n\n\Some people came to the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) and said"
"3154","Narrated Al-Mughirah bin Shu'bah:\The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) sent me to Najran. They said to me: 'Do you people not recite: O sister of Harun (19:28) - while between Musa and 'Eisa there is such (gap) as there is?' I did not know how to respond to them. So when I returned to the Prophet (ﷺ)"""
"3155","Narrated Abu Sa'eed Al-Khudri:\The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) recited: And warn them of a Day of griefs and regrets (19:39) and he said: 'Death will be brought as if it is a mixed black and white ram"""
"3156","**Abd ibn Humaid narrated to us:** Ya'la ibn Ubayd narrated to us, from Fudayl ibn Ghazwan, from Abu Hazim, from Abu Hurayrah (may Allah be pleased with him), from the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him), who said:\n\n**\Three things"
"3157","Narrated Sa'eed bin Jubair:from Ibn 'Abbas who said: \The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said to Jibra'il: 'What prevents you from visiting us more than you visit us?'\"" He said: \""So this Ayah was revealed: And we descend not except by the command of your Lord. To Him belongs what is before us and what is behind us.\"" Up to the end of the Ayah (19:)"""
"3158","Narrated Sa'eed bin Jubair:from Ibn 'Abbas who said: ""The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said to Jibra'il: 'What prevents you from visiting us more than you visit us?'"" He said: ""So this Ayah was revealed: And we descend not except by the command of your Lord. To Him belongs what is before us and what is behind us."" Up to the end of the Ayah (19:)"
"3159","Narrated Shu'bah:from As-Suffi from Murrah: \'Abdullah said: 'There is not one of you but will pass over it (19:71) - They pass over it"""
"3160","Narrated Abu Hurairah:that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \When Allah loves a slave He calls Jibra'il"""
"3161","Narrated Masruq:\I heard Khabbab bin Al-Aratt saying: 'I came to Al-'As bin Wa'il As-Sahmi to collect a debt he owed me. He said: 'You shall not be given anything until you deny Muhammad.' So I said: 'No"""
"3162","Narrated Abu Hurairah:\While the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) was returning from Khaibar he traveled during the night until he became sleepy and he sat down to rest. Then he said: 'O Bilal! Stand guard for us for the night.'\"" He said: 'So Bilal performed Salat"""
"3163","Narrated Abu Sa'eed:that the Prophet (ﷺ) said: \Woe is the valley of Jahannam"""
"3164","Narrated 'Aishah:that a man came and sat in front of the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) and said: \O Messenger of Allah! I have two slaves who lie to me"""
"3165","Muḥammad ibn Bashshār narrated to us; ʿUmar ibn Yūnus al-Yamāmī narrated to us; ʿIkrimah ibn ʿAmmār narrated to us; Abū Zumayl narrated to us; ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿAbbās narrated to us; ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb narrated: The Prophet of Allah ﷺ looked at the polytheists, who were one thousand, and his Companions were three hundred and thirteen men. The Prophet of Allah ﷺ faced the Qiblah, stretched forth his hands, and began to cry out to his Lord: ""O Allah, fulfill for me what You promised me. O Allah, give me what You promised me. O Allah, if You destroy this band of the people of Islam, You will not be worshipped on the earth."" He continued crying out to his Lord, stretching his hands, facing the Qiblah, until his cloak fell from his shoulders. Abū Bakr came, took his cloak, threw it over his shoulders, then embraced him from behind and said: ""O Prophet of Allah, your supplication to your Lord is sufficient for you; He will fulfill for you what He promised you."" Then Allah revealed: (When you asked help of your Lord, and He answered you: Indeed, I will reinforce you with a thousand angels, following one another.) So Allah reinforced them with the angels. Abū ʿĪsā said: This is a ḥasan ṣaḥīḥ gharīb ḥadīth; we do not know it from the ḥadīth of ʿUmar except from the ḥadīth of ʿIkrimah ibn ʿAmmār from Abū Zumayl. Abū Zumayl's name is Simāk al-Ḥanafī. And this was on the day of Badr."
"3166","Narrated Ibn 'Abbas:\The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) stood to deliver a Khutbah"""
"3167","Narrated 'Imran bin Husain:when (the following) was revealed: \O mankind! Have Taqwa of your Lord! Verily the earthquake of the hour is a terrible thing...\"" up to His saying: \""But Allah's torment is severe...(22:1 & 2)\"" - he said: \""These Ayat were revealed while he (ﷺ) was on a journey and he said: 'Do you know what Day this is?' So they said: 'Allah and His Messenger know better.' He said: 'That is the day when Allah says to Adam: Send forth those who are to be sent to the Fire. So he says: O Lord! How many are to be sent? He says: Nine-hundred and ninety-nine in the Fire"""
"3168","Narrated 'Imran bin Husain:\We were with the Prophet (ﷺ) on a journey when some of his Companions fell behind. So the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) raised his voice reciting these two Ayat: \""O mankind! Have Taqwa of your Lord! Verily the earthquake of the hour is a terrible thing...\"" up to His saying: but Allah's torment is severe (21:1 & 2).\"" When his Companions heard that"""
"3169","Narrated 'Abdullah bin Az-Zubair:that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \It is only called Al-Bait Al-'Atiq because it has not been conquered by a tyrant"""
"3170","Muḥammad ibn Bashshār narrated to us; Yaḥyā ibn Saʿīd, Muḥammad ibn Jaʿfar, Ibn Abī ʿAdī, and Suhayl ibn Yūsuf narrated to us; they said: ʿAwf ibn Abī Jamīlah narrated to us; Yazīd al-Fārisī narrated to us; Ibn ʿAbbās narrated to us: I said to ʿUthmān ibn ʿAffān: ""What made you put together al-Anfāl, which is among the Mathānī, and Barā'ah, which is among the Mi'īn, and you did not write the line 'Bismillāh al-Raḥmān al-Raḥīm' between them, and you placed them among the Seven Long Surahs? What compelled you to do that?"" ʿUthmān said: ""The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to have periods when revelation would descend upon him with surahs of specific numbers. When something was revealed to him, he would call some of those who wrote and say: 'Place these verses in the surah where such-and-such is mentioned.' When a verse was revealed, he would say: 'Place this verse in the surah where such-and-such is mentioned.' Al-Anfāl was among the first revealed in Medina, and Barā'ah was among the last of the Qur'an. Its story was similar to its story, so I thought it was part of it. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ died without clarifying to us that it was part of it. Therefore, I joined them and did not write the line 'Bismillāh al-Raḥmān al-Raḥīm' between them, and I placed them among the Seven Long Surahs."" Abū ʿĪsā said: This is a ḥasan ḥadīth; we do not know it except from the ḥadīth of ʿAwf from Yazīd al-Fārisī from Ibn ʿAbbās. Yazīd al-Fārisī narrated other ḥadīths from Ibn ʿAbbās. He is said to be Yazīd ibn Hurmuz. Yazīd al-Raqāshī is Yazīd ibn Abān al-Raqāshī, and he did not meet Ibn ʿAbbās; he only narrated from Anas ibn Mālik. Both are Tābiʿīn from the people of Baṣrah. Yazīd al-Fārisī is older than Yazīd al-Raqāshī."
"3171","Narrated Sa'eed bin Jubair:\When the Prophet (ﷺ) was expelled from Makkah a man said: 'They have driven out their Prophet' so (the following) was revealed: \""Permission (to fight) is given to those who are fought against"""
"3172","Narrated 'Umar bin Al-Khattab [may Allah be pleased with him]:\When revelation came to the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ)"""
"3173","Narrated Anas bin Malik:that Ar-Rubai' bint An-Nadr came to the Prophet (ﷺ) - and her son Harithah bin Suraqah had been killed on the Day of Badr"
"3174","Narrated 'Abdur-Rahman bin [Sa'eed bin] Wahb - that is Al-Hamdani:that 'Aishah the wife of the Prophet (ﷺ) said: \I asked about the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) about this Ayah: And those who give that which they give with their hearts full of fear... (23:60)\"" 'Aishah said: \""Are they those who drink Khamr and steal?\"" He said: \""No"""
"3175","Narrated Abu Sa'eed Al-Khudri:that the Prophet (ﷺ) said: \Therein they will grin"""
"3176","**Narrated by Ibn Abi 'Umar, who narrated from Sufyan, from Abu Ishaq, from Zaid bin Yuthay', who said:**\n\n\We asked 'Alī (may Allāh be pleased with him): 'With what were you sent during the [Farewell] Hajj?' He replied: 'I was sent with four [commands]: That no one should circumambulate the House [i.e."
"3177","Narrated Sa'eed bin Jubair:\I was asked about those who were involved in the case of Li'an and if they are to be separated"""
"3178","Narrated Ibn 'Abbas:\Hilal bin Umayyah went to the Prophet (ﷺ) and accused his wife of committing illegal sexual intercourse with Sharik bin Sahma. The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: 'Either you produce proof"""
"3179","Al-Ḥusayn ibn Yazīd al-Kūfī narrated to us, ʿAbd al-Salām ibn Ḥarb narrated to us, from Ghutayf ibn Aʿyan, from Muṣʿab ibn Saʿd, from ʿAdī ibn Ḥātim, who said:\n\n\I came to the Prophet ﷺ while I was wearing a gold cross around my neck. He ﷺ said: **'O ʿAdī"
"3180","**Narrated by Ziyād ibn Ayyūb al-Baghdādī, who narrated from ʿAffān ibn Muslim, who narrated from Hammām, who narrated from Thābit, from Anas رضي الله عنه, that Abū Bakr رضي الله عنه related to him, saying:**\n\n\I said to the Prophet ﷺ while we were in the cave: 'If any one of them were to look at his feet"
"3181","Narrated 'Abdullah:\I said: 'O Messenger of Allah (ﷺ)! What is the worst sin?' He said: 'That you make and equal to Allah"""
"3182","Narrated 'Abdullah:\I asked the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) which sin is the worst.' He said: 'That you make an equal to Allah while it is He who created you"""
"3183","Narrated 'Aishah:\When this Ayah was revealed: 'And warn your tribe of near kindred (26:214).' The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: 'O Safiyyah bint 'Abdul-Muttalib! O Fatimah bint Muhammad! O Banu 'Abdul-Muttalib! I have no power to help you at all before Allah! Ask of me whatever you want from my wealth"""
"3184","Narrated Abu Hurairah:\When (the following) was revealed: 'And warn your tribe of near kindred (26:214)' the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) gathered the (families) of the Quraish (calling them) one and all"""
"3185","Narrated Qasamah bin Zuhair:\Al-Ash'ari said: 'When (the following) was revealed: 'And warn your tribe of near kindred (26:214)' the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) placed his fingers in his ears"""
"3186","Narrated Abu Hurairah:that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \A beast will emerge from the earth. With it shall be the ring of Sulaiman and the staff of Musa. It will brighten the face of the believer"""
"3187","**Muhammad ibn Bashshar narrated to us** — **Abd ar-Rahman ibn Mahdi narrated to us** — **Ibrahim ibn Sa'd narrated to us**, from **az-Zuhri**, from **Ubayd ibn as-Sabbak**, that **Zayd ibn Thabit** — رضي الله عنه — narrated to him, saying:\n\nAbu Bakr as-Siddiq — رضي الله عنه — sent for me at the time of the massacre of the people of Yamamah, and behold, Umar ibn al-Khattab — رضي الله عنه — was with him. Abu Bakr said: \Indeed"
"3188","**Muḥammad ibn Bashshār narrated to us, ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Mahdī narrated to us, Ibrāhīm ibn Saʿd narrated from al-Zuhrī, from Anas, that Ḥudhayfah came to ʿUthmān ibn ʿAffān — may Allah be pleased with them both — while he was engaged in military campaigns alongside the people of Shām in the conquest of Armenia and Adharbījān together with the people of ʿIrāq. Ḥudhayfah observed their differences regarding the Qurʾān, so he said to ʿUthmān ibn ʿAffān, \O Commander of the Faithful"
"3189","Narrated Umm Hani:that regarding Allah's saying: '...And you practice evil in your meetings... (29:29) that the Prophet (ﷺ) said: \They would throw pebbles at people of the land and make a mockery of them"""
"3190","Narrated Ibn 'Abbas:that regarding \Alif Lam Mim. The Romans have been defeated\"" (In the nearest land"""
"3191","Abd ibn Humayd narrated to us, al-Hajjaj ibn Minhal narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Ali ibn Zayd, from Yusuf ibn Mihran, from Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him), that the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) said:\n\n\When Allah drowned Pharaoh"
"3192","Narrated by Muhammad ibn ʿAbd al-Aʿlā al-Ṣanʿānī, who narrated from Khālid ibn al-Ḥārith, who reported from Shuʿbah, who informed me from ʿAdīy ibn Thābit and ʿAṭāʾ ibn al-Sāʾib, from Saʿīd ibn Jubayr, from Ibn ʿAbbās — one of them mentioned that the Prophet ﷺ said:\n\n\Indeed"
"3193","Narrated Niyar bin Mukram Al-Aslami:\When (the following) was revealed: 'Alif Lam Mim. The Romans have been defeated. In the nearest land"""
"3194","Narrated Abu Umamah:that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \Do not sell the female singers"""
"3195","Anas bin Malik said about this Ayah:Their sides forsake their beds (32:16) - \It was revealed about waiting for [this] Salat which you call Al-'Atamah"""
"3196","Narrated Abu Hurairah:that the Prophet (ﷺ) said: \Allah Most High said: 'I have prepared for My righteous worshipers what no eye has seen"""
"3197","Abd ibn Humaid narrated to us, from Husayn al-Ju'fi, from Zāʾidah, from ʿAbd al-Malik ibn ʿUmayr, from ʿAbd ar-Raḥmān ibn Abī Laylā, from Muʿādh ibn Jabal, who said:\n\nA man came to the Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him, and said: \O Messenger of Allah"
"3198","**Narration Chain:**\nMuhammad ibn Bashshār narrated to us — Yaḥyā ibn Sa'īd narrated to us — from Sulaymān al-Taymī — from Abū 'Uthmān — from Ibn Mas'ūd (may Allāh be pleased with him):\n\nThat a man committed an unlawful kiss with a woman, and so he came to the Prophet ﷺ and asked him regarding its expiation. Thereupon the following verse was revealed:\n\n> *\Establish prayer at the two ends of the day and in the approaching hours of the night. Indeed"
"3199","Narrated Anas:\My paternal uncle Anas bin An-Nadr - after whom I was named - did not participate in the battle of Badr with the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ). This distressed him and he said: 'I was absent from the first battle which the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) attended. By Allah! If Allah gives me the opportunity to participate in another battle along with the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ)"""
"3200","Narrated Anas bin Malik:\My paternal uncle was absent from the fighting of Badr"""
"3201","Narrated Musa bin Talhah:\I entered upon Mu'awiyah and he said:' Shall I not give you some good news?' I said: 'Of course!' He said: 'I heard the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) saying: 'Talhah is among those who fulfilled their vow"""
"3202","**Narrated by Abū Hurayrah (may Allāh be pleased with him):**\n\nMaḥmūd ibn Khidāsh al-Baghdādī narrated to us, saying: Saif ibn Muḥammad al-Thawrī narrated to us, from al-Aʿmash, from Abū Ṣāliḥ, from Abū Hurayrah, from the Prophet ﷺ regarding Allāh's statement:\n\n> **\And We have made some of these [fruits] superior to others in taste\""** (Sūrat al-Raʿd"
"3203","Narrated 'Aishah [may Allah be pleased with her]:\When the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) was ordered to tell his wives to make a choice"""
"3204","Narrated 'Umar bin Abi Salamah - the step-son of the Prophet (ﷺ):\When these Ayat were revealed to the Prophet (ﷺ): 'Allah only wishes to remove the Rijs from you"""
"3205","Narrated to us Ibn Abi 'Umar, narrated to us Sufyan, from Dawud ibn Abi Hind, from al-Sha'bi, from Masruq, who said:\n\n'Ā'ishah, may Allah be pleased with her, recited this verse: *\On the Day when the earth will be changed to another earth\""* (Sūrah Ibrāhīm"
"3206","Narrated 'Aishah [may Allah be pleased with her]:\If the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) was to have concealed anything that was revealed to him"""
"3207","Narrated 'Aishah [may Allah be pleased with her]:\If the Prophet (ﷺ) was to have hidden anything from the Revelation"""
"3208","Narrated Ibn 'Umar:\We called Zaid bin Harithah nothing but 'Zaid bin Muhammad' until the Qur'an was revealed (saying): 'Call them by their fathers"""
"3209","Narrated Dawud bin Abi Hind:from Ash-Sha'bi regarding the saying of Allah [the Mighty and Sublime]: 'Muhammad is not the father of any one of your men (33:40)' he said: \No male children of his would live among them"""
"3210","Narrated Umm 'Umarah Al-Ansariyyah:that she came to the Prophet (ﷺ) and said: \I do not see but that everything is for the men"""
"3211","Narrated Anas:\When this Ayah was revealed: 'But you did hide in yourself that which Allah will make manifest... (33:37)' about Zainab bint Jahsh"""
"3212","Narrated Anas:\When this Ayah was revealed about Zainab bint Jahsh: 'So when Zaid had completed his aim with her"""
"3213","Narrated Anas:""When this Ayah was revealed about Zainab bint Jahsh: 'So when Zaid had completed his aim with her, We gave her to you in marriage (33:37)' - he said: ""She used to boast to the wives of the Prophet (ﷺ): 'Your families married you (to him) while Allah married me (to him) from above the Seven Heavens"
"3214","Narrated Ibn 'Abbas:\All types of women were prohibited for the Messenger of ALlah (ﷺ) except for the believing women among those who emigrated. (Allah) said: 'It is not lawful for you (to marry other) women after this"""
"3215","Narrated 'Aishah:\The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) did not die until the women had been made lawful for him"""
"3216","Narrated by Ya'qub ibn Ibrahim al-Dawraqi, narrated by Abu Tumaylah, from al-Zubayr ibn Junadah, from Ibn Buraydah, from his father, who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, said: \When we arrived at Bayt al-Maqdis"
"3217","Narrated Al-Ja'd bin Abi 'Uthman:from Anas bin Malik: \The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) got married"""
"3218","Narrated Anas bin Malik:\The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) was staying with one of his wives"""
"3219","Narrated Abu Mas'ud Al-Ansari:\The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) came to us while we were sitting in a gathering of Sa'd bin 'Ubadah. Bashir bin Sa'd said: 'Allah ordered us to say Salat upon you"""
"3220","Narrated Abu Mas'ud Al-Ansari:""The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) came to us while we were sitting in a gathering of Sa'd bin 'Ubadah. Bashir bin Sa'd said: 'Allah ordered us to say Salat upon you, so how do we say Salat upon you?'"" The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) was silent, until we thought that we had not even asked him. Then the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: 'Say: O Allah! Send Salat upon Muhammad and upon Muhammad's family just as you have sent [upon Ibrahim and] upon Ibrahim's family. And bless Muhammad and Muhammad's family just as you have blessed [Ibrahim and] Ibrahim's family among the nations. Indeed you are praised, the glorious.' And the Salam is as you have learned"
"3221","Narrated Farwah bin Musaik Al-Muradi:\I went to the Prophet (ﷺ) and said: 'O Messenger of Allah! Shall I not fight those who turn away among my people"""
"3222","Narrated Abu Hurairah:that the Prophet (ﷺ) said: \When Allah decrees a matter in the Heavens"""
"3223","Narrated Abu Hurairah:that the Prophet (ﷺ) said: \When Allah decrees a matter in the Heavens"
"3224","Qutaybah narrated to us, that Yaḥyā ibn Zakariyyā ibn Abī Zāʾidah narrated to us, from Dāwūd ibn Abī Hind, from ʿIkrimah, from Ibn ʿAbbās, who said: The Quraysh said to the Jews, \Give us something with which we may question this man.\"" They said"
"3225","Narrated Abu Sa'eed Al-Khudri:\Banu Salamah's dwellings were on the outskirts of Al-Madinah"""
"3226","Narrated Abu Sa'eed Al-Khudri:""Banu Salamah's dwellings were on the outskirts of Al-Madinah, so they wanted to relocate closer to the Masjid. Then this Ayah was revealed: 'Verily, We give life to the dead, and We record that which they send before (them), and their traces... (36:12)' So the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: 'Your steps are recorded, so do not relocate"
"3227","Narrated Anas bin Malik:that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \No caller invites to anything except that he is detained along with"""
"3228","Narrated Ubayy bin Ka'b:\I asked the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) about the saying of Allah"""
"3229","**Abd ibn Humayd narrated to us:** Sulayman ibn Dawud narrated to us, from Shu'bah, from Abu Bishr, from Sa'eed ibn Jubayr — and he did not mention Ibn 'Abbas — and from Hushaym, from Abu Bishr, from Sa'eed ibn Jubayr, from Ibn 'Abbas, regarding the Words of Allah, the Most High:\n\n> **\And do not recite your prayer aloud\""** (Surah Al-Isra"
"3230","Narrated Samurah:that the Prophet (ﷺ) said: \Sam was the father of Arabs"""
"3231","**Narrated by Ibn Abi 'Umar, who narrated from Sufyan, from Mis'ar, from 'Asim ibn Abi an-Najud, from Zirr ibn Hubaysh, who said:**\n\nI said to **Hudhayfah ibn al-Yamān** (may Allah be pleased with him): \Did the Messenger of Allah ﷺ pray in **Bayt al-Maqdis** (Jerusalem)?\""\n\nHe said: **\""No.\""**\n\nI said: **\""Indeed"
"3232","Ibn Abī ʿUmar narrated to us; Sufyān narrated to us, from ʿAlī ibn Zayd ibn Judʿān, from Abū Naḍrah, from Abū Saʿīd, who said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: ""I am the master of the children of Adam on the Day of Resurrection, and no boast. In my hand is the Banner of Praise, and no boast. There is no prophet on that day—Adam and whoever came after him—except he will be under my banner. I am the first for whom the earth will split open, and no boast."" He said: ""The people will be terrified three times. They will come to Adam and say: 'You are our father, Adam. Intercede for us with your Lord.' He will say: 'I committed a sin for which I was sent down to the earth. But go to Nūḥ.' They will come to Nūḥ, and he will say: 'I supplicated against the people of the earth, and they were destroyed. But go to Ibrāhīm.' They will come to Ibrāhīm, and he will say: 'I told three lies.' Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'None of them was a lie except that he thereby avoided something for the sake of Allah's religion. But go to Mūsā.' They will come to Mūsā, and he will say: 'I killed a soul I was not commanded to kill. But go to ʿĪsā.' They will come to ʿĪsā, and he will say: 'I was worshipped besides Allah. But go to Muḥammad.' They will come to me, and I will set out with them."" Ibn Judʿān said: Anas said: ""It is as if I see the Messenger of Allah ﷺ saying: 'I will take hold of the ring of the gate of Paradise and shake it. It will be said: ""Who is this?"" It will be said: ""Muḥammad."" They will open for me and welcome me, saying: ""Welcome."" I will fall prostrate, and Allah will inspire me with praise and glorification. It will be said to me: ""Raise your head. Ask, and you shall be given. Intercede, and your intercession shall be accepted. Speak, and your speech shall be heard."" That is the Station of Praise (al-Maqām al-Maḥmūd) which Allah mentioned: (It may be that your Lord will raise you to a praised station.)'"" Sufyān said: ""Nothing is from Anas except this statement: 'I will take hold of the ring of the gate of Paradise and shake it.'"" Abū ʿĪsā said: This is a ḥasan ḥadīth. Some narrated this ḥadīth from Abū Naḍrah from Ibn ʿAbbās with its full length."
"3233","**Narrated by Ibn Abi 'Umar, who narrated from Sufyan, from 'Amr ibn Dinar, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, who said:**\n\nI said to Ibn 'Abbas, \Indeed"
"3234","Narrated Mu'adh bin Jabal [may Allah be pleased with him]:\One morning"""
"3235","Narrated 'Abdullah bin Az-Zubair:from his father who said: \When (the following) was revealed: 'Then"""
"3236","Narrated Asma bint Yazid:\I heard the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) reciting: 'Say: \""O My slaves who have transgressed against themselves! Despair not of the mercy of Allah"""
"3237","Narrated 'Abdullah:\A Jew came to the Prophet (ﷺ) and said: 'O Muhammad! Allah will seize the heavens upon a finger"""
"3238","Narrated 'Abdullah:\So the Prophet (ﷺ) laughed in amazement and approval"""
"3239","Abū Sa‘īd al-Ashajj and Abū Mūsā Muḥammad ibn al-Muthannā narrated to us, both saying: Ibn Idrīs narrated to us, from his father, from Simāk ibn Ḥarb, from ‘Alqamah ibn Wā’il, from al-Mughīrah ibn Shu‘bah (may Allāh be pleased with him), who said:\n\nThe Messenger of Allāh (peace and blessings be upon him) sent me to Najrān. They said to me: “Do you not recite [in your Book]: ‘O sister of Hārūn’ (Maryam 19:28), yet there was [a great span of time] between ‘Īsā (Jesus, peace be upon him) and Mūsā (Moses, peace be upon him)?” I did not know how to answer them. So I returned to the Messenger of Allāh (peace and blessings be upon him) and informed him. He said: “Why did you not inform them that they used to name their children after their prophets and the righteous who came before them?”\n\nAbū ‘Īsā [al-Tirmidhī] said: This is a ḥasan ṣaḥīḥ gharīb hadith; we do not know it except through the narration of Ibn Idrīs."
"3240","Narrated Mujahid:that Ibn 'Abbas said: \Do you know what is the width of Jahannam?\"" I said: \""No.\"" He said: \""Yes"""
"3241","Narrated Masruq:that 'Aishah said: \O Messenger of Allah! - On the Day of Resurrection the whole earth will be grasped by His Hand and the heavens will be rolled up in His Right Hand (39:67). Where will the believers be?\"" He said: \""Upon the Sirat O 'Aishah"""
"3242","Narrated Abu Sa'eed Al-Khudri:that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \How can I be comfortable when the one with the horn is holding it in his lips and his forehead is leaning forward"""
"3243","Narrated 'Abdullah bin 'Amr [may Allah be pleased with him]:\A Bedouin said: 'O Messenger of Allah! What is As-Sur?' He said: 'A horn which is blown into"""
"3244","Muḥammad ibn Bashshār narrated to us: Yaḥyā ibn Saʿīd narrated to us: Shuʿbah narrated to us, from al-Suddī, from Murrah, from ʿAbdullāh ibn Masʿūd, regarding the verse: *\And there is none among you but will pass over it [Hell]\""* (Qurʾān 19:71). He said: \""They will pass over it"
"3245","Narrated Abu Hurairah:that the Prophet (ﷺ) said: \A caller will call out: 'You shall have life and never die; you shall be healthy and never be ill; you shall be young and never grow old; you shall live in favor and never suffer difficult circumstances.' That is the saying of Allah Most High: This is Paradise"""
"3246","Narrated An-Nu'man bin Bashir:that the Prophet (ﷺ) said: \Supplication is the worship.\"" Then he recited: 'And your Lord said: 'Call upon Me"""
"3247","**Narrated by Abu Hurayrah (may Allah be pleased with him):**\n\nWhen the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) returned from Khaybar, he traveled through the night until drowsiness overcame him. He then dismounted and rested for the night. He (ﷺ) said, \O Bilal"
"3248","Narrated 'Abdullah:\I was hiding beneath the covering of the Ka'bah"""
"3249","Narrated Anas bin Malik:that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) recited: Verily those who say: \Our Lord is Allah"""
"3250","Narrated Tawus:Ibn 'Abbas was asked about this Ayah: Say: \No reward do I ask of you for this except to be kind for my kinship with you (42:23).\"" So Sa'eed bin Jubair said: 'To be kind to the family of Muhammad.' Ibn 'Abbas replied: 'You know that there was no family of the Quraish except that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) had some relatives among them.' He said: 'Except that you should uphold ties of kinship that exist between me and you"""
"3251","Narrated Tawus:Ibn 'Abbas was asked about this Ayah: Say: ""No reward do I ask of you for this except to be kind for my kinship with you (42:23)."" So Sa'eed bin Jubair said: 'To be kind to the family of Muhammad.' Ibn 'Abbas replied: 'You know that there was no family of the Quraish except that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) had some relatives among them.' He said: 'Except that you should uphold ties of kinship that exist between me and you"
"3252","Narrated Abu Umamah:that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \No people go astray after having been guided"""
"3253","Narrated Masruq:\A man came to 'Abdullah and said: 'A story teller has said that a smoke will appear from the earth"""
"3254","Narrated Anas bin Malik:that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \There is no believer except that he has two doors: A door through which his deeds ascend"""
"3255","Narrated 'Abdul-Malik bin 'Umair:from the nephew of 'Abdullah bin Salam who said: \When they were after 'Uthman"""
"3256","Narrated 'Aishah [may Allah be pleased with her]:\When the Prophet (ﷺ) saw storm clouds he would pace back and forth. And when it rained"""
"3257","Yaḥyā ibn Mūsā, ʿAbd ibn Ḥumayd, and others narrated to us; the meaning is one. They said: ʿAbd al-Razzāq narrated to us, from Yūnus ibn Sulaym, from al-Zuhrī, from ʿUrwah ibn al-Zubayr, from ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn ʿAbd al-Qārī, who said: I heard ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb, may Allah be pleased with him, say: The Prophet ﷺ, when revelation descended upon him, a sound like the buzzing of bees would be heard near his face. One day it descended upon him, and we waited a while. Then he was relieved. He faced the Qiblah, raised his hands, and said: ""O Allah, increase us and do not decrease us. Honor us and do not humiliate us. Give us and do not deprive us. Prefer us and do not prefer others over us. Make us pleased and be pleased with us."" Then the Prophet ﷺ said: ""Ten verses were revealed to me. Whoever establishes them will enter Paradise."" Then he recited: (Successful indeed are the believers) until he completed ten verses. Muḥammad ibn Abān narrated to us; ʿAbd al-Razzāq narrated to us, from Yūnus ibn Sulaym, from Yūnus ibn Yazīd, from al-Zuhrī, with this chain, similarly in meaning. Abū ʿĪsā said: This is more authentic than the first ḥadīth. I heard Isḥāq ibn Rāhwayh say..."
"3258","**Abd ibn Humayd narrated to us:** Rawh ibn 'Ubadah narrated to us, from Sa'id, from Qatadah, from Anas ibn Mālik (may Allāh be pleased with him), that **al-Rubayyi' bint al-Naḍr** came to the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him), whose son **Ḥārithah ibn Surāqah** had been struck on the Day of Badr by a stray arrow. She came to the Messenger of Allāh (peace and blessings be upon him) and said:\n\n*\Inform me about Ḥārithah. If he has attained good"
"3259","**Narrated by Ibn Abi 'Umar, who narrated from Sufyan, who narrated from Malik ibn Mihwal, from 'Abd ar-Rahman ibn Sa'id ibn Wahb al-Hamdani, that 'Ā'ishah (may Allāh be pleased with her), the wife of the Prophet ﷺ, said:**\n\n\I asked the Messenger of Allāh ﷺ about this verse: *'And those who give what they give while their hearts are fearful'* (Sūrah al-Mu'minūn"
"3260","Narrated Abu Hurairah:\Some people among the Companions of the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: 'O Messenger of Allah! Who are these people whom Allah mentioned"""
"3261","**Abd ibn Humayd narrated to us:** Rawh ibn 'Ubaydah narrated to us, from 'Ubaydullah ibn al-Akhnas, who informed me: 'Amr ibn Shu'ayb narrated to me, from his father, from his grandfather, who said:\n\nThere was a man called **Marthad ibn Abi Marthad**, who used to carry captives from Makkah to bring them to al-Madinah. He said: There was a prostitute in Makkah called **'Anaq**, who was a companion of his. He had promised one of the captives of Makkah that he would carry him (to safety).\n\nHe said: I came until I reached the shade of one of the walls of Makkah on a moonlit night. He said: Then 'Anaq came and saw the darkness of my shadow beside the wall. When she reached me, she recognized it and said, \Marthad?\"" I said"
"3262","Narrated Anas [May Allah be pleased with him]:\While the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) was returning from Al-Hudaibiyyah it was revealed to him"""
"3263","Narrated Anas:that eighty people swooped down from the mountain of At-Tan'im to kill the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) during Salat As-Subh"
"3264","**Narrated by ʿĀʾishah (may Allah be pleased with her):**\n\nShe said: \When that which was said about me was mentioned — and I was unaware of it — the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) stood up among the people to address them. He pronounced the *tashahhud* and praised Allah and extolled Him with that which He is worthy. Then he said: **'Now then: advise me regarding certain people who have slandered my household. By Allah"
"3265","Narrated 'Abdullah bin Az-Zubair:\Al-Aqra' bin Habis arrived to meet the Prophet (ﷺ)\"" - he said - \""so Abu Bakr said: 'O Messenger of Allah! Appoint him over his people.' 'Umar said: 'Do not appoint him O Messenger of Allah!' They continued talking before the Prophet (ﷺ) until they raised their voices. Abu Bakr said to 'Umar: 'You only wanted to contradict me.' So ['Umar] said: 'I did not want to contradict you.'\"" He said: \""So this Ayah was revealed: 'O you who believe! Do not raise your voices above the voice of the Prophet (49:2).'\"" He said: \""After that"""
"3266","Narrated 'Abdullah bin Az-Zubair:""Al-Aqra' bin Habis arrived to meet the Prophet (ﷺ)"" - he said - ""so Abu Bakr said: 'O Messenger of Allah! Appoint him over his people.' 'Umar said: 'Do not appoint him O Messenger of Allah!' They continued talking before the Prophet (ﷺ) until they raised their voices. Abu Bakr said to 'Umar: 'You only wanted to contradict me.' So ['Umar] said: 'I did not want to contradict you.'"" He said: ""So this Ayah was revealed: 'O you who believe! Do not raise your voices above the voice of the Prophet (49:2).'"" He said: ""After that, when 'Umar spoke before the Prophet (ﷺ), his speech could not be heard until he told him he could not understand him."" He (one of the narrators) said: ""And Ibn Az-Zubair did not mention his grandfather"" meaning Abu Bakr"
"3267","Narrated Abu Jubairah bin Ad-Dahhak:\A man among us would be known by two or three names. He would be called by one that perhaps he disliked"""
"3268","Narrated Abu Nadrah:\Abu Sa'eed Al-Khudri recited: And know that among you there is the Messenger of Allah. If he were to obey you in much of the matter"""
"3269","Narrated Ibn 'Umar:that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) gave a Khutbah to the people on the day of the conquest of Makkah"
"3270","Narrated Al-Hasan:from Samurah that the Prophet (ﷺ) said: \Al-Hasab is wealth and Al-Karam is Taqwa"""
"3271","Narrated Anas bin Malik:that Allah's Prophet (ﷺ) said: \Jahannam will continue saying: 'Are there any more' until the Might Lord puts His Foot over it. It will say: 'Enough! Enough! By Your Might.' And one side of it will close in on the other"""
"3272","Narrated Abu Wa'il:from a man of Rabi'ah who said: \I arrived in Al-Madinah"""
"3273","Narrated Abu Wa'il:that Al-Harith bin Yazid Al-Bakri said: \I arrived in Al-Madinah and entered the Masjid and found it full with the people and I also noticed a black banner raised high"""
"3274","Narrated Ibn 'Umar:that the Prophet (ﷺ) said: \And at the setting of the stars (52:49) (about) the two Rak'ah before Fajr. And after the prostrations (50:40) 'The two Rak'at after Al-Maghrib"""
"3275","Narrated ['Abdullah] bin Mas'ud:\When the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) reached Sidrat Al-Muntaha\"" He said: 'There terminates everything that ascends from the earth"""
"3276","Narrated Ash-Shaibani:\I asked Zirr bin Hubaish about the saying of Allah the Might and Sublime: And was a distance of two bow lengths or less (53:9). So he said: 'Ibn Mas'ud informed me that the Prophet (ﷺ) saw Jibra'il"""
"3277","Narrated by al-Husayn ibn Hurayth, who narrated from Mu'awiyah ibn 'Amr, from Abu Ishaq al-Fazari, from Sufyan al-Thawri, from Habib ibn Abi 'Amrah, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn 'Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both), regarding the Words of Allah, the Most High:\n\n**\Alif"
"3278","Narrated 'Ikrimah:that Ibn 'Abbas said: \Muhammad saw his Lord.\"" I said: \""Did Allah not say: No vision can grasp Him"""
"3279","Narrated Abu Salamah:from Ibn 'Abbas regarding Allah's saying: And indeed he saw him at a second descent. Near Sidrat Al-Muntaha (53:13 & 14). So He revealed to His worshiper whatever he revealed (53:10). And was a distance of two bow lengths or less (53:9). Ibn 'Abbas said: \The Prophet (ﷺ) saw Him"""
"3280","Narrated 'Ikrimah:that Ibn 'Abbas said (regarding the Ayah): The heart lied not in what he (ﷺ) saw (53:11). He said: \He saw Him with his heart"""
"3281","Narrated 'Abdullah bin Shaqiq:\I said to Abu Dharr: 'If I saw the Prophet (ﷺ) then I would asked him.\"" He said: 'What is it that you would have asked him about?' I said: 'I would have asked him if Muhammad saw his Lord?' He said: 'I did ask him that"""
"3282","Narrated 'Abdur-Rahman bin Zaid:from 'Abdullah (regarding the Ayah): The heart lied not in what he saw (53:11). He said: \The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) saw Jibra'il in a Hullah (dress normally made up of two pieces) of Rafraf filling what is between the heavens and the earth"""
"3283","Narrated 'Ata:from Ibn 'Abbas (regarding this Ayah): Those who avoid great sins and Al-Fawahish except Al-Lamam (minor sins) (53:32). He said: \The Prophet (ﷺ) said: 'Your forgiveness"""
"3284","**Narrated by Anas (may Allah be pleased with him):**\n\nMy uncle, Anas ibn An-Nadr — after whom I was named — had not been present at the Battle of Badr alongside the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), and this weighed heavily upon him. He said:\n\n*\The first battle in which the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) participated"
"3285","Narrated Ibn Mas'ud, may Allah be pleased with him:""We were with the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) in Mina, when the moon was cleft asunder into two parts. Part of it was behind the mountain, and part of it before it. The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said to us: 'Bear witness' meaning: The house has drawn near, and the moon has been cleft asunder (54:)"
"3286","Narrated Ibn Mas'ud:\The moon was cleft asunder during the time of the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ)"""
"3287","Narrated Ibn 'Umar:\The moon was split during the time of the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ). So the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: 'Bear witness"""
"3288","Narrated Muhammad bin Jubair bin Mut'im:from his father who said: \The moon was split during the time of the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) until it became as two sections"""
"3289","Narrated Abu Hurairah:\The idolaters of the Quraish came to the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) arguing about Qadar"""
"3290","Muhammad bin Al Munkadir narrated that:Jabir [may Allah be pleased with him] said: “The Messenger of Allah came out to his Companions"
"3291","Abu Hurairah narrated that the Messenger of Allah said:“Allah said: ‘I have prepared for My righteous worshippers"
"3292","Anas narrated that the Prophet said:“Indeed in Paradise there is a tree under whose shade a rider can travel for one hundred years without stopping. Recite if you wish: And in shave extended. And water flowing constantly.”"
"3293","**Qutaybah narrated to us, Ya'qūb ibn 'Abd al-Raḥmān narrated to us, from Mūsā ibn 'Uqbah, from Sālim, from Ibn 'Umar رضي الله عنهما, who said:**\n\n\We used not to call Zayd ibn Ḥārithah anything other than **'Zayd ibn Muḥammad'** until the Qur'anic revelation came:\n\n> **'Call them (adopted sons) by (the names of) their fathers; that is more just in the sight of Allāh.'**\n> *(Sūrat al-Aḥzāb"
"3294","Abu Abdur-Rahman narrated from Ali that :the Messenger of Allah said: And you make your provision your demise! – he said: “Your gratitude is expressed by saying: ‘We received rain because of this and that celestial position"
"3295","Anas [may Allah be pleased with him] said:“The Messenger of Allah recited: Verily"
"3296","**Aḥmad ibn 'Abdah al-Ḍabbī narrated to us, Ḥammād ibn Zayd narrated to us, from Thābit, from Anas رضي الله عنه, who said:**\n\n\This verse was revealed:\n\n**'And you concealed in your heart that which Allāh was to bring to light"
"3297","Al-Hasan narrated that:Abu Hurairah said: “Once when the Prophet of Allah was sitting with his Companions"
"3298","Salamah bin Sakhr Al Ansari said:“I was a man who had an issue with intercourse with a women that none other than me had. When (the month of) Ramadan entered"
"3299","Ali bin Abi Talib said:“When (the following) was revealed: ‘O you who believe! When you consult the Messenger in private"
"3300","Anas bin Malik narrated that:A Jew came to the Prophet of Allah and his Companions and said: “As-Samu Alaikum (Death be upon you).” So the people replied to him. The Prophet of Allah said: “Do you know what this person said?” They said: “Allah and His Messenger know better – he said the Salam – O Allah’s Prophet.” He said: “No"
"3301","Ibn Umar [may Allah be pleased with him] said:“The Messenger of Allah ordered burning and cutting down the date palms of Banu An-Nadir"
"3302","Qutaybah ibn Sa'id narrated to us: Ja'far ibn Sulayman al-Duba'i narrated to us from al-Ja'd ibn 'Uthman, from Anas ibn Malik (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) married and consummated the marriage with his wife. My mother, Umm Sulaym, prepared hays (a dish of dates, cheese, and butter) and placed it in a cooking vessel (tawr). She said: ""O Anas, take this to the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) and say to him: 'My mother sends you her greetings of peace and says: This is a small gift from us to you, O Messenger of Allah.'"" So I took it to the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) and said: ""My mother sends you her greetings of peace and says: This is a small gift from us to you."" He said: ""Put it down."" Then he said: ""Go and invite so-and-so, and so-and-so, and so-and-so, and whomever you meet."" He named some men. So I invited those he named and those I met. I said to Anas: ""How many were you?"" He said: ""About three hundred."" The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said to me: ""O Anas, bring the vessel."" They entered until the Suffah and the room were filled. The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: ""Let them sit in circles of ten, and let each person eat from what is in front of him."" They ate until they were satisfied. Then one group left and another entered until they had all eaten. He said to me: ""O Anas, lift it (the vessel)."" I lifted it, and I do not know whether it was more when I put it down or when I lifted it. Groups of them remained sitting, conversing in the house of the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ), while the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) was sitting and his wife had turned her face toward the wall. They overstayed their welcome with the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ), so he went out and greeted his wives, then returned. When they saw the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) had returned, they thought they had burdened him, so they rushed to the door and all left. The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) came and lowered the curtain and entered, while I was sitting in the room. He did not stay but a short while before he came out to me, and these verses were revealed. The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) went out and recited them to the people: ""O you who have believed, do not enter the houses of the Prophet except when you are permitted for a meal, without awaiting its readiness..."" until the end of the verse. Al-Ja'd said: Anas said: ""I am the most recent of people in acquaintance with these verses, and the wives of the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) were veiled (hijab was ordained)."" Abu 'Isa said: This is a Hasan Sahih hadith. Al-Ja'd is ibn 'Uthman, also said to be ibn Dinar, kunya Abu 'Uthman, Basri, and he is trustworthy (thiqah) according to the people of hadith. Yunus ibn 'Ubayd, Shu'bah, and Hammad ibn Zayd narrated from him."
"3303","Abu Hurairah narrated:That a man from the Ansar had a guest spend the night with him"
"3304","Al-Hasan bin Muhammad – and he is Al-Hanafiyyah- narrated from Ubaidallah bin Abi Rafi who said:“I heard Ali bin Abi Talib saying: “the Messenger of Allah dispatched us – myself"
"3305","**Abd ibn Humayd narrated to us:** Rawh ibn 'Ubādah narrated to us, from 'Awf, from al-Hasan, Muhammad, and Khilās, from Abū Hurayrah (may Allāh be pleased with him), from the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him), who said:\n\n> Indeed, Mūsā (peace be upon him) was a man of great modesty and concealment, such that none of his skin was ever seen, out of his bashfulness. Thus, those among the Children of Israel who wished to harm him said: \He conceals himself with this covering only because of some defect in his skin — either leprosy"
"3306","Abu Kurayb, 'Abd ibn Humayd, and others narrated to us; they said: Abu Usamah informed us from al-Hasan ibn al-Hakam al-Nakha'i; Abu Sabrah al-Nakha'i narrated to us from Farwah ibn Musayk al-Muradi, who said: I came to the Prophet (ﷺ) and said: ""O Messenger of Allah, shall I not fight those who turned back from my people with those who came forward from them?"" He permitted me to fight them and appointed me (as commander). When I left him, he asked about me: ""What did al-Ghutayfi do?"" He was informed that I had set out. So he sent someone after me and had me brought back. I came to him while he was with a group of his Companions. He said: ""Call the people. Whoever accepts Islam from them, accept it from him; and whoever does not accept Islam, do not hasten against them until I send word to you."" Then what was revealed concerning Saba' was revealed. A man said: ""O Messenger of Allah, what is Saba'? A land or a woman?"" He said: ""It is neither a land nor a woman, but a man who fathered ten from the Arabs. Six of them went to Yemen (Tayammanu) and four went to Syria (Tasha'amu). As for those who went to Syria: Lakhm, Judham, Ghassan, and 'Amilah. As for those who went to Yemen: Azd, Ash'ariyun, Himyar, Madhhij, Anmar, and Kinda."" A man said: ""O Messenger of Allah, what is Anmar?"" He said: ""Those from whom are Khath'am and Bajilah."" This was also narrated from Ibn 'Abbas from the Prophet (ﷺ). Abu 'Isa said: This is a Hasan Gharib hadith."
"3307","Narrated Abu Hurayrah (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said:\n\n\When Allah decrees a matter in the heavens"
"3308","Nasr ibn 'Ali al-Jahdami narrated to us: 'Abd al-A'la narrated to us: Ma'mar narrated to us from al-Zuhri, from 'Ali ibn al-Husayn, from Ibn 'Abbas, who said: While the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) was sitting with a group of his Companions, a star was shot (across the sky) and it lit up. The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: ""What did you used to say about the like of this in the Jahiliyyah when you saw it?"" They said: ""We used to say: A great man dies or a great man is born."" The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: ""Rather, it is not shot for the death of anyone nor for his life. But when our Lord, Mighty and Majestic, decrees a matter, the Bearers of the Throne glorify Him, then the inhabitants of the heaven nearest to them glorify Him, then those nearest to them, until the glorification reaches this heaven of the world. Then the inhabitants of the sixth heaven ask the inhabitants of the seventh heaven: 'What did your Lord say?' They inform them. Then the inhabitants of each heaven seek information until the news reaches the inhabitants of the lowest heaven. The devils snatch the hearing, so they are pelted (with stars), and they cast it to their allies. Whatever they bring as it is, is true, but they distort and add to it."" Abu 'Isa said: This is a Hasan Sahih hadith. This hadith has also been narrated from al-Zuhri, from 'Ali ibn al-Husayn, from Ibn 'Abbas, from men of the Ansar (may Allah be pleased with them), who said: ""We were with the Prophet (ﷺ)."" Al-Awza'i narrated from al-Zuhri from 'Ubaydullah from Ibn 'Abbas from men of the Ansar, who said: ""We were with the Prophet (ﷺ),"" and he mentioned something similar in meaning. Al-Husayn ibn Hurayth narrated this to us: Al-Walid ibn Muslim narrated to us: Al-Awza'i narrated to us."
"3309","Abu Hurairah said:“We were with the Messenger of Allah when Surat Al-Jumuah was revealed"
"3310","Jabir said:“The Prophet was standing and delivering a Khutbah for us on one Friday"
"3311","Zaid bin Aslam said:“I was with my uncle when I heard Abdullah bin Ubayy bin Salul saying to his companions: Do not spend on those who are with the Messenger of Allah until they desert from him. If we return to Al-Madinah then the more honorable will expel the meaner among them. So I mentioned that to my uncle"
"3312","Zaid bin Arqam said:“We were participating in a battle along with the Messenger of Allah"
"3313","Al-Hakam bin Utaibah said:“I heard Muhammad bin Ka’b Al-Qurazi – forty years ago – narrating from Zaid bin Arqam [may Allah be pleased with him] that during the battle of Tabuk"
"3314","Sufyan narrated from Amr bin Dinar that he heard Jabir bin Abdullah saying:“We were in a battle” – Sufyan said: “They say it was the battle of Banu Mustaliq” – “A man from the Muhajirin kicked a man from the Ansar. The man from the Muhajirin said: ‘O Muhajirin!’ the man from the Ansar said: ‘O Ansar!’ The Prophet heard that and said: ‘What is this evil call of Jahliyyah?’ They said: ‘A man from the Muhajirin kicked a man from the Ansar.’ So the Prophet said: ‘Leave that"
"3315","Ad-Dahhak bin Muzahim narrated:From Ibn Abbas [may Allah be pleased with him] who said: “Whoever has wealth"
"3316","Ikrimah narrated that :Ibn Abbas was asked by a man about this Ayah: O you who believe! Verity"
"3317","Ikrimah narrated that :Ibn Abbas was asked by a man about this Ayah: O you who believe! Verity, among your wives and your children there are enemies for you; therefore beware of them! He said: “These are men who submitted (to Islam) in Makkah, and they wanted to come to the Prophet but their wives and children refused to allow them to come to the Messenger of Allah. So when they came to the Messenger of Allah, they saw that the people had gained such understanding in the religion that they wanted to punish them (their families). So Allah revealed the Ayah: O you who believe! Verily, among your wives and your children there are enemies for you; therefore beware of them!”"
"3318","Abdul-Wahid bin Sulaim said:“I arrived in Makkah and met Ata bin Abi Rabah. I said: ‘O Abu Muhammad! Some people with us speak about Al-Qadar.’ Ata said: ‘I met Al-Walid bin Ubadah bin As-Samit and he said: “My father narrated to me"
"3319","This hadith has also been narrated from Mu'adh ibn Jabal from the Prophet (ﷺ) at length, and he said: ""I dozed off, so sleep overcame me, and I saw my Lord in the most beautiful form. He said: 'In what do the Highest Assembly (al-Mala' al-A'la) dispute?'"" Muhammad ibn Bashshar narrated to us: Mu'adh ibn Hani' Abu Hani' al-Yashkuri narrated to us: Jahdam ibn 'Abdullah narrated to us from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir from Zayd ibn Salam from Abu Salam from 'Abd al-Rahman ibn 'A'ish al-Hadrami, that he narrated to him from Malik ibn Yukhamir al-Saksaki from Mu'adh ibn Jabal (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) was delayed from us one morning for the Fajr prayer until we almost saw the eye of the sun. He came out quickly, the iqamah was called, and the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) prayed, lightening his prayer. When he gave the taslim, he called out to us with his voice: ""Stay in your rows as you are."" Then he turned to us and said: ""I will tell you what detained me from you this morning. I stood in the night, performed wudu, and prayed what was decreed for me. I dozed off in my prayer until sleep overcame me, and behold, I saw my Lord, Blessed and Exalted, in the most beautiful form. He said: 'O Muhammad.' I said: 'Here I am, my Lord.' He said: 'In what do the Highest Assembly dispute?' I said: 'I do not know.' He said it three times. I saw Him place His palm between my shoulders until I felt the coolness of His fingertips between my breasts. Everything was unveiled for me and I knew. He said: 'O Muhammad.' I said: 'Here I am, my Lord.' He said: 'In what do the Highest Assembly dispute?' I said: 'In the expiations (al-kaffarat).' He said: 'What are they?' I said: 'Walking feet to the congregations, sitting in the mosques after the prayers, and perfecting wudu in difficult circumstances.' He said: 'Then what?' I said: 'Feeding food, gentleness of speech, and prayer at night while people sleep.' He said: 'Ask.' I said: 'O Allah, I ask You for the doing of good deeds, leaving evil deeds, love of the poor, and that You forgive me and have mercy on me. And if You intend to test a people, take me to You untested. I ask You for Your love, the love of those who love You, and the love of a deed that brings me near to Your love.'"" The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: ""Indeed, it is true, so study it and then learn it."" Abu 'Isa said: This is a Hasan Sahih hadith. I asked Muhammad ibn Isma'il about this hadith, and he said: ""This is a Hasan Sahih hadith."" And he said: ""This is more authentic than the hadith of Al-Walid ibn Muslim from 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Yazid ibn Jabir."" He said: Khalid ibn al-Lajlaj narrated to us: 'Abd al-Rahman ibn 'A'ish al-Hadrami narrated to me, saying: ""I heard the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ)..."" and he mentioned the hadith. This is not preserved (ghayr mahfuz). Thus Al-Walid mentioned in his hadith from 'Abd al-Rahman ibn 'A'ish: ""I heard the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ)."" Bishr ibn Bakr narrated from 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Yazid ibn Jabir this hadith with this chain from 'Abd al-Rahman ibn 'A'ish from the Prophet (ﷺ). And this is more authentic. 'Abd al-Rahman ibn 'A'ish did not hear from the Prophet (ﷺ)."
"3320","Abdur-Rahman bin Abdullah bin Sa’d Ar-Razi [and he is Ad-Dashtaki] narrated :that his father informed him"
"3321","Abu Sa’eed narrated :from the Prophet regarding Allah’s saying: Like Al-Muhl – he said: “Like boiling oil"
"3322","Ibn Abbas [may Allah be pleased with them] said:the Messenger of Allah did not recite for the jinns nor did he see them. The Messenger of Allah went out with a group of his Companions towards the Ukaz market. Something had been intervening between the Shayatin and the news from the heavens"
"3323","Muhammad ibn Bashshar narrated to us: Yahya ibn Sa'id narrated to us: Fudayl ibn 'Iyad narrated to us, from Mansur, from Ibrahim, from 'Abidah, from 'Abdullah, who said: So the Prophet (peace be upon him) laughed in amazement and affirmation. He said: This is a hasan sahih hadith."
"3324","Jabir bin Abdullah [may Allah be pleased with him] said:“I heard the Messenger of Allah – and he was narrating about the pause in Revelation – so he said in his narration: “I was walking"
"3325","Abu Sa’eed narrated that:The Messenger of Allah said: “As-Sa’ud is a mountain of fire"
"3326","Jabir [bin Abdullah] said:“Some people from the Jews said to some people among the Companions of the Prophet: ‘Does your Prophet know how many keepers are there in Jahannam?’ They said: ‘We do not know until we ask our Prophet and said: ‘O Muhammad! Your Companions were defeated today.’ He said: ‘In what were they defeated?’ He said: ‘Some Jews asked them if their Prophet knew how many keepers are there in Jahannam.’ He said: ‘So what did they say?’ He said: ‘They said: “We do not know until we ask our Prophet.” He said: ‘Are a people defeated who are asked about something that they do not know"
"3327","Anas bin Malik narrated that:The Messenger of Allah said regarding this Ayah: “He is the One deserving of the Taqwa"
"3328","Ibn Abbas said:“When the Quran was being revealed to the Messenger of Allah"
"3329","Ibn Abbas said:“When the Quran was being revealed to the Messenger of Allah, he would move his tongue in attempt to memorize it. So Allah, Blessed is He and Most High, revealed: Move not your tongue concerning it to make haste therewith.” He said: “So he would move his two lips.” And Sufyan (a sub-narrator) would move his two lips"
"3330","Aishah narrated:“He frowned and turned away” was revealed about Ibn Umm Maktum the blind man. He came to the Messenger of Allah saying: ‘O Messenger of Allah! Guide me.’ At that time"
"3331","Ibn Abbas narrated that :the Prophet said: “You will be gathered barefoot"
"3332","Ibn Umar narrated that:The Messenger of Allah said: “Whoever wishes to look at the Day of Resurrection"
"3333","Ibn Umar narrated that:The Messenger of Allah said: “Whoever wishes to look at the Day of Resurrection, as if he is seeing it with this eye, then let him recite: ‘When the sun Kuwwirat’ and ‘When the heaven is cleft sunder (Infatarat) and ‘When the heaven is split asunder.’”"
"3334","**Narration:**\n\nAbu Hafs 'Amr ibn al-Fallas narrated to us: Abu Qutaybah Salam ibn Qutaybah narrated to us: Suhayl ibn Abi Hazm al-Qata'i narrated to us: Thabit al-Bunani narrated to us from Anas ibn Malik (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) recited: *\Indeed"
"3335","Ibn Umar narrated from the Prophet:‘They Day when mankind will stand before the Lord of all that exists.’ He said: “One of them will be standing in sweat up to the middle of his ears.”"
"3336","Aishah said:“I heard that the Messenger of Allah saying: ‘Whoever is interrogated during the reckoning"
"3337","Anas narrated that:The Prophet said: “Whoever is reckoned with"
"3338","Abu Hurairah narrated that :the Messenger of Allah said: “Al-Yawmul-Maw’ud (the Promised Day) is the Day of Resurrection"
"3339","Abu Hurairah narrated that :the Messenger of Allah said: “Al-Yawmul-Maw’ud (the Promised Day) is the Day of Resurrection, and Al-Yawmul-Mashhud (the Attended Day) is the Day of Arafah, and Ash-Shahid (the witness) is Friday.” He said: “The sun does not rise nor set, upon a day that is more virtuous than it. In it, there is an hour in which no believing worshipper makes a supplication to Allah for good, except that Allah answers it for him, and he does not seek Allah’s aid for something, except that He aids him in it.”"
"3340","Jabir narrated that :the Messenger of Allah said: “I have been ordered to fight the people until they say: ‘La ilaha illallah’. So when they say that"
"3341","Imran bin Husain narrated that:The Prophet was asked about Ash-Shafi"
"3342","**Narrated by 'Alqamah (may Allah be pleased with him):**\n\nI said to Ibn Mas'ud (may Allah be pleased with him), \Did anyone among you accompany the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) on the Night of the Jinn?\"" He replied"
"3343","Ali [may Allah be pleased with him] said:“We were at a funeral at Al-Baqi when the Prophet came and sat. So we sat with him. He had a stick with which he was scratching his head toward the heavens"
"3344","Jundab Al-Bajali said:“I was with the Prophet in a battle when of his finger bled"
"3345","Anas bin Malik narrated from Malik bin Sa’sa’ah – a man among his people – that :the Prophet of Allah said: “While I was at the House"
"3346","Ismail bin Umayyah said:“I heard a Bedouin man saying: ‘I heard Abu Hurairah saying: “Whoever recited Surat ‘By At-Tim and Az-Zamzam’ Then he recited: ‘Is not Allah the best of judges?’ then let him say: ‘Of course"
"3347","Ikrimah narrated from Ibn Abbas [may Allah be pleased with them] regarding:We will call on the guards of Hell. He said: “Abu Jahl said: ‘If I see Muhammad praying"
"3348","Ibn Abbas narrated:“The Prophet was performing Salat when Abu Jahl came to him and said: ‘Have I not forbidden you from this? Have I not forbidden you from this? Have I not forbidden you from this?’ The Prophet turned and scolded him. So Abu Jahl said: ‘You know that no one has more to call for assistance than me.’ So Allah"
"3349","Ibn Abbas narrated:“The Prophet was performing Salat when Abu Jahl came to him and said: ‘Have I not forbidden you from this? Have I not forbidden you from this? Have I not forbidden you from this?’ The Prophet turned and scolded him. So Abu Jahl said: ‘You know that no one has more to call for assistance than me.’ So Allah, Blessed is He and Most High, revealed: Then let him call upon his council. We will call out the guards of Hell.” So Ibn Abbas said: “By Allah, if he had called his council, then the guards of Hell would have seized him.”"
"3350","Zirr bin Hubaish [and Zirr bin Hubaish’s Kunyah is Abu Mariam] said:“I said to Ubayy bin Ka’b: ‘Your brother Abdullah bin Mas’ud says: “Whoever stands (in voluntary prayer) the whole year"
"3351","Anas bin Malik narrated that:A man said to the Prophet: “O best of creatures!” So he said: “That is Ibrahim.”"
"3352","Narrated to us was ʿAbdullāh ibn Isḥāq al-Jawharī al-Baṣrī, who narrated to us from Abū Zayd, from Shuʿbah, from Dāwūd ibn Abī Hind, who said: I heard al-Shaʿbī narrating from Abū Jābirah ibn al-Ḍaḥḥāk, who said: \A man among us would have two or three names"
"3353","Mutarrif bin Abdullah bin Ash-Shikh-khir reported from his father"
"3354","Zirr bin Jubaish reported from Ali [may Allah be pleased with him] that he said:“We were still in doubt concerning the torment of the grave"
"3355","Abdullah bin Az-Zubair bin Al-Awwam narrated from his father who said:“When the following was revealed: Then on that Day"
"3356","Abu Hurairah said:“When this Ayah was revealed: ‘Then on that Day"
"3357","Abu Hurairah narrated that :the Messenger of Allah said: “Indeed the first of what will be asked about on the Day of Judgment – meaning the slave (of Allah) being questioned about the favors – is that it will be said to him: ‘Did We not make your body"
"3358","Abd ibn Humaid narrated to us: Zayd ibn Hubab narrated to us: Salam ibn Sulayman al-Nahwi, Abu al-Mundhir, narrated to us: Asim ibn Abi al-Najud narrated from Abu Wa'il, from al-Harith ibn Yazid al-Bakri, who said:\n\n\I arrived in Madinah and entered the mosque"
"3359","Anas narrated that the Messenger of Allah said:“While I was traveling through Paradise"
"3360","Abdullah bin `Umar narrated that :the Messenger of Allah said: “Al-Kauthar is a river in Paradise"
"3361","Ibn Abbas said:“Umar used to ask me questions in front of the Companions of the Prophet. So Abdur-Rahman bin Awf said to him: ‘Why do you ask him"
"3362","Ibn Abbas narrated:“One day the Messenger of Allah ascended As-Safa and called out: ‘O people! Come at once!’ So the Quraish gathered before him. He said: ‘I am a warner for you before the coming of a severe punishment. Do you think that if I informed you that the enemy was preparing to attack you in the evening or in the morning"
"3363","Abu Al-Aliyah narrated from Ubayy bin Ka’b:“The idolaters were saying to the Messenger of Allah: ‘Name the lineage of your Lord for us.’ So Allah"
"3364","Abu Al-Aliyah narrated:“The Prophet mentioned their (the idolater’s) gods"
"3365","Aishah narrated:“The Prophet looked at the moon and he said: ‘O Aishah! Do you seek refuge with Allah from the evil of this? For indeed this is Al-Ghasiqu Idha Waqab (The darkened one as it darkens).’”"
"3366","Uqbah bin Amir Al-Juhni narrated that:\\n\\nthe Prophet said: “Allah has revealed to me Ayat the likes of which have not been seen: “Say: I seek refuge in the Lord of mankind…” until the end of the Surat. “Say: I seek refuge in the Lord of Al-Falaq…” until the end of the Surat. \\nJam e Tirmazi Hadees: 3367 Arabic Hadees: 3367\""3367"""
"3367","ʿAbd ibn Ḥumayd narrated to us; ʿUbayd Allāh ibn Mūsā and Ibn Abī Rizmah narrated to us, from Isrāʾīl, from Abū Isḥāq, from ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Yazīd, from ʿAbd Allāh: (The heart did not lie about what it saw.) He said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ saw Jibrīl in a garment of rafraf filling what is between the heaven and the earth. Abū ʿĪsā said: This is a ḥasan ṣaḥīḥ ḥadīth."
"3368","He breathed the soul into him, then he sneezed and said: ‘All praise is due to Allah.’ So he praised Allah by His permission. Then His Lord said to him: ‘May Allah have mercy upon you O Adam. Go to those angels – to that gathering of them sitting – so say: “As-Salamu Alaikas-Salamu, Wa Rahmatullah’ Then he returned to his Lord, He said: ‘This is your greeting and the greeting of your children among each other.’ Then Allah said to him – while His Two Hands were closed – ‘Choose which of them you wish.’ He said: ‘I chose the right My Lord and both of the Hands of my Lord are right, blessed.’ Then He extended it, and there was Adam and his offspring in it.’ So he said: ‘What are these O my Lord?’ He said: ‘These are your offspring?’ Each one of them had his age written between his eyes. But among them there was a man who was the most illuminating of them – or among the most illuminated of them. He said: ‘O Lord! Who is this?’ He said: ‘This is your son Dawud, I wrote forty years for him.’ He said: ‘O Lord! Add to his age.’ He said: ‘That is what I have written for him.’ He said: ‘O Lord! Give him sixty of my years.’ He said: ‘So you shall have it.’” He said: “Then, he resided in Paradise as long as Allah willed, then he was cast from it, so Adam was counting for himself.” He said: “So the Angel of death came to him, and Adam said to him: ‘You are hasty, one-thousand years were written for me.’ He said: ‘Of course! But you gave sixty years to your son Dawud.’ So he rejected, and his offspring rejected, and he forgot, and his offspring forgot.” He said: “So ever since that day, what is written and witnessed has been decreed.” \\nJam e Tirmazi Hadees: 3368 Arabic Hadees: 3368\""3369"""
"3369","ʿAlī ibn Ḥajr narrated to us; ʿAlī ibn Mushir informed us, from al-Aʿmash, from Ibrāhīm, from Abū Maʿmar, from Ibn Masʿūd, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: While we were with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ at Minā, the moon split into two halves. One half was behind the mountain, and the other half was on this side of it. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to us: ""Bear witness."" Meaning: (The Hour has drawn near, and the moon has split.) Abū ʿĪsā said: This is a ḥasan ṣaḥīḥ ḥadīth."
"3370","Abu Hurairah narrated that:The Prophet said: “There is nothing more honorable with Allah [Most High] than supplication.”"
"3371","Anas bin Malik narrated that :the Prophet said: “The supplication is the essence of worship.”"
"3372","An-Nu`man bin Bashir narrated that:The Prophet said: “The supplication"
"3373","Abu Hurairah (ra) narrated that :the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: “Indeed"
"3374","Abu Musa Al-Ash`ari (ra) said:“We were with the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) on a military expedition. When we returned"
"3375","Abdullah bin Busr (ra) narrated that:A man said: “O Messenger of Allah (ﷺ), indeed, the legislated acts of Islam have become too much for me, so inform me of a thing that I should stick to.” He (ﷺ) said: “Let not your tongue cease to be moist with the remembrance of Allah.”"
"3376","Abu Sa’eed Al-Khudri narrated that:The Messenger of Allah was asked: “Which of the worshippers is superior in rank with Allah on the Day of Judgment?” He said: “Those men who remember Allah much [and women].” He said: “I said: ‘O Messenger of Allah! What about the fighter in the cause of Allah?’ He said: ‘If he were to strike with his sword among the disbelievers and the idolater"
"3377","Abu Ad-Darda [may Allah be pleased with him] narrated that :the Prophet said: “Should I not inform you of the best of your deed"
"3378","Abū Kurayb narrated to us, saying: Rizdīn ibn Saʿd narrated to us, from ʿAmr ibn al-Ḥārith, from Darrāj, from Abū al-Haytham, from Abū Saʿīd al-Khudriy رضي الله عنه, from the Prophet ﷺ regarding His (Exalted is He) words: *“And couches raised high”* (Qur’an 56:34). He ﷺ said: **“Their height is as the distance between the heaven and the earth, and the journey between them is five hundred years.”**\n\nAbū ʿĪsā (al-Tirmidhī) said: *“This is a ḥasan gharīb hadith; we do not know it except through the narration of Rizdīn.”*\n\nSome of the scholars of knowledge said: *“And their height is as the distance between the heaven and the earth.”* They explained: *“The elevation of the raised couches refers to the degrees (of Paradise), and the distance between each two degrees is as the distance between the heaven and the earth.”*"
"3379","Abu Sa’eed Al Khudri narrated the:Mu’awiyah came out to the Masjid and said: “What has caused you to gather for this sitting.” They said: “We gathered so that we may remember Allah.” He said"
"3380","Abu Hurairah [may Allah be pleased with him] narrated that :the Prophet said: “No group gather in a sitting in which they do not remember Allah"
"3381","Jabir narrated that :the Messenger of Allah said: “There is none who utters a supplication"
"3382","Abu Hurairah [may Allah be pleased with him] narrated that:The Messenger of Allah said: “Whoever wishes that Allah would respond to him during hardship and grief"
"3383","Jabir bin `Abdullah (ra) narrated that :the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: “The best remembrance is: ‘there is none worthy of worship except Allah (Lā ilāha illallāh)’ and the best supplication is: ‘All praise is due to Allah (Al-ḥamdulillāh).’”"
"3384","A'ishah (ra) narrated that :the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) used to remember Allah in all of his affairs"
"3385","Ibn `Abbas narrated from Ubayy bin Ka`b that :whenever the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) would mention someone and supplicate for him"
"3386","Umar bin Al-Khattab [may Allah be pleased with him] narrated:“Whenever the Messenger of Allah would raise his hands in supplication"
"3387","Abu Hurairah narrated that :the Prophet said: “One of you will be responded to, so long as he is not hasty, saying: ‘I supplicated, and I was not responded to.’”"
"3388","Aban bin `Uthman said:“I heard `Uthman bin `Affan (ra) saying: ‘The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: “There is no worshiper who says"
"3389","Thawban (ra) said:“The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: ‘Whoever says when he reaches the evening: “I am pleased with Allah as (my) Lord"
"3390","Narrated by Abd ibn Humayd, narrated by Abd al-Razzaq, from Ma'mar, from al-Zuhri, from 'Urwah, from 'Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her), who said: \The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) would not test [the believing women] except with the verse in which Allah"
"3391","Abu Hurairah (ra) said:The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) used to teach his Companions, saying: “When one of you reached the morning, then let him say: ‘O Allah, by You we enter the morning, and by You we enter the evening, and be You we live, and by You we died, and to You is the Return (Allāhumma bika aṣbaḥnā wa bika amsainā wa bika naḥyā wa bika namūtu wa ilaikal-maṣīr). And when he reaches the evening let him say: ‘O Allah, by You we enter the evening, and by You we enter the morning, and by You we live, and by You we die, and to You is the Resurrection (Allāhumma bika amsainā wa bika aṣbaḥnā wa bika naḥyā wa bika namūtu wa ilaikan-nushūr).’”"
"3392","Salamah ibn Shabib narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Yusuf al-Firyabi narrated to us, Qays ibn al-Rabi narrated from al-Agharr ibn al-Sabbah, from Khalifah ibn Husayn, from Abu Nasr, from Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him), regarding the Words of Allah, the Most High: \O you who believe"
"3393","Shaddad bin Aws narrated that:The Prophet (ﷺ) said to him: “Should I not direct you to the chief of supplications for forgiveness? ‘O Allah"
"3394","Al-Bara' bin `Azib narrated that:The Prophet (ﷺ) said to him: “Should I not teach you some words to say when you go to your bed"
"3395","Rafi` bin Khadij narrated that:The Prophet said: “When one of you lies down on his right side"
"3396","Abd ibn Humaid narrated to us: Ubayd Allah ibn Musa narrated to us, from Israil, from Abu Ishaq, from Zayd ibn Arqam, who said:\n\n\I was with my uncle when I heard Abdullah ibn Ubayy ibn Salul say to his companions: **'Do not spend upon those who are with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ until they disperse"
"3397","Abd ibn Humayd narrated to us: Ubaydullah ibn Musa narrated to us from Isra'il, from al-Suddi, from Abu Sa'id al-Azdi, who narrated to us: Zayd ibn Arqam said: We went on a military expedition with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and there were some Bedouins with us. We used to rush for water, and the Bedouins would get there before us. A Bedouin got ahead of his companions, so he filled the watering trough, placed stones around it, and spread a leather mat over it until his companions arrived. Then a man from the Ansar came to a Bedouin and let his camel's rope loose so it could drink, but the Bedouin refused to let him. The Ansari snatched the water bucket, so the Bedouin raised his wooden stick and struck the Ansari on the head, wounding him. The Ansari went to Abdullah ibn Ubayy, the leader of the hypocrites, and informed him; he was one of his companions. Abdullah ibn Ubayy became angry and then said: ""Do not spend on those who are with the Messenger of Allah until they disperse from around him."" He meant the Bedouins, who used to attend the Messenger of Allah ﷺ when food was brought. Abdullah said: ""When they disperse from Muhammad, bring Muhammad food so he and those with him may eat."" Then he said to his companions: ""By Allah, if we return to Medina, the more honorable will surely expel the more lowly from it."" Zayd said: I was riding behind the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and I heard Abdullah ibn Ubayy, so I informed my uncle. My uncle went and informed the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent for him, and he swore an oath and denied it. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ believed him and disbelieved me. My uncle came to me and said: ""You only wanted the Messenger of Allah ﷺ to despise you and the Muslims to disbelieve you."" Such grief fell upon me as never fell upon anyone. While I was walking with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ on a journey, my head drooping from grief, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ came to me, rubbed my ear, and smiled in my face. That was dearer to me than eternal life in this world. Then Abu Bakr caught up with me and said: ""What did the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say to you?"" I said: ""He said nothing except that he rubbed my ear and smiled in my face."" He said: ""Rejoice!"" Then Umar caught up with me and I told him the same as I told Abu Bakr. When morning came, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ recited Surat al-Munafiqun. Abu Isa said: This is a Hasan Sahih hadith."
"3398","Hudhaifah bin Al-Yaman (ra) narrated that:When the Prophet (ﷺ) would sleep, he would put his hand under his head then say: “O Allah, safeguard me from Your Punishment the Day You gather [Your slaves] (Allāhumma qinī `adhābaka yawma tajma`u [`ibādak])” or “you resurrect your slaves (tab`athu `ibādak).”"
"3399","Al-Bara' bin `Azib (ra) narrated that:The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) used to lay his head upon his right hand when going to sleep"
"3400","Abu Hurairah (ra) said:“The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) used to order that when one of us went to sleep"
"3401","Abu Hurairah (ra) narrated that :the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: “When one of you leaves his bed then returns to it"
"3402","**Abd ibn Humayd narrated to us:** Abd ar-Razzaq informed us, from Ma'mar, from az-Zuhri, from Ubaydullah ibn Abdullah ibn Abi Thawr, who said:\n\nI heard **Ibn Abbas** (may Allah be pleased with both of them) say:\n\n\I remained persistently eager to ask **Umar** (may Allah be pleased with him) about the two wives of the Prophet ﷺ concerning whom Allah"
"3403","Farwah bin Nawfal (ra) narrated that:He came to the Prophet (ﷺ) and said: “O Messenger of Allah"
"3404","Abd ibn Humayd narrated to us: Abd al-Rahman ibn Sa'd narrated to us from Amr ibn Abi Qays, from Simak ibn Harb, from Abdullah ibn Amir, from al-Ahnaf ibn Qays, from al-Abbas ibn Abd al-Muttalib, who said: He claimed he was sitting in al-Batha in a group, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was sitting among them when a cloud passed over them. They looked at it, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: ""Do you know what this is called?"" They said: ""Yes, this is a cloud (sahab)."" He said: ""And al-Muzn."" They said: ""And al-Muzn."" He said: ""And al-Anan."" They said: ""And al-Anan."" Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to them: ""Do you know the distance between the heaven and the earth?"" They said: ""No, by Allah, we do not know."" He said: ""The distance between them is either one, or two, or three and seventy years; and the heaven above it is likewise."" Until he counted seven heavens likewise. Then he said: ""Above the seventh heaven is a sea, between its top and bottom is the distance between heaven and heaven; and above that are eight angels, between their hooves and knees is the distance between heaven and heaven; then above their backs is the Throne, between its bottom and top is the distance between heaven and heaven; and Allah is above that."" Abd ibn Humayd said: I heard Yahya ibn Ma'in say: ""Abd al-Rahman ibn Sa'd does not intend to perform Hajj until we hear this hadith from him."" Abu Isa said: This is a Hasan Gharib hadith. Al-Walid ibn Abi Thawr narrated from Simak similarly and raised it. Sharik narrated from Simak part of this hadith and stopped it (did not raise it). And Abd al-Rahman is Ibn Abd Allah ibn Sa'd al-Razi."
"3405","A'isha (ra) said:“The Prophet (ﷺ) would not sleep until he recited Az-Zumar and Banu Isra’il.” Muhammad bin Ismail informed me: “This Abu Lubabah’s (a narrator in the chain) name is Marwan"
"3406","Ar-Irbad bin Sariyah (ra) narrated that:The Prophet (ﷺ) would not sleep until he had recited Al-Musabbihat"
"3407","A man from Banu Hanzalah said:“I accompanied Shaddad bin Aws [may Allah be pleased with him] on a journey"
"3408","Ali [may Allah be pleased with him] said:“Fatimah complained to me about her hands blistering from grinding flour. So I said: ‘If you were to approach your father and ask him for a servant?’ So he (the Prophet) said: ‘Should I not direct the two of you"
"3409","Ali [may Allah be pleased with him] said:“Fatimah went to the Prophet complaining of her hands blistering"
"3410","Abdullah bin `Amr [may Allah be pleased with both of them] said:“The Messenger of Allah said: ‘There are two characteristics over which a Muslim man does not guard"
"3411","Abdullah bin Amr [may Allah be pleased with him] said:“I saw the Messenger of Allah counting At-Tasbīḥ.”"
"3412","Ka’b bin Ujrah narrated that:The Prophet said: “There are Mu’aqqibat"
"3413","Zaid bin Thabit (ra) said:“We were ordered to say the Tasbīḥ at the end of every Salat thirty-three times"
"3414","**Abd ibn Humayd narrated to us** — Shabābah informed us, from Isrā'īl, from Thuwayr, who said: **I heard Ibn ʿUmar (may Allah be pleased with both of them) saying: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said:**\n\n> *\Indeed"
"3415","Maslamah bin `Amr said:“`Umair bin Hani used to perform a thousand prostrations every day and recite a hundred thousand Tasbīḥs every day.”"
"3416","Rabi`ah bin Ka`b Al-Aslami said:“I used to spend the night at the door of the Prophet (ﷺ)"
"3417","Hudhaifah bin Al-Yaman [may Allah be pleased with him] narrated that when the Prophet (ﷺ) wanted to sleep"
"3418","Abdullah bin `Abbas [may Allah be pleased with them] narrated"
"3419","Narrated by Yahya ibn Durust, a Basran scholar, who reported from Hammad ibn Zayd, from Ayyub, from Nafi', from Ibn 'Umar, may Allah be pleased with them both. Hammad stated that this narration is, in our view, elevated (marfū') to the Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him. The verse: \The Day when mankind will stand before the Lord of the Worlds\"" (Qur'an 83:6) — he"
"3420","Abu Salamah said:“I asked Aishah [may Allah be pleased with her]: ‘With what did the Prophet used to open his Salat when he stood up in the night?’ She said: ‘When he stood up in the night"
"3421","Ali bin Abi Talib narrated that whenever the Messenger of Allah would stand for Salat"
"3422","Ali bin Abi Talib narrated that whenever the Messenger of Allah would stand for Salat"
"3423","Ali bin Abi Talib narrated that :when the Messenger of Allah would stand for the obligatory prayer"
"3424","Al-Hasan bin Muhammad bin Ubaidullah bin Abi Yazid said:“Ibn Juraij said to me: “Ubaidullah bin Abi Yazid informed me that Ibn Abbas said: “A man came to the Prophet and said: ‘O Messenger of Allah! I had a dream at night while I was sleeping"
"3425","Aishah narrated:“When the Messenger of Allah would prostrate (for recitation of) the Qur’an"
"3426","Anas bin Malik narrated that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said:“Whoever says – that is: when he leaves his house – ‘In the Name of Allah"
"3427","Umm Salamah narrated that :When the Prophet (ﷺ) would leave his house, he would say: “In the Name of Allah, I place my trust in Allah. O Allah! We seek refuge in You from slipping unintentionally or becoming misguided, or committing oppression or being oppressed, or acting ignorantly or being treated ignorantly (Bismillāh, tawakkaltu `alallāh. Allāhumma, innā na`ūdhu bika min an nazilla aw naḍilla, aw naẓlima aw nuẓlam, aw najhala aw yujhala alainā).”"
"3428","**Muḥammad ibn Bashshār narrated to us, ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Mahdī narrated to us, Zāʾidah ibn Qudāmah narrated from Manṣūr ibn al-Muʿtamir, from Saʿd ibn ʿUbaydah, from Abū ʿAbd al-Raḥmān al-Sulamī, from ʿAlī (may Allāh be pleased with him), who said:**\n\n\We were at a funeral procession in al-Baqīʿ when the Prophet (ṣallallāhu ʿalayhi wa sallam) came and sat down"
"3429","Narrated by Ibn Abi 'Umar, who narrated from Sufyan ibn 'Uyaynah, from al-Aswad ibn Qays, from Jundub al-Bajali, who said:\n\n\I was with the Prophet ﷺ in a cave when his finger bled. The Prophet ﷺ said: **'You are nothing but a finger that has bled"
"3430","Al-Agharr Abu Muslim narrated that he bears witness from Abu Sa’eed Al-Khudri and Abu Hurairah"
"3431","Umar narrated that:The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: “Whoever sees a person afflicted and say: ‘All praise is due to Allah Who saved me from that which He has afflicted you with"
"3432","Abu Hurairah narrated that:The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: “Whoever sees an afflicted person then says: ‘All praise is due to Allah who saved me from that which He has afflicted you with"
"3433","Abu Hurairah narrated that:The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: “Whoever sits in a sitting and engages in much empty"
"3434","**Mahmūd ibn Ghaylān** narrated to us, that **Abū Dāwūd al-Ṭayālisī** narrated to them, that **al-Qāsim ibn al-Faḍl al-Ḥaddānī** narrated from **Yūsuf ibn Saʿd**, who said:\n\nA man stood before **al-Ḥasan ibn ʿAlī** (may Allah be pleased with him) after he had pledged allegiance to **Muʿāwiyah** (may Allah be pleased with him), and said: *\You have blackened the faces of the believers!\""* — or he said: *\""O you who have blackened the faces of the believers!\""*\n\nHe (al-Ḥasan ibn ʿAlī"
"3435","Narrated by Ibn Abi 'Umar, narrated by Sufyan, from 'Abdah ibn Abi Lubabah and 'Asim ibn Bahdalah, who both heard Zirr ibn Hubaysh — and Zirr ibn Hubaysh was known as Abu Maryam — say: I said to Ubayy ibn Ka'b, \Your brother 'Abdullah ibn Mas'ud says: 'Whoever stands (in prayer) throughout the year will attain Laylat al-Qadr.'\"" Ubayy said: \""May Allah forgive Abu 'Abd al-Rahman. He knows that it is in the last ten nights of Ramadan"
"3436","Abu Hurairah narrated that:When a matter would worry the Prophet (ﷺ)"
"3437","Sa`d bin Abi Waqqas narrated:From Khawlah bint Al Hakim As-Sulamiyyah"
"3438","Mahmūd ibn Ghaylān narrated to us, saying: Wahb ibn Jarīr narrated to us, saying: Shuʿbah narrated to us from Qatādah, from Muṭarrif ibn ʿAbdullāh ibn al-Shikhkhīr, from his father, that he came upon the Prophet"
"3439","Abdullah bin Sarjis narrated that:When the Prophet (ﷺ) wanted to travel"
"3440","**Narrator:** This tradition was related by al-Zubayr ibn al-Awwam (may Allah be pleased with him), from his father.\n\n**Chain of Transmission:** Through the chain of narration — Ibn Abi 'Umar narrated to us; Sufyan ibn 'Uyaynah related to us, from Muhammad ibn 'Amr ibn 'Alqamah, from Yahya ibn 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Hatib, from 'Abdullah ibn al-Zubayr ibn al-'Awwam, from al-Zubayr himself (may Allah be pleased with him).\n\n**Text of the Narration:**\n\nWhen the verse of the Qur'an was revealed: *\Then you will surely be asked that Day about the pleasures [you enjoyed]\""* (Surah al-Takathur"
"3441","Anas narrated that:When the Prophet would return from a trip and see the walls of Al-Madinah"
"3442","Abd ibn Humaid narrated to us, from Shabābah, from ʿAbdullāh ibn al-ʿAlāʾ, from al-Ḍaḥḥāk ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn ʿArzam al-Ashʿarī, who said: I heard Abū Hurayrah (may Allāh be pleased with him) say: The Messenger of Allāh (peace and blessings be upon him) said: \Indeed"
"3443","Salim narrated that :when he intended to undertake a journey, Ibn `Umar used to say to a person to “Come close to me so that I may bid you farewell as the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) used to bid us farewell.” Then he would say: “I entrust to Allah your religion, and your trusts, and the last of your deeds (Astawdi`ullāha dīnaka wa amānataka wa khawātīma `amalik).”"
"3444","Anas said:“A man came to the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) and said: ‘I intend to undertake a journey"
"3445","Abu Hurairah [may Allah be pleased with him] narrated that :a man said: “O Messenger of Allah (ﷺ)"
"3446","Ali bin Rabi’ah said:“I witnessed Ali having an animal brought to him to ride. When he placed his foot in the stirrup he said: ‘In the Name of Allah"
"3447","Ibn `Umar narrated that:When the Prophet (ﷺ) wanted to travel, when he mounted his riding camel, he would say the Takbir three times and say: Glory is to Him Who has subjected this to us, and we were not able to do it. And, surely, to our Lord are we returning (Subḥān alladhī sakh-khara lanā hādhā wa mā kunnā lahū muqrinīn. Wa innā ilā rabbinā lamunqalibūn). Then he would say: “O Allah, I ask You in this journey of mine from the righteousness and piety and actions that which you are pleased with. O Allah, ease for us the path, and make near for us the distance of the land. O Allah, You are the companion in the journey, and the caretaker for the family. O Allah, accompany us in our journey, and take care of our families (Allāhumma innī as’aluka fī safarī hādhā minal-birri wat-taqwā, wa minal-`amali mā tarḍā. Allāhumma hawwin `alainal-masīra, waṭwi `annā bu`dal-arḍ. Allāhumma antaṣ-ṣāḥibu fis safari wal-khalīfatu fil-ahli. Allāhumma aṣḥabnā fī safarinā wakhlufnā fī ahlinā).” And when he would return to his family, he would say: “(We are) Returning, if Allah wills, repenting, worshipping, and to our Lord directing the praise (Ā’ibūna in shā’ Allāh, tā’ibūna `ābidūna lirabbinā hāmidūn).”"
"3448","Abu Hurairah [may Allah be pleased with him] narrated :that the Messenger of Allah said: “Three supplications are responded to: The supplication of the oppressed"
"3449","Abd ibn Humayd narrated to us: Ubayd Allah ibn Musa narrated to us, from Abu Ja'far ar-Razi, from ar-Rabi', from Abu al-Aliyah, that the Prophet ﷺ mentioned their gods, and they said: \Describe your Lord for us.\"" He said: Then Jibril (عليه السلام) came to him with this Surah: **\""Say: He is Allah"
"3450","Narrated by Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her): The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) looked at the moon and said, \O Aisha"
"3451","Bilal bin Yahya bin Talhah bin `Ubaidullah narrated :from his father"
"3452","Muhammad ibn Bashshar narrated to us: Safwan ibn Isa narrated to us: al-Harith ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Dhubab narrated to us from Sa'id ibn Abi Sa'id al-Maqburi, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: When Allah created Adam and breathed the spirit into him, he sneezed and said: ""Alhamdulillah (Praise be to Allah)."" So he praised Allah by His permission. His Lord said to him: ""May Allah have mercy on you, O Adam. Go to those angels, to an assembly of them sitting, and say: As-salamu alaykum."" They said: ""Wa alaykum as-salam wa rahmatullah."" Then he returned to his Lord and said: ""This is your greeting and the greeting of your descendants among themselves."" Allah said to him, and His two hands were closed: ""Choose whichever you wish."" He said: ""I choose the right hand of my Lord, and both of my Lord's hands are right and blessed."" Then He opened it, and there were Adam and his offspring. He said: ""O Lord, who are these?"" He said: ""These are your offspring."" And every human had his lifespan written between his eyes. Among them was a man, the most radiant of them, or one of the most radiant. He said: ""O Lord, who is this?"" He said: ""This is your son Dawud; I have written for him a lifespan of forty years."" He said: ""O Lord, increase his lifespan."" He said: ""That is what I have written for him."" He said: ""O Lord, then I have given him sixty years from my lifespan."" He said: ""You and that (are agreed)."" Then he was lodged in Paradise for whatever Allah willed, then he was brought down from it. Adam used to count (the years) for himself. Then the Angel of Death came to him, and Adam said: ""You have hastened; a thousand years were written for me."" He said: ""Yes, but you gave your son Dawud sixty years."" So he denied, and his offspring denied; and he forgot, and his offspring forgot. From that day, writing and witnesses were ordained. Abu Isa said: This is a Hasan Gharib hadith from this route. It has been narrated from other routes from Abu Hurayrah from the Prophet ﷺ, from the narration of Zayd ibn Aslam from Abu Salih from Abu Hurayrah from the Prophet ﷺ."
"3453","Abu Sa’eed Al-Khudri narrated that:He heard the Prophet saying: “When one of you sees a dream that he likes"
"3454","Abu Hurairah [may Allah be pleased with him] narrates, saying:“When the people would see the first fruit, they would bring it to the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ). When the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) would take it, he would say: ‘O Allah, bless for us our fruits, and bless for us our city, and bless for us our Sa` and our Mudd, O Allah, verily, Ibrahim is Your worshipper and Your friend and Your Prophet, and verily I am Your slave and Your Prophet, and indeed, he (i.e., Ibrahim AS) supplicated to You for Makkah, and I supplicate to You for Al-Madinah with the like of that with which he supplicated to You for Makkah, and the like of it with it.’ He said: Then he would call the smallest young child he saw and give him that fruit"
"3455","Abu Umamah narrated that :when the table spread would be lifted from in front of him"
"3456","Abu Sa`eed [may Allah be pleased with him] narrated that:When the Prophet (ﷺ) used to eat or drink"
"3457","Sahl bin Mu`adh bin Anas narrated from his father that:The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: “Whoever eats food and then says: ‘All praise is due to Allah who fed me this and granted it as provision to me"
"3458","Abu Hurairah [may Allah be pleased with him] narrated that:The Prophet said: “when you hear the crowing of the roosters"
"3459","Abdullah bin Amr narrated that :the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: “there is not anyone upon the earth who says: ‘None has the right to be worshipped but Allah"
"3460","Abu Musa Al-Ash`ari said:“We were with the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) on a military expedition. When we returned"
"3461","Ibn Mas`ud narrated that:The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: “I met Ibrahim on the night of my ascent"
"3462","Muhammad ibn Bashshar narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi narrated to us, Sufyan narrated from Abu Ishaq, from al-Aghar Abu Muslim, that he bore witness upon Abu Hurayrah and Abu Sa'id al-Khudri that they bore witness upon the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, that he said:\n\n\There is no group of people who remember Allah except that the angels surround them"
"3463","Mus`ab bin Sa`d narrated from his father, that :the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said to those sitting with him: “Is one of you incapable of attaining a thousand good deeds?” So a questioner among those seated with him asked him: “How can one of us earn a thousand good deeds?” He said: “(When) one of you recites a hundred Tasbīḥāt a thousand good deeds are written for him, and a thousand evil deeds are wiped away from him.”"
"3464","Jabir narrated that :The Prophet (ﷺ) said: “Whoever says: ‘Glory is to Allah"
"3465","Abu Hurairah narrated that :the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: “Whoever says: ‘Glory is to Allah"
"3466","Abu Hurairah narrated that:The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: “There are two statements that are light on the tongue"
"3467","Abu Hurairah narrates that:The Mesenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: “Whoever says: ‘There is none worthy of worship except Allah"
"3468","Abu Hurairah narrated that:The Prophet (ﷺ) said: “Whoever says in the morning and in the evening ‘Glory is to Allah and with His Praise (Subḥān Allāh"
"3469","**Narrated by Ubayy ibn Ka'b رضي الله عنه:**\n\nThe Messenger of Allah ﷺ, whenever he mentioned someone and supplicated for him, he would begin by supplicating for himself first.\n\n**Abu 'Isa (al-Tirmidhi) said:** This is a *hasan gharib sahih* hadith. And Abu Qatn's name is 'Amr ibn al-Haytham.\n\n- **\بَدَأَ بِنَفْسِهِ\""""""""** — \""""""""he would begin by supplicating for himself\"""""""" — This reflects the noble practice of the Prophet ﷺ to place himself first in supplication when praying for others"
"3470","Abū Mūsā, Muḥammad ibn al-Muthannā, Ibrāhīm ibn Yaʿqūb, and others narrated to us, saying: Ḥammād ibn ʿĪsā al-Juhaniyy narrated to us, from Ḥanẓalah ibn Abī Sufyān al-Jumaḥiyy, from Sālim ibn ʿAbdullāh, from his father, from ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb (may Allāh be pleased with him), who said:\n\nThe Messenger of Allāh (peace and blessings be upon him) would, when he raised his hands in supplication, not lower them until he wiped his face with them.\n\nMuḥammad ibn al-Muthannā said in his narration: \He did not return them until he wiped his face with them.\""\n\nAbū ʿĪsā said: This is a ṣaḥīḥ (authentic) and gharīb (uncommon) hadith. We do not know it except through the narration of Ḥammād ibn ʿĪsā"
"3471","Az-Zuhri said:“A Tasbihah in Ramadan is better than a thousand Tasbihah in other that it.”"
"3472","Tamim Ad-Dari narrated that:The Messsenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: “Whoever says ten times: ‘I bear witness that none has the right to be worshipped but Allah. Alone"
"3473","Abu Dharr narrated that:The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: “Whoever says at the end of every Fajr prayer"
"3474","**Sufyān ibn Wakī' narrated to us**, saying: **Jarīr narrated to us**, from **al-Ḥasan ibn 'Ubayd Allāh**, from **Ibrāhīm ibn Suwayd**, from **'Abd al-Raḥmān ibn Yazīd**, from **'Abdullāh** (may Allāh be pleased with him), who said:\n\n> The Prophet ﷺ, when evening came upon him, would say:\n>\n> *\We have reached the evening"
"3475","Fadalah bin `Ubaid narrated:“While the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) was seated"
"3476","Amr bin Malik Al-Janbi narrated that he heard Fadalah bin `Ubaid saying:“The Prophet (ﷺ) heard a man supplicating in his Salat but he did not send Salat upon the Prophet (ﷺ)"
"3477","Asma bint Yazid narrated that the Prophet (ﷺ) said:“Allah's greatest name is in these two Ayah: ‘And your deity is One deity"
"3478","Abu Hurairah narrated that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said:“Call upon Allah while being certain of being answered"
"3479","Abu Hurairah narrated that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said:“Call upon Allah while being certain of being answered, and know that Allah does not respond to a supplication from the heart of one heedless and occupied by play.”"
"3480","Narrated to us Ishaq ibn Mansur, that Affan ibn Muslim narrated to them, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Thabit, from Anas ibn Malik (may Allah be pleased with him), that when the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) retired to his bed, he would say:\n\n\All praise is due to Allah"
"3481","Abdullah bin `Amr narrated that:The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) used to say: “O Allah"
"3482","Imran bin Husain narrated:“The Prophet (ﷺ) said to my father: ‘O Husain"
"3483","Abū Kurayb narrated to us: Isḥāq ibn Manṣūr — he is the Salūlī — informed us, from Ibrāhīm ibn Yūsuf ibn Abī Isḥāq, from his father, from Abū Isḥāq, from Abū Burdah, from al-Barāʾ ibn ʿĀzib, may Allāh be pleased with them both, who said:\n\n\The Messenger of Allāh"
"3484","**Abdullāh ibn 'Abd al-Rahmān narrated to us, 'Amr ibn 'Awn informed us, Khālid ibn 'Abdullāh informed us from Suhayl, from his father, from Abū Hurayrah (may Allāh be pleased with him), who said:**\n\nThe Messenger of Allāh (peace and blessings be upon him) used to command us, when one of us took his bed, to say:\n\n*\O Allāh"
"3485","Anas narrated that :The Prophet (ﷺ) used to supplicate, saying: “O Allah, indeed, I seek refuge in You from laziness, weakness of old age, cowardice, stinginess, the trial of Al-Masih, and the punishment of the grave (Allāhumma innī a`ūdhu bika minal-kasali wal-harami wal-jubni wal-bukhli wa fitnatil-masīḥi wa `adhabil-qabr).”"
"3486","Anas bin Malik narrated that:The Prophet (ﷺ) visited a man who was so emaciated that he had become like a baby bird. He (ﷺ) said to him: “And did you not used to supplicate? Did you not used to ask Your Lord for sound health?” He said: “I used to say: “O Allah"
"3487","Hisham bin Hassan narrated from Al-Hasan :concerning the saying of Allah: O our Lord"
"3488","Hisham bin Hassan narrated from Al-Hasan :concerning the saying of Allah: O our Lord, give us good in this world, and good in the Hereafter. He said: “Knowledge and worship in this world, and Paradise in the Hereafter.”"
"3489","Abu Ad-Darda’ narrated that :the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: “It used to be from the supplication of Dawud that he would say: ‘O Allah"
"3490","Abdullah bin Yazid Al-Khatmi Al-Ansari narrated that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) used to say in his supplication:“O Allah grant me Your love and the love of those whose love will benefit me with You. O Allah"
"3491","Abdullah bin Yazid Al-Khatmi Al-Ansari narrated that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) used to say in his supplication:“O Allah grant me Your love and the love of those whose love will benefit me with You. O Allah, whatever you have provided me of that which I love, then make it strength for me for that which You love. O Allah, and what you have kept from me of that which I love, then make it for me a period of rest in that which You love. (Allāhummarzuqnī ḥubbuka, wa ḥubba man yanfa`unī ḥubbuhū `indak. Allāhumma mā razaqtanī mimmā uḥibbu faj`alhu quwwatan lī fīmā tuḥibb. Allāhumma wa mā zawaita `annī mimmā uḥibbu faj`alhu farāghan lī fīmā tuḥibb). “"
"3492","Aishah narrated:“I was sleeping at the side of the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ)"
"3493","Abdullah bin `Abbas narrated:that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) used [to teach them this supplication as he used] to teach them a Surat of the Quran: “O Allah"
"3494","Aishah narrated that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) used to supplicate with these words:“O Allah"
"3495","Aishah said:“I heard the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) saying at his death: ‘O Allah"
"3496","Abu Hurairah narrated that the Messenger of Allah said:“None of you should say: ‘O Allah forgive me if You wish. O Allah have mercy on me if You wish.’ Let him be firm in asking"
"3497","Abu Hurairah narrated that the Messenger of Allah said:“Our Lord descends every night to the nearest heaven"
"3498","Narrated by 'Ubadah ibn al-Samit (may Allah be pleased with him), who reported that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said:\n\n\Whoever awakens during the night and says: 'There is no deity worthy of worship except Allah alone"
"3499","It was narrated to us by Ali ibn Hujr, who narrated to us by Maslamah ibn Amr, who said: \Umair ibn Hani' used to perform one thousand prostrations every day and recite one hundred thousand tasbihs (glorifications).\"""""
"3500","Anas narrated that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said:“Whoever says in the morning: ‘O Allah we have reached morning"
"3501","Ibn `Umar said:“Rarely would the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) stand from a sitting until he supplicated with these words for his Companions: ‘O Allah"
"3502","Ibn `Umar said:“Rarely would the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) stand from a sitting until he supplicated with these words for his Companions: ‘O Allah, apportion for us, fear of You, that shall come between us and disobedience of You, and of obedience to You, which shall cause us to obtain Your Paradise, and of certainty, which shall make the afflictions of the world easy for us, and enjoyment of our hearing, and our seeing, and our strength as long as You keep us alive, and make it the inheritor of us. And let our vengeance be upon those who have wronged us, and aid us against those who show enmity towards us, and do not make our affliction in our religion, and do not make this world our greatest concern, nor the limit of our knowledge, and do not give power over us to those who will not have mercy on us. (Allāhumma-qsim lanā min khashyatika mā yaḥūlu, bainanā wa baina ma`āṣīka wa min ṭā`atika mā tuballighuna bihī jannatak, wa minal-yaqīni mā tuhawwinu bihī `alainā muṣībatid-dunyā, wa matti`na bi-asmā`inā wa abṣārina wa quwwatina mā aḥyaytanā, waj`alhul-wāritha minnā, waj`al tha’ranā `alā man ẓalamanā, wanṣurna `alā man `ādānā, wa lā taj`al muṣībatanā fī dīninā, wa lā taj`alid-dunyā akbara hamminā wa lā mablagha `ilminā, wa lā tusalliṭ `alainā man lā yarḥamunā).’”"
"3503","Abdullah ibn Abd al-Rahman narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Imran ibn Abi Layla informed us: my father narrated to me: Ibn Abi Layla narrated to me from Dawud ibn Ali — he is Ibn Abd Allah ibn Abbas — from his father, from his grandfather Ibn Abbas, who said: I heard the Prophet of Allah ﷺ say one night when he finished his prayer: ""O Allah, I ask You for a mercy from Yourself that guides my heart, gathers my affairs, joins my scattered state, rectifies my absence, raises my witness, purifies my deed, inspires me with my guidance, returns my affection, and protects me from every evil. O Allah, grant me faith and certainty after which there is no disbelief, and a mercy by which I attain the honor of Your generosity in this world and the Hereafter. O Allah, I ask You for success in giving, and contentment in decree, and the abode of martyrs, and the life of the fortunate, and victory over enemies. O Allah, I lay my need before You; and if my opinion falls short and my deed weakens, I am in need of Your mercy, so I ask You, O Judge of matters, O Healer of chests, as You adjudicate between the seas, to grant me refuge from the punishment of the Blaze, and from the cry of destruction, and from the trial of the graves. O Allah, whatever my opinion falls short of, and my intention does not reach, and my asking does not reach, of any good You promised any of Your creation, or any good You are giving to any of Your servants, I desire it from You and ask You for it by Your mercy, O Lord of the Worlds. O Allah, Possessor of the strong rope and the right command, I ask You for security on the Day of Promise, and Paradise on the Day of Eternity, with the brought-near witnesses, the bowing, the prostrating, those who fulfill the covenant. Indeed You are Merciful, Loving, and You do whatever You will. O Allah, make us guided, guiding, not misguided nor misguiding, at peace with Your allies and enemies to Your enemies; we love by Your love whoever loves You, and we oppose by Your enmity whoever opposes You. O Allah, this is the supplication, and upon You is the response; and this is the effort, and upon You is the reliance. O Allah, make for me light in my grave, light in my heart, light before me, light behind me, light on my right, light on my left, light above me, light below me, light in my hearing, light in my sight, light in my hair, light in my skin, light in my flesh, light in my blood, light in my bones. O Allah, magnify for me light, and give me light, and make for me light. Glory be to Him who assumed pride and spoke by it. Glory be to Him who wore majesty and was generous by it. Glory be to Him to whom glorification is due only. Glory be to the Lord of bounty and blessings. Glory be to the Lord of majesty and generosity. Glory be to the Lord of glory and honor."" Abu Isa said: This is a Gharib hadith; we do not know it except from the hadith of Ibn Abi Layla from this route. Shu'bah and Sufyan al-Thawri narrated from Salama ibn Kuhayl from Kurayb from Ibn Abbas from the Prophet ﷺ part of this hadith, but did not mention it in its full length."
"3504","Narrated by Yahya ibn Musa and others, who said: 'Umar ibn Yunus informed us, who said: 'Ikrimah ibn 'Ammar narrated to us, who said: Yahya ibn Abi Kathir narrated to us, who said: Abu Salamah narrated to us, who said:\n\n\I asked 'Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her): 'With what did the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) begin his prayer when he stood up at night?' She replied: 'When he stood up at night"
"3505","Abu Hurairah [may Allah be pleased with him] narrated the the Prophet said:“Indeed Allah has ninety-nine Names"
"3506","Al-Hasan ibn Ali al-Khallal narrated to us: Abu al-Walid al-Tayalisi narrated to us: Abd al-Aziz ibn Abi Salamah and Yusuf ibn al-Majishun narrated to us. Abd al-Aziz said: My uncle narrated to me. And Yusuf said: My father informed me: al-A'raj narrated to us from Ubaydullah ibn Abi Rafi from Ali ibn Abi Talib, who said: When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ stood for prayer, he would say: ""I have directed my face to Him who originated the heavens and the earth, inclining to truth (hanifan), and I am not of the polytheists. Indeed my prayer, my sacrifice, my living, and my dying are for Allah, Lord of the Worlds, no partner has He; and with that I was commanded, and I am of the Muslims. O Allah, You are the King, there is no god but You. You are my Lord and I am Your servant. I have wronged myself and confessed my sin, so forgive me all my sins; indeed none forgives sins but You. Guide me to the best of character; none guides to its best but You. Turn away from me its evil; none turns away its evil but You. Here I am at Your service, and all good is in Your hands, and evil is not attributable to You. I am by You and to You; Blessed are You and Exalted. I seek Your forgiveness and repent to You."" Then when he bowed, he would say: ""O Allah, to You I bowed, and in You I believed, and to You I submitted. My hearing, my sight, my bones, and my nerves have humbled themselves to You."" Then when he raised his head, he would say: ""O Allah, our Lord, to You is praise filling the heavens, filling the earth, filling what is between them, and filling whatever You will after that."" Then when he prostrated, he would say: ""O Allah, to You I prostrated, and in You I believed, and to You I submitted. My face prostrated to Him who created it, fashioned it, and brought forth its hearing and sight. Blessed is Allah, the Best of Creators."" Then he would say at the end, between the tashahhud and the taslim: ""O Allah, forgive me what I have sent forward and what I have left behind, what I have concealed and what I have declared, what I have exceeded, and what You know better than me. You are the Advancer and You are the Delayer; there is no god but You."" He said: This is a Hasan Sahih hadith."
"3507","**Al-Hasan ibn 'Ali al-Khallāl narrated to us**, who said: **Sulaymān ibn Dāwūd al-Hāshimī narrated to us**, who said: **'Abd ar-Rahmān ibn Abi'z-Zinād narrated to us**, from **Mūsā ibn 'Uqbah**, from **'Abdullāh ibn al-Fadl**, from **'Abd ar-Rahmān al-A'raj**, from **'Ubaydullāh ibn Abī Rāfi'**, from **'Alī ibn Abī Tālib** (may Allāh be pleased with him), from the **Messenger of Allāh** (peace and blessings be upon him), that:\n\nWhen he (peace and blessings be upon him) stood for the **obligatory prayer (al-salāt al-maktūbah)**, he would raise his hands to the level of his shoulders. He would also do this **when he had completed his recitation and intended to bow into rukū'**, and he would do it **when he raised his head from rukū'**. He would **not** raise his hands during any part of his prayer while he was **seated**. And when he **stood up from the two prostrations (sajdatayn)**, he would likewise raise his hands and say the takbīr.\n\nWhen he opened the prayer, after the takbīr, he would say:\n\n> *\I have turned my face toward Him Who created the heavens and the earth"
"3508","Abu Hurairah narrated that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said:“When you pass by the gardens of Paradise"
"3509","Anas bin Malik [may Allah be pleased with him] narrated that the Messenger of Allah said:“When you pass by the gardens of Paradise"
"3510","**Narrated to us Sa'īd ibn Yaḥyā ibn Sa'īd al-Umawī:** My father narrated to us, from Ibn Jurayy, from Isḥāq ibn 'Abdullāh ibn Abī Ṭalḥah, from Anas ibn Mālik (may Allāh be pleased with him), who reported that the Messenger of Allāh (ṣallallāhu 'alayhi wa sallam) said:\n\n> *\Whoever says — meaning when he exits his home — 'Bismillāh"
"3511","Anas bin Malik narrated that a man came to the Prophet (ﷺ) and said:“O Messenger of Allah"
"3512","**Narrated by Ahmad ibn Mani'** — **Yazid ibn Harun** narrated to us — **Azhar ibn Sinan** informed us — **Muhammad ibn Wasi'** narrated to us, who said:\n\n\I came to Makkah"
"3513","Aishah narrated:“I said: ‘O Messenger of Allah, what is your view if I know when the Night of Al-Qadr is, then what should I say in it?” He said: ‘Say: “O Allah, indeed You are Pardoning, [Generous,] You love pardon, so pardon me (Allāhumma innaka `Afuwwun [Karīmun], tuḥibbul-`afwa fa`fu `annī).’”"
"3514","Ibn Umar narrated that the Messenger of Allah said (ﷺ):“Allah has not been asked for anything more beloved to Him than being asked for Al-`Āfiyah"
"3515","**Narrated to us Muhammad ibn 'Abdullah ibn Bazī' — narrated to us 'Abdul-Wārith ibn Sa'īd — from 'Amr ibn Dīnār, the mawlā of the family of al-Zubayr — from Sālim ibn 'Abdullah ibn 'Umar — from Ibn 'Umar — from 'Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said:**\n\n\Whoever sees one afflicted with a trial and says"
"3516","Abu Malik Al-Ash`ari narrated that the Messenger of Allah said:“Al-Wudu is half of faith"
"3517","Abdullah bin Amr narrated that the Messenger of Allah said:“At-Tasbīḥ is half of the Scale"
"3518","A man from Banu Sulaim narrated:“The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) counted them out in my hand” - or - “in his hand: ‘At-Tasbīḥ is half of the Scale"
"3519","Ali bin Abi Talib said:“The most of what the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) supplicated with during the afternoon at Arafat while standing was: ‘O Allah to You is the praise like the one You say"
"3520","Abu Umamah narrated:“The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) supplicated with many supplications of which we did not preserve a thing. We said: ‘O Messenger of Allah"
"3521","Shahr bin Hawshab said:“I said to Umm Salamah: ‘O Mother of the Believers! What was the supplication that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said most frequently when he was with you?” She said: ‘The supplication he said most frequently was: “O Changer of the hearts"
"3522","Sulaiman bin Buraidah narrated that his father said:“Khalid bin Al-Walid al Makhzumi complained to the Prophet (ﷺ) saying: ‘O Messenger of Allah"
"3523","Narrated to us Ahmad ibn 'Abdah al-Dhabbiyy, narrated to us Hammad ibn Zayd, from 'Asim al-Ahwal, from 'Abdullah ibn Sarjis, who said:\n\nWhen the Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him, would travel, he would say:\n\n\O Allah"
"3524","Anas narrated that the Prophet (ﷺ) said:“Be constant with: ‘O Possessor of Majesty and Honor (Yā Dhal-Jalāli wal-Ikrām).’”"
"3525","Abu Umamah Al-Bahili said:“I heard the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) saying: “Whoever goes to his bed while in a state of purity and remembering Allah"
"3526","Mu`adh bin Jabal narrated that the Prophet (ﷺ) heard a man supplicating"
"3527","Narrated to us Ismāʿīl ibn Mūsā al-Fazārī, narrated to us Saʿīd ibn Khuthaym, from Ḥanẓalah, from Sālim, that Ibn ʿUmar (may Allah be pleased with them both) used to say to a man when he intended to travel: \Come close to me so that I may bid you farewell"
"3528","Abu Rashid Al-Hubrani said:“I came to `Abdullah bin `Amr and said to him: ‘Report something to me that you heard from the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ).’ So he set forth before me a scroll and said: ‘This is what the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) wrote for me.’” He said: “So I looked in it and found in it: ‘Indeed"
"3529","Amr bin Murrah said:“I heard Abu Wa’il say: ‘`Abdullah bin Mas`ud said’ and I said to him: ‘Did you hear it from `Abdullah?’ He said: ‘Yes.’ And he narrated it in Marfu` form that he said: ‘There is none with more Ghirah than Allah"
"3530","Abdullah bin `Amr narrated from Abu Bakr As-Siddiq that he said:“O Messenger of Allah"
"3531","Al-Muttalib bin Abi Wada`ah said:“Al-`Abbas came to the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) and it is as if he heard something"
"3532","Al-Muttalib bin Abi Wada`ah said:“Al-`Abbas came to the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) and it is as if he heard something, so the Prophet (ﷺ) stood upon the Minbar and said: ‘Who am I?’ They said: ‘You are the Messenger of Allah, upon you be peace.’ He said: ‘I am Muhammad bin `Abdullah bin `Abdul-Muttalib, indeed Allah created the creation, and He put me in the best group of them, then He made them into two groups, so He put me in the best group of them, the He made them into tribes, so He put me in the best of tribes, then He made them into houses, so He put me in the best of them in tribe and lineage.’”"
"3533","Umarah bin Shabib As-Saba’i narrated that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said:“Whoever says: none has the right to be worshipped but Allah"
"3534","Zirr bin Hubaish said:“I came to Safwan bin `Assal Al Muradi to ask him about wiping over the Khuff"
"3535","Zirr bin Hubaish said:“I came to Safwan bin `Assal Al-Muradi so he said to me: ‘What has brought you"
"3536","Ibn `Umar narrated that the Prophet (ﷺ) said:“Indeed Allah accepts the repentance of a slave as long as (his soul does not reach his throat).”"
"3537","Abu Hurairah narrated that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said:“Allah is more delighted with the repentance of one of you"
"3538","Narrated by al-Ansari, narrated by Ma'n, narrated by Malik, and reported by Qutaibah, from Malik, from Suhail ibn Abi Salih, from his father, from Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him), who said:\n\n\When the people saw the first fruits"
"3539","Abu Sirmah narrated from Abu Ayyub, that:when death reached him, he said: “I have concealed something I heard from the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) from you. I heard the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) saying: ‘If you did not sin, Allah would create a creation that would sin, so He will forgive them.’”"
"3540","Abu Hurairah narrated that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said:“Allah created a hundred mercies"
"3541","Abu Hurairah narrated that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said:“If the believer knew what is with Allah of punishment"
"3542","Abu Hurairah narrated that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said:“Verily"
"3543","Anas said that:The Prophet (ﷺ) entered the Masjid and there was a man who had performed Salat and was supplicating. He was saying in his supplication: “O Allah"
"3544","Abu Hurairah narrated that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said:“May the man before whom I am mentioned - and he does not send Salat upon me - be humiliated. And may a man upon whom Ramadan enters and then passes"
"3545","Ali bin Abi Talib narrated that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said:“The stingy person is the one before whom I am mentioned"
"3546","Abdullah bin [Abi] Awfa narrated that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) used to say:“O Allah"
"3547","Ibn `Umar narrated that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said:“Whomsoever of you the door of supplication is opened for"
"3548","That was narrated to us by Al-Qasim bin Dinar Al-Kufi (who said):“Ishaq bin Mansur narrated to us"
"3549","**Jābir (may Allāh be pleased with him) reported that the Prophet Muḥammad (ṣallallāhu ʿalayhi wa sallam) said:**\n\n**\Whoever says 'Subḥānallāhi l-ʿAẓīm wa bi-ḥamdihi' (Glorified is Allāh"
"3550","It was narrated to us Nasr ibn ‘Abd al-Rahman al-Kūfī, that al-Muhāribī narrated to them, from Mālik ibn Anas, from Sumayy, from Abū Ṣāliḥ, from Abū Hurayrah (may Allāh be pleased with him) that the Messenger of Allāh ﷺ said:\n\n\Whoever says ‘Subḥān Allāh wa bi-ḥamdihi’ (Glorified is Allāh"
"3551","Narrated by Abū Hurayra, may Allāh be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of Allāh, peace and blessings be upon him, said:\n\n\Two words which are light upon the tongue"
"3552","Abu Ayyub Al-Ansari narrated that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said:“Whoever says ten times: ‘None has the right to be worshipped by Allah"
"3553","Saffiyah narrated:“The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) entered upon me and before me were four thousand date pits"
"3554","Narrated Isma'il ibn Musa al-Kufi, from Dawud ibn al-Zibriqan, from Matar al-Warraq, from Nafi', from Ibn 'Umar (may Allah be pleased with both), who said:\n\nThe Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said one day to his companions: \Say 'Subhan Allah wa bihamdihi' (Glory be to Allah and His is the praise) one hundred times. Whoever says it once shall have ten good deeds written for him; whoever says it ten times shall have one hundred written for him; and whoever says it one hundred times shall have one thousand written for him. And whoever increases beyond that"
"3555","Muḥammad ibn Wazīr al-Wāsiṭī narrated to us, Abū Sufyān al-Ḥimyarī, who is Saʿīd ibn Yaḥyā al-Wāsiṭī, narrated to us, from al-Ḍaḥḥāk ibn Ḥumrah, from ʿAmr ibn Shuʿayb, from his father, from his grandfather, who said:\n\nThe Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, said:\n\n\Whoever glorifies Allah (says *SubḥānAllāh*) one hundred times in the morning and one hundred times in the evening"
"3556","Abu Hurairah narrated that:A man was supplicating with his two fingers so the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: “Make it one"
"3557","**Qutaybah ibn Sa'īd narrated to us, al-Layth narrated to us, from al-Khalīl ibn Murrah, from al-Azhar ibn 'Abdillāh, from Tamīm al-Dārī, from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, that he said:**\n\n\Whoever says ten times: *'I bear witness that there is no deity worthy of worship except Allah alone"
"3558","Abu Bakr narrated:That the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: “He who seeks forgiveness has not been persistent in sin"
"3559","Abu Umamah narrated:That `Umar bin Al-Khattab [may Allah be pleased with him] wore a new garment and said: “All praise is due to Allah who clothed me with what I may cover my `Awrah"
"3560","Umar bin Al-Khattab narrated:That the Prophet (ﷺ) sent an expedition in the direction of Najd. They gained many spoils of war and returned quickly. A man among those who did not go out said: “We have not seen an expedition quicker in return or greater in spoils than this expedition.” So the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: “Should I not direct you to a group greater in spoils and quicker in return? A group who attended Salat As-Subh"
"3561","Ibn `Umar narrated from `Umar:that he sought permission from the Prophet (ﷺ) concerning `Umrah"
"3562","Ali [may Allah be pleased with him] narrated:that a Mukatib came to him and said: “Indeed I am not capable of my Kitabah so aid me.” He said: “Should I not teach you words that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) taught me? If you had a debt upon you similar to the mountain of Sir"
"3563","Ali said:“I was ill and the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) passed by me while I was saying: ‘O Allah"
"3564","Abū Kurayb narrated to us, Muʿāwiyah ibn Hishām narrated to us, from Ḥamzah al-Zayyāt, from Ḥabīb ibn Abī Thābit, from ʿUrwah, from ʿĀʾishah (may Allāh be pleased with her), who said: The Messenger of Allāh (peace and blessings be upon him) used to say: \O Allāh"
"3565","Ali bin Abi Talib narrated:that the Prophet (ﷺ) used to say in his Witr: “O Allah"
"3566","Mus`ab bin Sa`d and `Amr bin Maimun narrated:“Sa`d used to teach his children these words just as the Muktib teaches children"
"3567","**Narrated by Imran ibn Husayn (may Allah be pleased with him):**\n\nHe said: The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said to my father, \O Husayn"
"3568","Az-Zubair bin `Awwam narrated:that the Prophet (ﷺ) said: “There is not a morning that the slave of Allah reached except that a caller calls out: ‘Glorify the King"
"3569","Narrated by Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) used to supplicate, saying:\n\n\O Allah"
"3570","Abdullah narrated that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said:“Ask Allah of His Bounty. For verily"
"3571","Zaid bin Arqam [may Allah be pleased with him] said that the Prophet (ﷺ) used to say:“O Allah"
"3572","Jubair bin Nufair narrated that `Ubadah bin As-Samit narrated to them that"
"3573","Al-Bara’ bin `Azib narrated that the Prophet (ﷺ) said:“When you go to your bed"
"3574","Abū Kurayb narrated to us — Muḥammad ibn Fuḍayl narrated to us — from Muḥammad ibn Saʿd al-Anṣārī — from ʿAbdullāh ibn Rabīʿah al-Dimashqī — ʿĀʾidhullāh, Abū Idrīs al-Khawlānī, narrated to us — from Abū al-Dardāʾ, who said:\n\nThe Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, said:\n\n\It was from the supplication of Dāwūd"
"3575","Abdullah bin Busr narrated:“The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) stayed with my father.” So he said: “We brought some food near him"
"3576","Bilal bin Yasar bin Zaid [the freed slave of the Prophet(ﷺ)] narrated:“My father narrated to me"
"3577","Uthman bin Hunaif narrated that a blind man came to the Prophet (ﷺ) and said:“Supplicate to Allah to heal me.” He (ﷺ) said: “If you wish I will supplicate for you"
"3578","Abu Umamah [may Allah be pleased with him] said:`Amr bin `Abasah reported to me that he heard the Prophet (ﷺ) say: “The closest that the Lord is to a worshipper is during the last part of the night"
"3579","Abu Umamah [may Allah be pleased with him] said:`Amr bin `Abasah reported to me that he heard the Prophet (ﷺ) say: “The closest that the Lord is to a worshipper is during the last part of the night, so if you are able to be of those who remember Allah in that hour, then do so.”"
"3580","Narrated to us was Harun bin Ishaq, narrated to us Abdah, from Hisham bin Urwah, from Abbad bin Abdullah bin al-Zubair, from Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her), she said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) saying at the time of his death: \O Allah"
"3581","Safwan bin Sulaim said:“No angel has risen from the earth until he said: ‘There is no might or power except with Allah (Lā ḥawla wa lā quwwata illā billāh).’”"
"3582","Humaidah bint Yasir narrated from her grandmother Yusairah - and she was one of those who emigrated - she said:“The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said to us: ‘Hold fast to At-Tasbih"
"3583","Anas narrated that when the Prophet (ﷺ) would go out for an expedition"
"3584","**Narrated by 'Alī ibn Ḥujr — from 'Abd al-Ḥamd ibn 'Umar al-Hilālī — from Sa'īd ibn Iyās al-Jurayrī — from Abū al-Salīl — from Abū Hurayrah (may Allāh be pleased with him):**\n\nA man said: \O Messenger of Allāh ﷺ"
"3585","Amr bin Shu`aib narrated from his father, from his grandfather, that the Prophet (ﷺ) said:“The best of supplication is the supplication of the Day of `Arafah. And the best of what I and the Prophets before me have said is: None has the right to be worshipped but Allah, Alone, without partner, to Him belongs all that exists, and to Him belongs the Praise, and He is powerful over all things. (Lā ilāha illallāh, waḥdahu lā sharīka lahu, lahul-mulku wa lahul-ḥamdu, wa huwa `alā kulli shai’in qadīr).’”"
"3586","**Narrated by Ibn 'Umar (may Allah be pleased with him):**\n\nIt was seldom that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) would rise from a gathering without supplicating with these words for his Companions (may Allah be pleased with them):\n\n> \O Allah"
"3587","Muhammad bin Sulaim narrated:“Thabit Al-Bunani narrated to me"
"3588","**Narrated by ʿAlī ibn Khashram**, who said: **al-Faḍl ibn Mūsā** informed us, from **al-Ḥusayn ibn Wāqid**, from **Abū Isḥāq**, from **al-Ḥārith**, from **ʿAlī** (may Allāh be pleased with him), who said:\n\nThe Messenger of Allāh (ṣallallāhu ʿalayhi wa-sallam) said to me: **\Shall I not teach you words which"
"3589","Abu Hurairah [may Allah be pleased with him] narrated that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said:“No worshipper has ever said: None has the right to be worshipped but Allah (Lā ilāha illallāh)’ sincerely"
"3590","Narrated by Abū Hurayrah (may Allāh be pleased with him), from the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him), who said:\n\n\Indeed"
"3591","Ibn `Umar [may Allah be pleased with him] said:“We were with the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) when a man among the people said: ‘Allah is most exceedingly great"
"3592","Abu Dharr narrated that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) visited him"
"3593","Anas bin Malik narrated that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said:“The supplication is not rejected between the Adhan and the Iqamah.” They said: “So what should we say"
"3594","Anas [bin Malik] narrated that the Prophet (ﷺ) said:“The supplication is not rejected between the Adhan and the Iqamah.”"
"3595","Abu Hurairah narrated that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said:“The Mufarridun have preceded.” They said: “And who are the Mufarridun"
"3596","Abu Hurairah [may Allah be pleased with him] narrated that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said:“That I should say: ‘Glory is to Allah (Subḥān Allāh).’ ‘All praise is due to Allah (Al-ḥamdulillāh)"
"3597","Abu Hurairah narrated that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said:“There are three whose supplication is not rejected: The fasting person when he breaks his fast"
"3598","**Narrated by al-Tirmidhi:**\n\nAhmad ibn Mu'ayyad narrated to us, 'Ubaydah ibn Humayd narrated to us, from Yazid ibn Abi Ziyad, from 'Abdullah ibn al-Harith, from al-'Abbas ibn 'Abd al-Muttalib (may Allah be pleased with him), who said:\n\n\I said: 'O Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him)"
"3599","Abu Hurairah or Abu Sa`eed Al-Khudri narrated that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said:“Indeed"
"3600","Abu Hurairah said:“The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said to me: ‘Be frequent in saying: “There is no might or power except by Allah"
"3601","Abu Hurairah narrated that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said:“Every Prophet has a (special) supplication which is answered. Verily"
"3602","Abu Hurairah [may Allah be pleased with him] narrated that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said:“Allah"
"3603","Abu Hurairah narrated that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said:“Seek refuge with Allah from the punishment of Hell"
"3604","Abu Hurairah narrated that:The Prophet said: “There is nothing more honorable with Allah [Most High] than supplication.”"
"3605","Narrated Wathilah bin Al-Asqa':that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: ""Indeed Allah has chosen Isma'il from the children of Ibrahim, and He chose Banu Kinanah from the children of Isma'il, and He chose the Quraish from Banu Kinanah, and He chose Banu Hashim from Quraish, and He chose me from Banu Hashim"
"3606","Narrated Al-'Abbas bin 'Abdul-Muttalib:\I said: 'O Messenger of Allah! Indeed the Quraish have sat and spoken between themselves about the best of them"""
"3607","Narrated Al-Muttalib bin Abi Wada'ah:\Al-Abbas came to the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ)"""
"3608","Narrated Abu Hurairah:\They said: 'O Messenger of Allah (ﷺ)! When was the Prophethood established for you?' He said: 'While Adam was between (being) soul and body"""
"3609","Narrated Anas bin Malik:that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \I am the first of the people to appear upon their being resurrected"""
"3610","Narrated Abu Hurairah [may Allah be pleased with him]:that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \I am the first for whom the earth will be split"""
"3611","Narrated Abu Hurairah:that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \Ask Allah to grant me Al-Wasilah.\"" They said: \""O Messenger of Allah! And what is Al-Wasilah?\"" He said: \""The highest level of Paradise. No one will attain it except for one man"""
"3612","Narrated At-Tufail bin Ubayy bin Ka'b:from his father that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \The parable of me and the Prophets is that of a man who built a house"""
"3613","Narrated 'Abdullah bin 'Amr:that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \If you hear the Muadh-dhin then say as he says. Then send Salat upon me"""
"3614","Narrated Abu Sa'eed:that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \I am the master of the children of Adam on the Day of Judgement"""
"3615","Narrated Ibn 'Abbas:that a group of people from the Companions of the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) sat waiting for him. He said: \Then he came out"""
"3616","Narrated 'Abdullah bin Salam:\The description of Muhammad is written in the Tawrah"""
"3617","Narrated Anas bin Malik:\On the day in which the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) entered Al-Madinah"""
"3618","Narrated Anas bin Malik:""On the day in which the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) entered Al-Madinah, everything in it was illuminated. Then, on the day in which he died, everything in it was dark. And we did not remove our hands from the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ), while we were burying him because our hearts felt so estranged"
"3619","Ibn Abi Umar narrated to us: Sufyan narrated to us from Asim ibn Abi al-Najud, from Zirr ibn Hubaysh, who said: I came to Safwan ibn Assal al-Muradi to ask him about wiping over the leather socks (khuffayn). He said: ""What brought you, O Zirr?"" I said: ""Seeking knowledge."" He said: ""Indeed the angels lower their wings for the seeker of knowledge, pleased with what he seeks."" I said: ""There is a doubt in my chest about wiping over the khuffayn after defecation and urination, and you were a man from the Companions of the Prophet ﷺ, so I came to ask you: did you hear him mention anything about that?"" He said: ""Yes. He used to command us, when we were traveling or wayfarers, not to remove our khuffs for three days and nights, except from major ritual impurity (janabah); but not from defecation, urination, or sleep."" I said: ""Did you hear him mention anything about desire (al-hawa)?"" He said: ""Yes. We were with the Prophet ﷺ on a journey. While we were with him, a Bedouin called out to him with a loud, harsh voice: 'O Muhammad!' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ answered him in a similar tone: 'Here I am (Ha'um).' We said to him: 'Woe to you! Lower your voice, for you are with the Prophet ﷺ, and you have been forbidden from this.' He said: 'By Allah, I will not lower it.' The Bedouin said: 'A man loves a people but has not yet joined them.' The Prophet ﷺ said: 'A man will be with whom he loves on the Day of Resurrection.'"" He continued narrating to us until he mentioned a gate on the side of the West, the breadth of its width is a journey of forty or seventy years for a rider. Sufyan said: ""Towards Sham; Allah created it on the day He created the heavens and the earth, open — meaning for repentance — it will not be closed until the sun rises from it."" Abu Isa said: This is a Hasan Sahih hadith."
"3620","Narrated Ibn 'Abbas:\The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) received Revelation when he was forty years old. So he stayed in Makkah for thirteen years and in Al-Madinah for ten. And he died when he was sixty-three years old"""
"3621","Narrated Ibn 'Abbas:\The Prophet (ﷺ) died when he was sixty-five years old"""
"3622","Narrated Anas bin Malik:\The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) was not very tall nor was he [very] short"""
"3623","**Qutaybah narrated to us; al-Layth narrated to us, from Muḥammad ibn Qayṣ, the storyteller of ʿUmar ibn ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz, from Abū Ṣirmah, from Abū Ayyūb, that he said when death approached him:**\n\n*\I had concealed from you something I heard from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say:*\n\n**'Were it not that you commit sins"
"3624","Narrated Abu Al-'Ala:from Samurah bin Jundab that he said: \We were with the Prophet (ﷺ) and we would take turns (eating) from a bowl from the morning till the evening. Ten would stand and ten would sit.\"" We said: \""So what was filling it up?' He said: \""What are you amazed at? It wasn't filled up from anywhere but here"""
"3625","Narrated 'Ali bin Abi Talib:\I was with the Prophet (ﷺ) in Makkah. We departed to one of its suburbs"""
"3626","Narrated Anas bin Malik:\The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) used to give Khutbah next to a tree"""
"3627","Narrated Ibn 'Abbas:\A Bedouin came to the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) and said: 'How shall I know that you are a Prophet?' He said: 'If I were to call this date cluster from this palm tree"""
"3628","Narrated Abu Zaid bin Akhtab:\The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) wiped his hand over my face and supplicated for me.\"" 'Azrah (one of the narrators) said: \""Indeed he lived for one-hundred and twenty years"""
"3629","Narrated Anas bin Malik:\Abu Talhah said to Umm Sulaim: 'I heard the voice of the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) sounding weak and I sensed some hunger in it. Do you have anything? She said: 'Yes.' So she got some loaves of wheat bread"""
"3630","Narrated Anas bin Malik:\I saw the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) at the time when the 'Asr prayer had drawn near"""
"3631","Narrated 'Aishah:\The first of what the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) initiated with of Prophethood"""
"3632","Narrated by al-Hasan ibn 'Arafah, narrated by Yazid ibn Harun, from 'Abd ar-Rahman ibn Abi Bakr al-Qurashi al-Mulaiki, from Musa ibn 'Uqba, from Nafi', from Ibn 'Umar, who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, said: \Whoever among you has the door of supplication opened for him"
"3633","Narrated 'Aishah:that Al-Harith bin Hisham asked the Prophet (ﷺ): 'How does the Revelation come to you?' The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: 'Sometimes it comes to me like the ringing of a bell and that is the hardest upon me"
"3634","Narrated Al-Bara:\I have not seen anyone with hair past his shoulders in a red Hullah more handsome than the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ). He had hair that would flow on his shoulders"""
"3635","Narrated Abu Ishaq:\A man asked Al-Bara: 'Was the face of the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) like a sword?' He said: 'No"""
"3636","Narrated Abu Ishaq:\A man asked Al-Bara: 'Was the face of the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) like a sword?' He said: 'No"
"3637","Narrated to us Mūsā ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān al-Kindī al-Kūfī, narrated to us Zayd ibn Ḥabbāb, and Sufyān al-Thawrī informed me from Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Abī Laylā, from al-Shaʿbī, from ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Abī Laylā, from Abū Ayyūb al-Anṣarī, who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, said:\n\n\Whoever says ten times: 'There is no deity except Allah alone"
"3638","Narrated 'Urwah:that 'Aishah said: \The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) did not speak quickly like you do now"""
"3639","Narrated Anas bin Malik:that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) would repeat a statement three times so that it could be understood"
"3640","Narrated Ibn Jaz:\I have not seen anyone who smiled more than the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ)"""
"3641","Narrated Ibn Jaz:\The laughter of the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) was not but smiling"""
"3642","Narrated As-Sa'ib bin Yazid:\My maternal aunt took me to the Prophet (ﷺ)"""
"3643","Narrated Jabir bin Samurah:\The seal of the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ)\"" - meaning the one which was between his two shoulder blades - \""was fleshy and red"""
"3644","Narrated Jabir bin Samurah:\The two shins of the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) were thin"""
"3645","Narrated Jabir bin Samurah:\The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) had a wide mouth (Dali' Al-Fam)"""
"3646","Narrated Jabir bin Samurah:\The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) had a wide mouth (Dali' Al-Fam)"""
"3647","Narrated Abu Hurairah:\I have not seen anything more beautiful than the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ). It was as if the sun flowed upon his face. And I have not seen anyone quicker in his walking than the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ). It was as if the earth was made easy for him. We would be exerting ourselves while he would not be struggling"""
"3648","Narrated Jabir:that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \The Prophets were presented to me"""
"3649","Narrated Ibn 'Abbas:\The Prophet (ﷺ) died when he was sixty-five years old"""
"3650","Narrated Ibn 'Abbas:\The Prophet (ﷺ) died when he was sixty-five years old"""
"3651","Narrated Ibn 'Abbas:\The Prophet (ﷺ) stayed in Makkah for thirteen years - meaning while he was receiving Revelation - and he died when he was sixty-three years old"""
"3652","Narrated Jabir [bin 'Abdullah]:that he heard Mu'awiyah bin Abi Sufyan giving a Khutbah"
"3653","Narrated 'Aishah [may Allah be pleased with her]:\The Prophet (ﷺ) died when he was sixty-three years old"""
"3654","Ahmad ibn al-Hasan narrated to us: Sulayman ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Dimashqi narrated to us: al-Walid ibn Muslim narrated to us: Ibn Jurayj narrated to us from Ata ibn Abi Rabah and Ikrimah, the freed slave of Ibn Abbas, from Ibn Abbas, who said: While we were with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, Ali ibn Abi Talib came to him and said: ""May my father and mother be ransomed for you, this Qur'an has slipped from my chest, and I do not find myself able to retain it."" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to him: ""O Abu al-Hasan, shall I not teach you words by which Allah will benefit you, and benefit whoever you teach them, and firmly establish what you have learned in your chest?"" He said: ""Yes, O Messenger of Allah, teach me."" He said: ""If it is the night of Friday, and you are able to stand in the last third of the night, then do so, for it is a witnessed hour and supplication therein is answered. And my brother Yaqub said to his sons: 'I will ask forgiveness for you from my Lord' (12:98) — meaning until the night of Friday comes. If you are not able, then stand in its middle; if you are not able, then stand in its beginning. Pray four rak'ahs: in the first rak'ah recite Fatihat al-Kitab and Surah Ya Sin; in the second, Fatihat al-Kitab and Ha Mim al-Dukhan; in the third, Fatihat al-Kitab and Alif Lam Mim Tanzil al-Sajdah; in the fourth, Fatihat al-Kitab and Tabaraka al-Mufassal. When you finish the tashahhud, praise Allah and extol Him in the best manner, send blessings upon me and do so excellently, and upon the rest of the prophets, and seek forgiveness for the believing men and women and for your brothers who preceded you in faith. Then say at the end: 'O Allah, have mercy on me by leaving sins forever as long as You keep me alive; have mercy on me that I do not burden myself with what does not concern me; provide me with good outlook in what pleases You. O Allah, Originator of the heavens and the earth, Possessor of Glory and Honor and the Might that is not attained, I ask You, O Allah, O Most Merciful, by Your Glory and the Light of Your Face, to bind my heart to the memorization of Your Book as You taught me, and provide me to recite it in the manner that pleases You. O Allah, Originator of the heavens and the earth, Possessor of Glory and Honor and the Might that is not attained, I ask You, O Allah, O Most Merciful, by Your Glory and the Light of Your Face, to illuminate my sight with Your Book, loosen my tongue with it, relieve my heart with it, expand my chest with it, and wash my body with it, for none helps me to the truth but You, and none gives it but You, and there is no power and no strength except by Allah, the High, the Great. O Abu al-Hasan, do this for three Fridays, or five, or seven, and you will be answered by Allah's permission. And by Him who sent me with the truth, no believer has ever failed in it.'"" Abdullah ibn Abbas said: By Allah, Ali did not stay but five or seven (Fridays) until he came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ in a similar gathering and said: ""O Messenger of Allah, I used to not take except four verses or so, and when I recited them to myself they would slip away; and today I learn forty verses or so, and when I recite them to myself it is as if the Book of Allah is between my eyes. And I used to hear a hadith, and when I repeated it, it would slip away; and today I hear ahadith, and when I narrate them, I do not miss a single letter."" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said at that: ""A believer, by the Lord of the Ka'bah, O Abu al-Hasan."" Abu Isa said: This is a Hasan Gharib hadith; we do not know it except from the hadith of al-Walid ibn Muslim."
"3655","**Narrated to us** Bushr ibn Mu'adh al-'Aqadi al-Basri: **Narrated to us** Hammad ibn Waqid, from Isra'il, from Abu Ishaq, from Abu al-Ahwas, from 'Abdullah (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: **The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said:**\n\n**\Ask Allah from His bounty"
"3656","Narrated 'Abdullah bin Shaqiq:\I said to 'Aishah: 'Which of the Companions of the Prophet (ﷺ) were the most beloved to the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ)?' She said: 'Abu Bakr.' I said: 'Then who?' She said: ''Umar.' I said: \""Then who?' She said: 'Then Abu 'Ubaidah bin Al-Jarrah.'\"" He said: \""I said: 'Then who?''\"" He said: \""Then she was silent"""
"3657","Narrated Abu Sa'eed:that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \Indeed the people of the higher levels"""
"3658","Narrated Ibn Abi Mu'alla:from his father: \The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) gave a Khutbah one day and said: 'Indeed there is a man whose Lord has given him the choice between living in this life as long as he wishes to live"""
"3659","Narrated Abu Sa'eed Al-Khudri:\The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) sat upon the Minbar and said: 'Indeed a worshiper has been given a choice by Allah"""
"3660","Narrated Abu Hurairah:that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \There is no favor due upon us from anyone"""
"3661","Narrated Hudhaifah:that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \Stick to the two after me"""
"3662","Narrated Hudhaifah [may Allah be pleased with him]:\We were sitting with the Prophet (ﷺ) and he said: 'I do not know how long I will be with you"""
"3663","Narrated Anas:that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said about Abu Bakr and 'Umar: \These two are the masters of the elder people among the inhabitants of Paradise. From the first ones and the last ones"""
"3664","Narrated Anas:that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said about Abu Bakr and 'Umar: ""These two are the masters of the elder people among the inhabitants of Paradise. From the first ones and the last ones, not including the Prophets and the Messengers. But do not inform them O 'Ali"
"3665","Narrated 'Ali:that the Prophet (ﷺ) said: \Abu Bakr and 'Umar are the masters of the elder people among the inhabitants of Paradise"""
"3666","Narrated Abu Sa'eed Al-Khudri:that Abu Bakr said: \Am I not the most deserving of it among the people"""
"3667","Narrated Anas:that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) used to go out to his Companions from The Muhajirin and the Ansar while they were sitting"
"3668","Narrated Ibn 'Umar:that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) departed one day and entered the Masjid"
"3669","Narrated Ibn 'Umar:that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said to Abu Bakr: \You are my companion at the Hawd"""
"3670","Narrated 'Abdullah bin Hantab:that the Prophet (ﷺ) saw Abu Bakr and 'Umar and said: \These two are the hearing and the seeing"""
"3671","Narrated 'Aishah:that the Prophet (ﷺ) said: \Order Abu Bakr to lead the people in Salat.\"" 'Aishah said: \""O Messenger of Allah! If Abu Bakr takes your place"""
"3672","Narrated 'Aishah:that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \It is not befitting that a group"""
"3673","Narrated Abu Hurairah:that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \Whoever spends a pair of things in the path of Allah"""
"3674","Narrated Zaid bin Aslam:\I heard 'Umar bin Al-Khattab saying: 'We were ordered by the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) to give in charity"""
"3675","Narrated Jubair bin Mut'im:that a woman came to the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) to speak to him about something. Then he ordered her with something"
"3676","**Narrated by Ibn ʿUmayr (may Allah be pleased with both of them):**\n\nHe said: \While we were praying with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him)"
"3677","Narrated 'Aishah:that the Prophet (ﷺ) ordered the closing of all the gates"
"3678","Narrated 'Aishah:that Abu Bakr entered upon the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ)"
"3679","Narrated Abu Sa'eed Al-Khudri:that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \There is no Prophet except that he has two ministers among the inhabitants of the heavens"""
"3680","Narrated Ibn 'Umar:that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \O Allah! Honor Islam through the most dear of these two men to you: Through Abu Jahl or through 'Umar bin Al-Khattab.\"" He said: \""And the most dear of them to Him was 'Umar"""
"3681","Abu Kurayb narrated to us: Abu Mu'awiya narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurayrah (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said:\n\n\For me to say 'SubhanAllah"
"3682","Narrated Ibn 'Abbas:that the Prophet (ﷺ) said: \O Allah honor Islam through Abu Jahl bin Hisham or through 'Umar bin Al-Khattab.\"" He said: \""So it happened that 'Umar came the next day to the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) and accepted Islam"""
"3683","Narrated Jabir bin 'Abdullah:that 'Umar said to Abu Bakr: \O best of people after the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ)!\"" So Abu Bakr said: \""If you say that"""
"3684","Narrated Muhammad bin Sirin:\I don't think that a man who degrades Abu Bakr and 'Umar loves the Prophet (ﷺ)"""
"3685","Narrated 'Uqbah bin 'Amir:that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \If there was to have a Prophet after me"""
"3686","Narrated Ibn 'Umar:\The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: 'I saw that I was brought a cup of milk"""
"3687","Narrated Anas:that the Prophet (ﷺ) said: \I entered Paradise and it was as if I was in a palace of gold. So I said: 'Whose palace is this?' They said: 'A youth's"""
"3688","Narrated Abu Buraidah:\The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) awoke in the morning and called for Bilal"""
"3689","Narrated Buraidah:\The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) went out for one of his expeditions"""
"3690","Narrated 'Aishah:that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) was sitting and we heard a scream and the voices of children. So the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) arose"
"3691","Narrated Ibn 'Umar:that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \I am the first for whom the earth will split"""
"3692","Narrated 'Aishah:that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \Among the nations"""
"3693","Narrated 'Abdullah bin Mas'ud:that the Prophet (ﷺ) said: \A man among the inhabitants of Paradise will appear before you.\"" So Abu Bakr appeared. Then he said: \""A man among the inhabitants of Paradise will appear before you.\"" So 'Umar appeared"""
"3694","Narrated Abu Hurairah:that the Prophet (ﷺ) said: \While a man was tending some of his sheep"""
"3695","Narrated Abu Hurairah [may Allah be pleased with him]:that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) was at Hira"
"3696","Narrated by Abu Dawud, Sulayman ibn al-Ash'ath al-Sijistani narrated to us; Qatn al-Basri narrated to us; Ja'far ibn Sulayman reported to us from Thabit, from Anas رضي الله عنه, who said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said:\n\n\Let each one of you ask his Lord for all of his needs"
"3697","Salih ibn Abdullah narrated to us, who informed us: Ja'far ibn Sulayman narrated to us, from Thabit al-Bunani, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, said:\n\n\Let one of you ask his Lord for his needs"
"3698","Narrated Talhah bin 'Ubaidullah:that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \For every Prophet there is a friend (Rafiq)"""
"3699","Narrated Abu 'Abdur-Rahman As-Sulami:\When 'Uthman was besieged"""
"3700","Narrated 'Abdur-Rahman bin Khabbab:\I witnessed the Prophet (ﷺ) while he was exhorting support for the 'army of distress.' 'Uthman bin 'Affan stood and said: 'O Messenger of Allah! I will take the responsibility of one-hundred camels"""
"3701","Narrated 'Abdur-Rahman bin Samurah:that 'Uthman went to the Prophet (ﷺ) with one-thousand Dinar\ - Al-Hasan bin Waqi (one of the narrators) said: \""And in another place in my book: 'In his garment when the 'army of distress' was being prepared. So he poured them into his lap.'\"" - 'Abdur-Rahman said: \""So I saw the Prophet (ﷺ) turning them over in his lap"""
"3702","Narrated Anas bin Malik:that when the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) ordered the pledge of Ridwan"
"3703","Narrated Thumamah bin Hazn Al-Qushairi:\I was present at the house when 'Uthman appeared above them saying: 'Bring me your two companions who have gathered you against me.'\"" He said: \""So they were brought as if they were two camels"""
"3704","Narrated Abu Al-Ash'ath As-Sana'ani:\Some people were delivering Khutbah in Ash-Sham"""
"3705","Narrated 'Aishah:that the Prophet (ﷺ) said: \O 'Uthman! Indeed Allah may give you a shirt"""
"3706","Narrated 'Uthman bin 'Abdullah bin Mawhab:\A man among the people of Egypt performed Hajj to the House"""
"3707","Narrated Ibn 'Umar:""While the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) was alive, we used to say: 'Abu Bakr, and (then) 'Umar, and (then) 'Uthman"
"3708","Narrated Ibn 'Umar:that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) mentioned the Fitnah and said: \This one will be wrongfully killed during it"""
"3709","Narrated Jabir:that the Prophet (ﷺ) was brought the body of a deceased man, to perform Salat for him, but he did not pray over him. It was said: ""O Messenger of Allah! We have not seen you avoiding prayer over anyone before this?"" He said: ""He used to hate 'Uthman, so Allah hates him"
"3710","Narrated Abu Musa Al-Ash'ari:\I went with the Prophet (ﷺ) and he entered a garden of the Ansar"""
"3711","Narrated Abu Sahlah:\The day of the house (when he was besieged)"""
"3712","Narrated 'Imran bin Husain:that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) dispatched an army and he put 'Ali bin Abi Talib in charge of it. He left on the expedition and he entered upon a female slave. So four of the Companions of the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) scolded him"
"3713","Narrated to us al-Faḍl ibn Sahl, Abū al-ʿAbbās al-Aʿraj al-Baghdādī, narrated to us ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Ghazwān, Abū Nūḥ, reported to us Yūnus ibn Abī Isḥāq, from Abū Bakr ibn Abī Mūsā, from his father, who said:\n\nAbū Ṭālib set out for Syria, and the Prophet ﷺ accompanied him, along with a group of elders from Quraysh. When they drew near to the monk, they dismounted and began to unpack their saddles. The monk came out to them, although previously they had passed by him and he would not come out to them nor pay them any attention.\n\nHe said: While they were unpacking their saddles, the monk moved among them until he came and took the hand of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, saying: \This is the Master of the worlds. This is the Messenger of the Lord of the worlds. Allah shall send him as a mercy to all the worlds.\""\n\nThe elders of Quraysh said to him: \""How do you know this?\"" He replied: \""When you appeared over the pass"
"3714","Narrated 'Ali bin Abi Talib:that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \May Allah have mercy upon Abu Bakr"""
"3715","Muhammad ibn Bashshar narrated to us, Ibn Abi Adi narrated to us, from Hisham, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, who said: \The Prophet"
"3716","Narrated Al-Bara bin 'Azib:that the Prophet (ﷺ) said to 'Ali bin Abi Talib: \You are from me"""
"3717","Narrated by Muhammad ibn Bashshar and Mahmud ibn Ghaylan, who both reported from Abu Dawud al-Tayalisi, from Sulayman ibn Mu'adh al-Dhabbi, from Simak ibn Harb, from Jabir ibn Samurah, who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, said: \Indeed"
"3718","the people of the Ansar, used to recognize the hypocrites, by their hatred for 'Ali bin Abi Talib. \\nJam e Tirmazi Hadees: 3717 Arabic Hadees: 3717\""3719"""
"3719","Abbad ibn Yaqub al-Kufi narrated to us: al-Walid ibn Abi Thawr narrated to us from al-Suddi, from Abbad ibn Abi Yazid, from Ali ibn Abi Talib, who said: I was with the Prophet ﷺ in Makkah, and we went out in some of its valleys. No mountain or tree met him except it said: ""As-salamu alayka, O Messenger of Allah."" He said: This is a Gharib hadith. Others narrated from al-Walid ibn Abi Thawr and they said: from Abbad Abu Yazid, among them Farwah ibn Abi al-Maghra."
"3720","Narrated Hubshi bin Junadah:that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \'Ali is from me and I am from 'Ali. And none should represent me except myself or 'Ali"""
"3721","Narrated Ibn 'Umar:that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) made bonds of brotherhood among his Companions. So 'Ali came crying saying: \O Messenger of Allah! You have made a bond of brotherhood among your Companions"""
"3722","Narrated Anas bin Malik:\There was a bird with the Prophet (ﷺ)"""
"3723","Narrated 'Ali:that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \I am the house of wisdom"""
